{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition","id":1379003,"title":"Why not the Imbued instead of the Second Inquisition?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-06T09:23:14-07:00","id":1379003,"title":"Why not the Imbued instead of the Second Inquisition?","content":"I really don't like the Second Inquisition.. It just feels.. so cliche and horrible. From somehow breaking into Schrecknet, then the Vatican getting involved, then this group of mortals just wrecking everything.. Yeah no. The Camarilla nor Sabbat wouldn't be taken out by such a thing in their pre-V5 unnerfed state realistically (even with the whole Beckoning nonsense, lets be real). The worst egress of this Gary-Stu faction was how they somehow <i>bombed</i> the Vienna Chantry- a magic fortress/university basically that has probably existed longer than all the operators within the SI combined and literally can't be comprehended by mortals at all because it always teleports IIRC. Not only that this Gary-Stu faction has cleared out cities with high level Kindred, some Anchillae too who probably weren't compelled by the Beckoning.. somehow... The Second Inquisition.. is horrible.<br /> <br /> What would have been way more compelling was to bring the Imbued in as the primary Human antagonists instead of the SI. More interesting, has clear abilities that would've allowed them to spot Vienna in the first place with True Sight, a clear precedent of their power is known so there is a logical justification for how their KO'ing the Camarilla and the Sabbat (<i>especially the Sabbat</i>), and they would've been generally more compelling. Because I don't understand the fuss about the Second Inquisition, their faction doesn't make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T10:22:53-07:00","id":1379015,"title":"","content":"Yes. The Camarilla DEFINITELY wouldn't have been taken on by an inquisition armed with technology they barely understand /s.<br /> <br /> I get that people want vampires to be blood gods that don't have to fear mortals but. They aren't. They never have been, and they never will be. Even the Antediluvians have to move in the shadows. The Camarilla was formed because the first inquisition, you know, the one that had just pitchforks and torches effectively was a threat to them. Older books even explained how with the advent of missiles, flamethrowers and machine guns mortals are even more of a terrifying threat to vampires.<br /> <br /> As for Vienna, yes. Magical rituals do a lot, but there's only so much preparation that one can do when you know, dealing with high power explosives unexpectedly and then true faith armed hunters with their own magical relics raiding the place. Tremere have had a lot of bullshit over the years but I don't recall them ever having &quot;Ward against bombs&quot; or &quot;Ward against true faith.&quot;. The Tremere's strength like many other vampires has always been their secrecy or ability to deal with small scale hunters, but their weakness has always been hubris. Even if many of the Tremere there had max level fortitude, they'd be unlikely to survive the initial bombing and even if they did, their escape routes would be limited. Vienna was the safe place to be, the impregnable fortress so there weren't escape routes from there. I'd also need evidence that the chantry 'always teleports'.<br /> <br /> Oh, or the sabbat. The sect of: &quot;Masquerade? What's that?&quot; Yes. They adhere to the silence of the blood, but their actions and ritae to someone explicitly looking for the right thing would stand out. But we don't know too much how the second inquisition has impacted the Sabbat, mostly that they've largely went off on their crusade's to the middle east.<br /> <br /> As for wiping out entire cities. You are severely underestimating the mortal surveillance networks that are in place now. Vampires don't buy toilet paper or food, they don't buy human necessities that often and with a dedicated group watching them silently for years. It's a matter of vampires not understanding their foe which is a major theme in even previous editions. Elders don't understand technology that well, and in the last 20 or so years, we've grown to the point of everyone walking around with cameras being a regular thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T10:47:58-07:00","id":1379019,"title":"","content":"Even with mass surveillance the nu-Inquisitors wouldn't be able to defeat entire cities of Kindred at all. Bullets only do bashing and the Camarilla has a HUGE list of trained of killers who are atleast 400+ years old. They are more smarter than average humans, adapt more better since they even bothered to survive that long, and some Camarilla (aka Alastors) literally hunt down the deadliest Kindred for their entire unlives. The whole Second Inquisition debacle would've warranted a whole wartime effort to smash it down entirely. To a point a an Imperator would've probably assume total military command. The entire Camarilla would shift into a full war paradigm- not whatever their doing in V5 entirely. I'm even going to mention the type of hitter they have in the Sabbat because that is probably going to last til' Wednesday to type up. Barring all that- all the disciplines they have. The nu-Inquisitors are basically hobos, how the hell are they beating both the Camarilla and the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Maybe you can say with the Elders gone the Inquistion might've had a chance, but literally whole slew of very strong Anchillae were left in the cities too. Some Elders even resisted the beckoning. The only reason why Vampires were so badly hurt by the Inquisition in the High Middle-Ages to Renaissance era was because there was no Camarilla yet or any other vampiric organization really besides varying degrees of vassal loyalty. This is different. This is the Camarilla that have been operating under the noises of the entire humanity for centuries without any stop at all. The people who head the Camarilla is lets face it- the Venture. They plan out almost every contingency possible to even remain at their staple of the foodchain.<br /> <br /> They aren't going to be knocked off by some nu-Inquisitors this time at all. This is why the Imbued instead being the central human antagonist is much more compelling because they have an in-verse reason to do this much damage. Not some cliche &quot;nu-inquisition&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also why do people make Elders out to be complete idiots? They aren't ontop of the pyramid for nothing. At that point of surviving all those nights their highly intelligent near-predators, actually scratch that, PREDATORS- they are highly adaptive to every era (barring some of course). They damn sure do understand technology. Even if they didn't, must Elders worth their salt know to fully learn about something less their rival utilizes their ignorance to scrap'em off. To note about the &quot;unknowable&quot; theme about the Second Inquisition, yeah they know what it is. Its literally just the Society of Leopold 2.0 with backing from a bunch of intelligence agencies all at once since they somehow broke into Schrecknet (the heavily encoded/ciphered network that was entirely disconnected from the regular internet and completely manned by Noseferatu and its antitribu sect) and is now going on a Gary Stu spree some how mass KO'ing one of the deadliest creatures in WoD.<br /> <br /> This is something that the Imbued can pull off. Not whatever the Second Inquisition is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-06-2020, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T11:57:02-07:00","id":1379030,"title":"","content":"Re Vienna: consider how many vampiric factions would be happy to see the Prime Chantry destroyed. The Salubri, the Tzimisce, the Banu Haqim, the Hecata, the Tremere Antitribu, <i>Tremere himself</i>, hell, even the Order of Hermes probably.<br /> <br /> Even if you think mortals shouldn't be a threat to vampires (in which case, why is the game called &quot;Vampire <b>the Masquerade</b>&quot;?), there's plenty of precedent for vampiric elders pointing hunters at their enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T12:03:02-07:00","id":1379031,"title":"","content":"I think you're putting the cart before the horse a little bit.<br /> <br /> 1. You're underestimating what the worst monsters of all(humans) are capable of.<br /> <br /> and <br /> <br /> 2. The Second Inquisition is getting a book this year that will likely detail the ways in which they are a severe threat to all things supernatural.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T12:13:51-07:00","id":1379033,"title":"","content":"The Imbued Seem to have been all but Retconned<br /> Is the Masquerade Completely gone?<br /> <br /> Or Anymore Point in keeping it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T12:14:38-07:00","id":1379034,"title":"","content":"I despise the implementation of the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> That said, I'm going to actually address a different point that people could be focusing on instead of trying to defend it: the Imbued are a bad choice to replace them.<br /> <br /> The reason is simple: I want to play Hunter the Reckoning, not Modern Ages: Inquisitor. The Imbued getting their act together to the point of being able to take down something like the Vienna Chantry as an organized operation is the end point of default play in Hunter. It's like diablerie up to 4th Gen, becoming a Legendary Ranked Garou, reaching Archmaster status, etc. You've made it so far you either stop playing and start over, or acknowledge that your game has shifted radically off course from what you got hooked playing with.<br /> <br /> Hunter shouldn't lose what makes it special for Vampire to have a cool antagonist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T12:18:46-07:00","id":1379035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379019#post1379019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with mass surveillance the nu-Inquisitors wouldn't be able to defeat entire cities of Kindred at all. Bullets only do bashing and the Camarilla has a HUGE list of trained of killers who are atleast 400+ years old. They are more smarter than average humans, adapt more better since they even bothered to survive that long, and some Camarilla (aka Alastors) literally hunt down the deadliest Kindred for their entire unlives. The whole Second Inquisition debacle would've warranted a whole wartime effort to smash it down entirely. To a point a an Imperator would've probably assume total military command. The entire Camarilla would shift into a full war paradigm- not whatever their doing in V5 entirely. I'm even going to mention the type of hitter they have in the Sabbat because that is probably going to last til' Wednesday to type up. Barring all that- all the disciplines they have. The nu-Inquisitors are basically hobos, how the hell are they beating both the Camarilla and the Sabbat?<br /> <br /> Maybe you can say with the Elders gone the Inquistion might've had a chance, but literally whole slew of very strong Anchillae were left in the cities too. Some Elders even resisted the beckoning. The only reason why Vampires were so badly hurt by the Inquisition in the High Middle-Ages to Renaissance era was because there was no Camarilla yet or any other vampiric organization really besides varying degrees of vassal loyalty. This is different. This is the Camarilla that have been operating under the noises of the entire humanity for centuries without any stop at all. The people who head the Camarilla is lets face it- the Venture. They plan out almost every contingency possible to even remain at their staple of the foodchain.<br /> <br /> They aren't going to be knocked off by some nu-Inquisitors this time at all. This is why the Imbued instead being the central human antagonist is much more compelling because they have an in-verse reason to do this much damage. Not some cliche &quot;nu-inquisition&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also why do people make Elders out to be complete idiots? They aren't ontop of the pyramid for nothing. At that point of surviving all those nights their highly intelligent near-predators, actually scratch that, PREDATORS they are highly adaptive to every era (barring some of course). They damn sure do understand technology. Even if they didn't, must Elders worth their salt know to fully learn about something less their rival utilizes their ignorance to scrap'em off. To note about the &quot;unknowable&quot; theme about the Second Inquisition, yeah they know what it is. Its literally just the Society of Leopold 2.0 with backing from a bunch of intelligence agencies all at once since they somehow broke into Schrecknet (they heavily encoded/ciphered network that was entirely disconnected from the regular internet and completely manned by Noseferatu and its antitribu sect) and is now going on a Gary Stu spree some how mass KO'ing one of the deadliest creatures in WoD.<br /> <br /> This is something that the Imbued can pull off. Not whatever the Second Inquisition is.</div> </div> </div> </div>A few things about the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> They're not just equipped with equipment S.W.A.T. might possess. They're equipped with high tech stuff designed specifically to combat Cainites. They have weapons made of Snakewood (one of the toughest types of wood, according to London Has Fallen), special coagulants that interferes with a Cainites ability to use vitae on Disciplines, healing, blood surges, and blush of health, just to list some of what they have access to. They also have access to other military grade equipment. <br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition also has numbers, and doesn't send teams in blindly to take out targets. They assess the threat a target presents, then apply whatever resources (number of teams, equipment, etc.) they feel necessary to get the job done. Teams sent to take down Cainites have likely practiced for that specific raid for weeks. I would also assume that they are executing operations to kill or capture Cainites during the day.<br /> <br /> One other thing to consider. Unless actually confirmed, targets of the Second Inquisition thought eliminated may not in fact be dead. While I could have missed it, I don't believe it's confirmed that the members of the Tremere Inner Council of Seven have been actually destroyed (the level 5 ritual Escape To A True Sanctuary, formerly Escape To A True Friend, is certainly a method some of them could have used to escape). There are almost certainly a lot of elders, and even ancillae that escaped and went into hiding. Even if the Second Inquisition believes a particular target was eliminated, any information regarding this that's stated in character can't be completely trusted as true. There's a lot of instances where a Cainite thought dead later turns up still alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T12:19:30-07:00","id":1379036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379019#post1379019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even with mass surveillance the nu-Inquisitors wouldn't be able to defeat entire cities of Kindred at all. Bullets only do bashing and the Camarilla has a HUGE list of trained of killers who are atleast 400+ years old. They are more smarter than average humans, adapt more better since they even bothered to survive that long, and some Camarilla (aka Alastors) literally hunt down the deadliest Kindred for their entire unlives. The whole Second Inquisition debacle would've warranted a whole wartime effort to smash it down entirely. To a point a an Imperator would've probably assume total military command. The entire Camarilla would shift into a full war paradigm- not whatever their doing in V5 entirely. I'm even going to mention the type of hitter they have in the Sabbat because that is probably going to last til' Wednesday to type up. Barring all that- all the disciplines they have. The nu-Inquisitors are basically hobos, how the hell are they beating both the Camarilla and the Sabbat?</div> </div> </div> </div>We go back to: They did the exact same thing during the first inquisition when the mortals had less weapons and surveillance. Bullets might only do superficial damage. But enough bullets directed at a vampire will still knock them into torpor. This also doesn't factor in that they have stake launchers, daylight raids, fire, bombs. Etc. Yes. The Camarilla has Alastors. Who couldn't even hunt down Caiaphas Smith. A mortal hunter. The cam's official policy was to literally bunker down and hide if this guy was seen. This wasn't in V5, this was V20 and older material.<br /> <br /> The Camarilla's response has not, never will be, and shouldn't be to 'go to war' with an inquisition. Because vampires will LOSE that fight. They can't operate during the day, they will die if they are attacked during the day and the humans have numbers, which outright warring against them would just draw more attention to their fight which means more mortals to help fuel the inquisition. The Camarilla's response would to try and black mail and discredit the inquisitors, to get it shut down. But. If you don't realize that there is a problem, say because they aren't making waves and acting yet, you can't really go after them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379019#post1379019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you can say with the Elders gone the Inquistion might've had a chance, but literally whole slew of very strong Anchillae were left in the cities too. Some Elders even resisted the beckoning. The only reason why Vampires were so badly hurt by the Inquisition in the High Middle-Ages to Renaissance era was because there was no Camarilla yet or any other vampiric organization really besides varying degrees of vassal loyalty. This is different. This is the Camarilla that have been operating under the noises of the entire humanity for centuries without any stop at all. The people who head the Camarilla is lets face it- the Venture. They plan out almost every contingency possible to even remain at their staple of the foodchain.<br /> <br /> They aren't going to be knocked off by some nu-Inquisitors this time at all. This is why the Imbued instead being the central human antagonist is much more compelling because they have an in-verse reason to do this much damage. Not some cliche &quot;nu-inquisition&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Again. The Camarilla's policy was to make the masquerade and hide. You can sit here and pretend that vampires are these immortal blood gods who are nigh untouchable. But they had MORE influence in the middle ages individually. A vampire's very much do not work well together. They are backstabbing and untrusting, so them having an organization that is corrupt and based around stabbing your way to the top is not going to organize a resistance to the hunters.<br /> <br /> They are going to die to hunters. Because in every single edition of vampire, humans have been a scary threat. The Ventrue might imagine they've planned for every contingency but if that were true then they'd all still be alive. Vampires, like it or not, can't rule humans because humans can operate all the time. Vampires will literally die if they try and fight during the day.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also why do people make Elders out to be complete idiots? They aren't ontop of the pyramid for nothing. At that point of surviving all those nights their highly intelligent near-predators, actually scratch that, PREDATORS they are highly adaptive to every era (barring some of course). They damn sure do understand technology. Even if they didn't, must Elders worth their salt know to fully learn about something less their rival utilizes their ignorance to scrap'em off. To note about the &quot;unknowable&quot; theme about the Second Inquisition, yeah they know what it is. Its literally just the Society of Leopold 2.0 with backing from a bunch of intelligence agencies all at once since they somehow broke into Schrecknet (they heavily encoded/ciphered network that was entirely disconnected from the regular internet and completely manned by Noseferatu and its antitribu sect) and is now going on a Gary Stu spree some how mass KO'ing one of the deadliest creatures in WoD.<br /> <br /> This is something that the Imbued can pull off. Not whatever the Second Inquisition is. </div> </div> </div>No. They really don't, and no. The Imbued aren't special in that regard. For hundreds upon hundreds of years, the most advanced form of travel was a carriage pulled by horses. Then it jumped up to cars. They go faster, they are impressive and sturdier but same basic concept. And then we've made the internet in the last 100 years. Then we've had cellphones become common place in the last 20. The cellphone cameras became common place. Vampires have always had a theme of being stuck in their ways. We have humans that are struggling to adapt to desktop computers, let alone a vampire that to him, in a blink of an eye we go from newspapers being the most advanced form of communication to TikTok? He might get the basic concept, but the depth of that isn't going to sink in.<br /> <br /> And yes Shrecknet. The ever so secure network by the Nosferatu. Which is still a computer network and access to one terminal provides access to the entire network. You know, like how computers and the like operate.<br /> <br /> It's not that elders are idiots. It's that elders haven't had to adopt to anything like this until recently. It's that your entire argument, calling human's Gary Stu's while requiring the ACTUAL Gary Stu splat to step in and take care of the problem. &quot;Hunter: We fight supernatural monsters by becoming exactly like them without question.&quot; while ignoring that every edition has indicated that humans have the potential to do the damage they are now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T13:14:11-07:00","id":1379044,"title":"","content":"Humans are only ever a threat to Vampires in the point where if they entirety of it knew of it (aka nukes). Not by a faction basis- which exactly what the Second Inquisition is doing entirely somehow. Again- the first Inquisition was more of a thread because Vampires were less organized than they were to respond to such an organization. The way the Second Inquisition is hammering down on the Camarilla, they would've went on full warpath mode immediately fullstop. Nothing would be able to stop the Camarilla in that level of militarization. Realistically even the Sabbat would temporarily team up with the Cam aswell since such a human faction would be an upfront nuisance that definitely would need consolidation to deal with his ALL of vampire society was threatened by the Second Inquisition. They don't have to be Immortal Blood gods- they have enough combined experience together between every SI operative that taking them piece by piece realistically should've been childs play. Not to mention almost every part of the criminal and legal influence the Camarilla easily has across Western society as a whole.<br /> <br /> Again- Vampires aren't humans. Elders who don't quickly adapt meet Final Death eventually through not keeping up with their rivals. There are literally countless Elders who are centuries old who very easy understand the modern world because their already so used to adapting to every new technology that comes out. You act as if Elders are braindead idiots when it isn't the case of the setting at all really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T13:25:23-07:00","id":1379046,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, the Second Inquisition is better organized and has more resources, better training and better technology than the Imbued. Plus they have access to the supernatural powers of the Society of Saint Leopold.<br /> <br /> Who are Gary and Stu?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T13:36:02-07:00","id":1379051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379044#post1379044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans are only ever a threat to Vampires in the point where if they entirety of it knew of it (aka nukes). Not by a faction basis- which exactly what the Second Inquisition is doing entirely somehow. Again- the first Inquisition was more of a thread because Vampires were less organized than they were to respond to such an organization. The way the Second Inquisition is hammering down on the Camarilla, they would've went on full warpath mode immediately fullstop. Nothing would be able to stop the Camarilla in that level of militarization. Realistically even the Sabbat would temporarily team up with the Cam aswell since such a human faction would be an upfront nuisance that definitely would need consolidation to deal with his ALL of vampire society was threatened by the Second Inquisition. They don't have to be Immortal Blood gods- they have enough combined experience together between every SI operative that taking them piece by piece realistically should've been childs play. Not to mention almost every part of the criminal and legal influence the Camarilla easily has across Western society as a whole.<br /> <br /> Again- Vampires aren't humans. Elders who don't quickly adapt meet Final Death eventually through not keeping up with their rivals. There are literally countless Elders who are centuries old who very easy understand the modern world because their already so used to adapting to every new technology that comes out. You act as if Elders are braindead idiots when it isn't the case of the setting at all really.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires are not 'more organized' nor would a warpath help them. When you are murdering entire swaths of the intelligence community, others will notice. That also assumes that kindred know WHO to hit. They know that this is a big problem in intelligence agencies, but it's a matter of figuring out who has been 'corrupted' by it and who hasn't. Kindred are arrogant and vain creatures. Why would they lend their aid to fighting this (Back when the threat could be managed) when someone else will deal with it, or it won't be a problem if they keep their head down?<br /> <br /> Yes. Vampires have enough experience that an individual hunter who doesn't have much experience isn't a problem. But no, it's not just individual hunters. It's co-ordination of clandestine organizations working with technology that's beyond even what the neonates understand. These are groups of mortals who do what kindred do, except they have the backing of governments behind them as well. They also have quite a few advantages: Vampires can't work in the day, at best, they can operate through mortal servants. SI agents don't draw attention until they act or are explicitly focused on kindred. Kindred draw attention by virtue of existing. There exists technology to find vampires (Again, something that existed in older editions). There isn't technology to identify &quot;Oh, this guy is part of the SI&quot;. If the conflict gets attention drawn to it, kindred will ultimately lose so Kindred have to fight this with a bit more stealth.<br /> <br /> Vampires aren't humans. That is correct. They are monsters that get stuck in ruts. See: Villouis or many other elders. And again. They have not needed to adapt this much until recent years. Technology has boomed. The techniques of old worked for hundreds, upon hundreds of years. Culture changed, certain devices became more efficient. But until recently, they've never needed to deal with something on this scale. And you know what elders do have to keep up with their rivals? Servants and neonates who were, recently, mortal.<br /> <br /> I'm not acting as if Elders are braindead idiots. I'm acting as if elders are shown as elders have been shown. Creatures that are reluctant to move forward to the future unless they must and act through pawns and proxies to protect themselves with all of the risks and flaws that come with that.<br /> <br /> You haven't made one credible argument for why the large scale information gathering networks that we have, alongside the advanced equipment that the governments have in the real world couldn't possibly deal with ancient elders who. Again. Died to mortals with pitchforks and torches. Them being more 'organized' is a piss poor argument because vampires have been shown to exploit opportunities to get at foes all the time. If they COULD behave reasonably and co-operate against large scale threats then the world of darkness would be a different place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T13:43:50-07:00","id":1379052,"title":"","content":"Generally, the Imbued have never been particularly popular versus more mundane Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T13:46:00-07:00","id":1379053,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> no one I know has ever played one of the Imbued.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T14:02:50-07:00","id":1379055,"title":"","content":"To go with a different explanation, V:TM has always been done as a conspiracy-heavy socially relevant game with the conflict between capitalism and the have-nots being a major source of the War of Ages-themes. The Anarchs predate the rise of Occupy, Bernie, and other grassroots resistance movements with a hefty dose of crime as well as victimhood of police brutality. The Second Inquisition is an attempt to embody the post 9/11 surveillance state and deal with the fact the Masquerade would be fundamentally different in our post-War on Terror world where trillions of dollars are spent gathering the data of every citizen on the globe, spy satellites (or Google), plus a shift from large scale military engagements to small squad-based military attacks.<br /> <br /> A lot of fans are dealing with this shift because humans have kind of been shit on by previous Editions and the Masquerade was de-emphasized to the point that it was assumed that humans were all but helpless against the undead.<br /> <br /> A mistake, IMHO, because hunters are an eternal part of vampire lore. This is just about restoring them to their rightful place as a main vampire antagonist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T14:10:46-07:00","id":1379056,"title":"","content":"Mind you, I think that if any vampire forgot to do, &quot;Wake with Mornings Freshness&quot; then they are utterly fucked if they're older than a couple of centuries.<br /> <br /> Humanity 2 Trenere Methuselah: &quot;I can Lure of Flames!&quot;<br /> <br /> Storyteller: Roll two dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T14:46:35-07:00","id":1379063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379051#post1379051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You haven't made one credible argument for why the large scale information gathering networks that we have, alongside the advanced equipment that the governments have in the real world couldn't possibly deal with ancient elders who. Again. Died to mortals with pitchforks and torches.</div> </div> </div> </div>One thing: dying to the Inquisition isn't the same as dying to peasants with pitchforks. It was things like Ferdinand and Isabella using real military power to seize the land of accused heretics. A group of peasants with pitchforks storming a castle full of ghouled soldiers is laughable, even during the day. The king seizing a creepy lord's land is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.history.com/topics/religion/inquisition\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/aenetworks/image/upload/c_fill,w_1200,h_630,g_auto/dpr_auto/f_auto/q_auto:eco/v1/gettyimages-51240189-2?_a=BAVMn6E80\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.history.com/topics/religion/inquisition\" target=\"_blank\"> Inquisition - Spanish, Roman &amp; Torture | HISTORY </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.history.com/topics/religion/inquisition\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.history.com/topics/religion/inquisition </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Inquisition was a powerful office within the Catholic Church which rooted out and punished heresy throughout Euro... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T15:50:43-07:00","id":1379083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379063#post1379063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing: dying to the Inquisition isn't the same as dying to peasants with pitchforks. It was things like Ferdinand and Isabella using real military power to seize the land of accused heretics. A group of peasants with pitchforks storming a castle full of ghouled soldiers is laughable, even during the day. The king seizing a creepy lord's land is not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.history.com/topics/religion/inquisition\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/aenetworks/image/upload/c_fill,w_1200,h_630,g_auto/dpr_auto/f_auto/q_auto:eco/v1/gettyimages-51240189-2?_a=BAVMn6E80\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.history.com/topics/religion/inquisition\" target=\"_blank\"> Inquisition - Spanish, Roman &amp; Torture | HISTORY </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.history.com/topics/religion/inquisition\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.history.com/topics/religion/inquisition </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> The Inquisition was a powerful office within the Catholic Church which rooted out and punished heresy throughout Euro... </div> </div> </div><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it happened quite a lot in the world of vampire because vampire is based on a very cinematic stylized universe. Mind you, in this universe, the castle probably had 20 ghouls because you can't maintain an army of ghouls with even a coterie of vampires.<br /> <br /> Fun fact: The 2nd Anarch Revolt in my games is primarily motivated by the fact automatic weapons, shotguns, and even the six shooter dramatically evened a fight between Elders and Neonates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T16:24:29-07:00","id":1379089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379044#post1379044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humans are only ever a threat to Vampires in the point where if they entirety of it knew of it (aka nukes). Not by a faction basis- which exactly what the Second Inquisition is doing entirely somehow. Again- the first Inquisition was more of a thread because Vampires were less organized than they were to respond to such an organization. The way the Second Inquisition is hammering down on the Camarilla, they would've went on full warpath mode immediately fullstop. Nothing would be able to stop the Camarilla in that level of militarization. Realistically even the Sabbat would temporarily team up with the Cam aswell since such a human faction would be an upfront nuisance that definitely would need consolidation to deal with his ALL of vampire society was threatened by the Second Inquisition. They don't have to be Immortal Blood gods- they have enough combined experience together between every SI operative that taking them piece by piece realistically should've been childs play. Not to mention almost every part of the criminal and legal influence the Camarilla easily has across Western society as a whole.<br /> <br /> Again- Vampires aren't humans. Elders who don't quickly adapt meet Final Death eventually through not keeping up with their rivals. There are literally countless Elders who are centuries old who very easy understand the modern world because their already so used to adapting to every new technology that comes out. You act as if Elders are braindead idiots when it isn't the case of the setting at all really.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, most elders have not completely adapted to the times, not unless they've gone out of their way to keep up, which a lot haven't done. I'm not saying they're completely anachronistic, but there's a lot of elders that are often blindsided by many types of modern tech. In 1903 the Wright Brothers had their first flight of an airplane. In 1969 we landed on the moon. The advancement of technology in the last century or so has built up considerable speed, and it's difficult for most elders to keep up. One way to combat this is by embracing childer or creating ghouls familiar with the current times that can act as advisers.<br /> <br /> If humans were only a threat because of nukes, the Masquerade wouldn't have become a thing until nukes were invented. Humans are absolutely a threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 04-06-2020, 07:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T17:21:42-07:00","id":1379102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archasimos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379089#post1379089\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, most elders have not completely adapted to the times, not unless they've gone out of their way to keep up, which a lot haven't done. I'm not saying they're completely anachronistic, but there's a lot of elders that are often blindsided by many types of modern tech. In 1903 the Wright Brothers had their first flight of an airplane. In 1969 we landed on the moon. The advancement of technology in the last century or so has built up considerable speed, and it's difficult for most elders to keep up. One way to combat this is by embracing childer or creating ghouls familiar with the current times that can act as advisers.<br /> <br /> If humans were only a threat because of nukes, the Masquerade wouldn't have become a thing until nukes were invented. Humans are absolutely a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of why they did this was because of Elder creep.<br /> <br /> Elders were ridiculously overpowered and it seemed impossible that they'd ever die.<br /> <br /> Now, it's a simple matter of finding them during the daytime, stab, decapitate, burn.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T17:36:05-07:00","id":1379105,"title":"","content":"I am totally fine with the most heinous monster of WoD, humankind, finally pulling its shit together and being able to fight back properly w/o any aid from supernatural hunters or any other fantasy stuff. Finally they stopped playing meek idiots en masse being pushed around by dominate and presence pretending to be helpless icompetent bodybags.<br /> <br /> Also, why an underground club of deformed vampires would be better at IT than mortals? Lol, really? It's clearly stated in CC, in the Cryptography section, that vampires can't even hope to stay on par with mortals in ares involving ingenuity and creativity, let alone hope to surpass it. Add sheer numbers and technological capacities of governmental structures tasked with what SI was tasked with and voila. An absolutely logical and legit development.<br /> <br /> VtM states another quite mundane and obvious but easily forgotten (at least by RPG community) truth: Information is everything. And there is no deadlier weapon than a human intellect. No Dicsipline, Magic or combat prowess can help you against dedicated masses wielding aforementioned weapons with coordinated and focused effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T17:39:53-07:00","id":1379108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379046#post1379046\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who are Gary and Stu?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gary-Stu is a masculine form of the Mary-Sue trope/cliche. While the specific definition is varied, it's generally used to connote a character that's unrealistically by in-setting standards successful/competent/etc. and skates past any flaws or mistakes without consequences. Frequently these characters are associated with wish fulfillment by the author.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379053#post1379053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> no one I know has ever played one of the Imbued.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's hardly a compelling statement. I've played more Imbued than most people I know have played any WoD characters. So what?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379052#post1379052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Generally, the Imbued have never been particularly popular versus more mundane Hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally, this is bullshit. The Imbued have sold more books, and more secondary products, than all the mundane style hunters in the WoD combined; and despite being a very late addition to the WoD.<br /> <br /> Even CofD's Hunter the Vigil, which is seen as more of what the fans wanted, has hunters that operate more like the Imbued with the Tier 3 Conspiracies including multiple groups with overt supernatural powers along side high-tech government run black op squads; acknowledging that there's appeal to the Imbued to include in such books.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T17:40:38-07:00","id":1379109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379102#post1379102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of why they did this was because of Elder creep.<br /> <br /> Elders were ridiculously overpowered and it seemed impossible that they'd ever die.<br /> <br /> Now, it's a simple matter of finding them during the daytime, stab, decapitate, burn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm cool with elders being powerful, but no one is invincible, nor can every contingency be accounted for. I think they did it to give humans the bite the Masquerade always implied they had. Why even enforce the Masquerade if humans weren't the threat they were stated to be? Now there's a reason to take it more seriously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T17:47:40-07:00","id":1379111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379108#post1379108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even CofD's Hunter the Vigil, which is seen as more of what the fans wanted, has hunters that operate more like the Imbued with the Tier 3 Conspiracies including multiple groups with overt supernatural powers along side high-tech government run black op squads; acknowledging that there's appeal to the Imbued to include in such books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters with supernatural powers have always been a thing. They were called Numina. What they disliked was that all of the Imbued were empowered by supernatural beings rather than being psychics ala Anne Rice's Talamasca or True Faith Hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T17:50:17-07:00","id":1379112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379102#post1379102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think part of why they did this was because of Elder creep.<br /> <br /> Elders were ridiculously overpowered and it seemed impossible that they'd ever die.<br /> <br /> Now, it's a simple matter of finding them during the daytime, stab, decapitate, burn.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's stupid. Why would you nerf the Elders into the ground? They are still a threat, as they SHOULD be. Their main tactic, as it was back then, to put a meat shield of childer back then, and Anarch/Sabbat mobs nowadays, between themselves and the hunters. Not to go out in the field flinging their 6 Potence and 7 Foritude screaming &quot;Fight me puny mortals!&quot; <br /> <br /> Getting to any elder would and should always feel like a huge accomplishment.<br /> Really, CTPhipps, any specific reason in removing elder creep? how does it benefit the game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:19:39-07:00","id":1379117,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379112#post1379112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's stupid. Why would you nerf the Elders into the ground? They are still a threat, as they SHOULD be. Their main tactic, as it was back then, to put a meat shield of childer back then, and Anarch/Sabbat mobs nowadays, between themselves and the hunters. Not to go out in the field flinging their 6 Potence and 7 Foritude screaming &quot;Fight me puny mortals!&quot;<br /> <br /> Getting to any elder would and should always feel like a huge accomplishment.<br /> <br /> Really, CTPhipps, any specific reason in removing elder creep? how does it benefit the game?</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends what exactly you want from your Elders. For me, the iconic Elder is Dracula who was killed by a cowboy with a Bowie knife. Elders shouldn't have superpowers but have a variety of powers that they use intelligently. For me, I find Elders like Karsh to be silly because any elder that is running around with a battle ax fighting Lupines would never last long enough to become an Elder in the first place. I prefer my Elders who are people who work in boxes and boxes and if they do their actions right then you never know what they're involved. What happens when a coterie of anger Anarchs attack a Elder?<br /> <br /> THEY RUN and send their minions!<br /> <br /> They are masters of survival.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wtq7L2zphPQ\" data-code=\"wtq7L2zphPQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wtq7L2zphPQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> These are my Elders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:26:12-07:00","id":1379118,"title":"","content":"Using only pawns for so long can only go so far. For Elders to even survive that long that'd have to be somewhat passable with some combat. Even Elders who don't even use any sort of violence as you suggested would probably have 6+ disciplines anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:27:51-07:00","id":1379119,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> you\u2019re being rude.<br /> <br /> I like the Imbued (though tbh I\u2019m a little annoyed cause one time when I got really bored I bought all the H:tR monster books and I didn\u2019t learn anything new that I didn\u2019t already know from the other game lines). I\u2019ve never seen them played, but they have cool powers and they\u2019re probably pretty effective in small groups. I was just pointing out that they don\u2019t have the temporal resources that the Second Inquisition does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:30:17-07:00","id":1379120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379117#post1379117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends what exactly you want from your Elders. For me, the iconic Elder is Dracula who was killed by a cowboy with a Bowie knife. Elders shouldn't have superpowers but have a variety of powers that they use intelligently. For me, I find Elders like Karsh to be silly because any elder that is running around with a battle ax fighting Lupines would never last long enough to become an Elder in the first place. I prefer my Elders who are people who work in boxes and boxes and if they do their actions right then you never know what they're involved. What happens when a coterie of anger Anarchs attack a Elder?<br /> <br /> THEY RUN and send their minions!<br /> <br /> They are masters of survival.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wtq7L2zphPQ\" data-code=\"wtq7L2zphPQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wtq7L2zphPQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> These are my Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> While he's not my favorite character, I don't find anything wrong with Karsh, though I can't say I ever picture any Cainite that hunts lupines to simply be running around with a battle axe fighting them. I'm sure it's much more nuanced than that, otherwise yeah, they would be dead. Also, it's obviously difficult and dangerous, otherwise there'd be a lot more Cainites that hunt lupines successfully.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:38:59-07:00","id":1379125,"title":"","content":"Well in Chicago by Night V5 they squirted that logic entirely because neonates take on entire packs of &quot;Lupines&quot; by themselves entirely.. apparently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:40:35-07:00","id":1379127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379125#post1379125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well in Chicago by Night V5 they squirted that logic entirely because neonates take on entire packs of &quot;Lupines&quot; by themselves entirely.. apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which neonates are actually taking on entire packs of lupines by themselves?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 04-06-2020, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:55:15-07:00","id":1379130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379111#post1379111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters with supernatural powers have always been a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, one of the sillier things about the attacks on HtR as a game for them having powers when that was already a thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What they disliked was that all of the Imbued were empowered by supernatural beings rather than being psychics ala Anne Rice's Talamasca or True Faith Hunters. </div> </div> </div>I've been around the WW fandom from before HtR came out. People weren't going on about the source of the Imbued's powers. They wanted Hunters Hunted to be a full core book, and projected than onto HtR rather than giving HtR a chance on it's own merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379119#post1379119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> you\u2019re being rude.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. But at the same time, bashing HtR as unpopular and unplayed is a long standing thing in the WoD fandom despite all of the games fans.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T18:59:36-07:00","id":1379132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Godforsaken</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1372626-v5-lupine-power-level?p=1372940#post1372940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"color:#2E3338\"><span style=\"font-family:Whitney\">For those of you who spoke about ambushes and smart tactics vampires can use, this is from the Chicago book:<br /> <i>&quot;...Kevin grabbed a broadsword off the wall and helped hold off the invading forces (Lupines). Kevin slew the pack leader in battle...&quot;</i><br /> Sayed Kevin, have str 4, melee 2, and fortitude of 4. Werewolf in the V5 book have 6 str, 5 brawl, Celerity 4, Fortitude 5, Potence 5....<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;...He prefers a deal, but he\u2019ll send his Hounds to hunt the werewolves down if he has to.&quot;</i><br /> The &quot;Hounds&quot; that are mentioned in the book don't have any impressive combat skills, disciplines or even resources to back this sentence. Again, comparing them to the common werewolf stats that are on the core V5 book I would say that a single lupine will most likely kill most if not all of those &quot;Hounds&quot;.<br /> <br /> I was really looking forward to running a campaign with this sourcebook, but I guess I will have to change a lot of things if I don't want the PCs to have delusions about &quot;hunting down lupines&quot;.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was referencing Godforsaken on this. Some neonate named Kevin actively hunting down &quot;Lupines&quot;. Also he had dogs that apparently that could kill Werewolves (correct me if I'm wrong though, he could've meant a name for his minions or something)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T19:02:50-07:00","id":1379134,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> <br /> Actually Wraith is the most bashed and underrated gameline in oWoD history. Hunter:The Reckoning atleast got its own game along with VTM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T19:06:56-07:00","id":1379135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379134#post1379134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a><br /> <br /> Actually Wraith is the most bashed and underrated gameline in oWoD history. Hunter:The Reckoning atleast got its own game along with VTM.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He never said HtR was the most bashed. Just that it IS bashed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Signed, a giant HtR fan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T19:10:48-07:00","id":1379136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379132#post1379132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I was referencing Godforsaken on this. Some neonate named Kevin actively hunting down &quot;Lupines&quot;. Also he had dogs that apparently that could kill Werewolves (correct me if I'm wrong though, he could've meant a name for his minions or something)</div> </div> </div> </div>While on the young side, Kevin Jackson is the current prince of Chicago. Hound is a term for a position held in the Camarilla, usually Cainites appointed specifically to assist the Sheriff. He does not have a pack of dogs that hunt werewolves. Also there's nothing in his writeup that indicates he actually hunts lupines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 04-06-2020, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T19:16:46-07:00","id":1379137,"title":"","content":"Also this from the V5 Chicago by Night book, which references a fight with a Sabbat pack, even though it mentions he found werewolves killing vampires and a few city elders. It does appear a bit confusing, and I'm not sure why they wrote it that way to be honest.<br /> <br /> Kevin played his part during the War of Chicago. Suspecting his sire would fall, he headed to the Prince\u2019s secured haven to steal Lodin\u2019s computer and thus obtain the older Ventrue\u2019s assets. Upon entering, he found werewolves killing vampires with a few city elders among them. Unsure of the outcome, he attacked to \u201csave\u201d his Camarilla peers. Kevin grabbed a broadsword off the wall and helped hold off the invading forces. Kevin slew the Sabbat pack leader in battle, but it was the two dozen armed Bloods who saved him. That fight earned him the brief nickname \u201cPaladin,\u201d influence, and access to Lodin\u2019s old accounts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":577,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","user":"Archasimos","date":". 04-06-2020, 10:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T19:49:25-07:00","id":1379144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379118#post1379118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using only pawns for so long can only go so far. For Elders to even survive that long that'd have to be somewhat passable with some combat. Even Elders who don't even use any sort of violence as you suggested would probably have 6+ disciplines anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a word for an Elder who ends up fighting man to man: failure.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T19:50:28-07:00","id":1379145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379125#post1379125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well in Chicago by Night V5 they squirted that logic entirely because neonates take on entire packs of &quot;Lupines&quot; by themselves entirely.. apparently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that they intend to take away Rage=Extra Actions for Lupines ala Celerity. When that happens, Lupines are perfectly killable by normal vampires. They lose all their super-advantages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-06T19:55:33-07:00","id":1379147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379144#post1379144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a word for an Elder who ends up fighting man to man: failure.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really think it depends on the character concept (whether NPC or PC). Fighting man to man is fine. The important thing is to pick your battles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u2019m a writer. A storyteller. They\u2019re my passions. They\u2019re what I do. The stories I tell, they are my mythologies. Like the Norse tales of Odin, Thor, and Loki, or the Celtic fables of Lugh or C\u00fa Chulainn, I want them to be the kind that people retell. They are the legacies I wish to leave behind.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/577-archasimos","name":"Archasimos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar577_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"180"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T02:47:11-07:00","id":1379191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379134#post1379134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually Wraith is the most bashed and underrated gameline in oWoD history. Hunter:The Reckoning atleast got its own game along with VTM.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware this was a competition all the sudden. Beyond what Larry aptly noted (and the two of us vocally agreeing on stuff is as rare as hen's teeth), called Wraith bashed or underrated is kinda of ridiculous.<br /> <br /> First off, Changeling holds that distinction due to the 1e/2e doing a poor job of representing the dark side of the game, leading a huge portion of the WoD fandom to dismiss it as too light and too whimsical for the WoD, and a bunch of mechanical issues that didn't get solved until C20 because Dreaming never got a Revised edition that seriously undercut gameplay rather than just being averagely not great 90s WoD rules.<br /> <br /> Second off, if we're going to view it as negative, Wraith holds the &quot;damned with faint praise award.&quot; It's reputation has long been as having the strongest concept of all of the WoD games, with top tier writing, setting, and game-play hooks... while being the game nobody could ever find the right group to play it with. It's so well regarded in concept, people felt scared of screwing it up more than excited to play it (esp. things like Shadow Guiding).<br /> <br /> Last, you could respond to the actual point on your own thread, rather than debating the quality of the Second Inquisition (there's been plenty of threads about that): why should HtR fans have their game redone to suit VtM's needs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:10:31-07:00","id":1379199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379117#post1379117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It depends what exactly you want from your Elders. For me, the iconic Elder is Dracula who was killed by a cowboy with a Bowie knife. Elders shouldn't have superpowers but have a variety of powers that they use intelligently. For me, I find Elders like Karsh to be silly because any elder that is running around with a battle ax fighting Lupines would never last long enough to become an Elder in the first place. I prefer my Elders who are people who work in boxes and boxes and if they do their actions right then you never know what they're involved. What happens when a coterie of anger Anarchs attack a Elder?<br /> <br /> THEY RUN and send their minions!<br /> <br /> They are masters of survival.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wtq7L2zphPQ\" data-code=\"wtq7L2zphPQ\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/wtq7L2zphPQ/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> These are my Elders.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK I get it, it's again YOUR idea on the game, not the game itself.<br /> <br /> I am sure the proper elders are still out there. You know, the ones who know both how to send their miniones, manipulate their surroundings, ensure two or three backup routs out of the city AND know how to swing a battleaxe with Potence 6 if being pressed into it. Just the regular, good old elders from the WoD we all played an enjoyed for years before V5.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:18:04-07:00","id":1379202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379199#post1379199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> OK I get it, it's again YOUR idea on the game, not the game itself.<br /> <br /> I am sure the proper elders are still out there. You know, the ones who know both how to send their miniones, manipulate their surroundings, ensure two or three backup routs out of the city AND know how to swing a battleaxe with Potence 6 if being pressed into it. Just the regular, good old elders from the WoD we all played an enjoyed for years before V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given I mentioned Karsh, I think its kind of obvious I know there's other kinds of Elders. :-p<br /> <br /> They just dialed them down to be more manageable.<br /> <br /> Hence the Beckoning taking the oldest and most broken off the board.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:39:29-07:00","id":1379208,"title":"","content":"This discussion again. <br /> The OP isn't right, but his detractors like NecroticBinder are more wrong. <br /> <br /> Humanity in WoD is worse than our humanity in the real world. It's more apathetic, more corrupt, more foolish. Even in our own world, we have rampant systemic injustices and nobody in 'civilised' society is doing about it, and if they are, well, they're powerless. That's more apparent in the world of darkness, which is even more of a neoliberal nightmare than what we're living in. Humanity is weak, and is no more likely to rid itself of the vampire menace than it is to become a socialist utopia. There's actually very little incentive for anyone with a possition of power (A very self-selective bunch) to work against rather than with a powerful, immortal vampiric benefactor. If you're happy working with something immoral like the military industrial complex, what's a bloodsucker to you? <br /> <br /> Because of this, Vampire hunters in the WoD have always been either people at the very bottom fighting the man at the top, or dogmatic nutters (Yes, SAD is the latter). Neither of which presents an existential threat to vampires. If pre-nerf vampires ever got wind of a large organization hunting them, they'd descend, dominate, corrupt and destroy, so vampire hunters have always been small-off the grid groups. They need to be small and secretive to survive, and they have to be small because only madmen or those seriously and very personally agreived by vampires would decide to hunt them. When you consider the logistic nightmare of the so-called second inquisition, it clearly doesn't work. You need funding, backers, large information networks... You simply cannot stop pre-nerf Vampire characters from absolutely wrecking the system. There can be no global network of vampire hunters, because each group needs to be small and secretive and there's no feasible way to find other groups and share information with them without compromising themselves. <br /> <br /> The Masquerade has always been a two-way hornet's nest. The Vampires don't want to start anything with humans because, never mind nukes, Tanks and Jets will ruin them. Most of the Humans who know, don't want to know. They don't want to use tanks and jets and endanger countless lives, they want to ride the gravy train that the vampires offer. The overwhelming majority of politicians and government agents want to keep the status quo as is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:44:34-07:00","id":1379212,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379202#post1379202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given I mentioned Karsh, I think its kind of obvious I know there's other kinds of Elders. :-p<br /> <br /> They just dialed them down to be more manageable.<br /> <br /> Hence the Beckoning taking the oldest and most broken off the board.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They were manageable back then just required much more effort than now, apparently. Karsh is not silly a concept to me - it's a cool concept which makes elders and vampiric populace overall more varied. having only one specific type of elder as a default model is uninspiring and I am pretty sure they won't go that way.<br /> <br /> We also don't know how many or whom exactly the Beckoning summoned; and what's most important we have no idea what's actually happening there. If they are being munched, or if they are munching someone else, or if they are guarding their grandsires against the crusaders. I thought it's quite obvious that the Gehenna war, the Beckoning and everything around it are developer tools only - for now, distant turmoils and threats looming in the horizon, not actual events involing your cainite neighbor. Guess we need to make sure we are not too quick with assumptions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T03:45:32-07:00","id":1379213,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> surprisingly, I agree with you 100%.<br /> <br /> Eisenhower said that. Which is really ironic, cause he WAS the military-industrial complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T04:11:51-07:00","id":1379218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379208#post1379208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This discussion again.<br /> The OP isn't right, but his detractors like NecroticBinder are more wrong.<br /> <br /> Humanity in WoD is worse than our humanity in the real world. It's more apathetic, more corrupt, more foolish. Even in our own world, we have rampant systemic injustices and nobody in 'civilised' society is doing about it, and if they are, well, they're powerless. That's more apparent in the world of darkness, which is even more of a neoliberal nightmare than what we're living in. Humanity is weak, and is no more likely to rid itself of the vampire menace than it is to become a socialist utopia. There's actually very little incentive for anyone with a possition of power (A very self-selective bunch) to work against rather than with a powerful, immortal vampiric benefactor. If you're happy working with something immoral like the military industrial complex, what's a bloodsucker to you?<br /> <br /> Because of this, Vampire hunters in the WoD have always been either people at the very bottom fighting the man at the top, or dogmatic nutters (Yes, SAD is the latter). Neither of which presents an existential threat to vampires. If pre-nerf vampires ever got wind of a large organization hunting them, they'd descend, dominate, corrupt and destroy, so vampire hunters have always been small-off the grid groups. They need to be small and secretive to survive, and they have to be small because only madmen or those seriously and very personally agreived by vampires would decide to hunt them. When you consider the logistic nightmare of the so-called second inquisition, it clearly doesn't work. You need funding, backers, large information networks... You simply cannot stop pre-nerf Vampire characters from absolutely wrecking the system. There can be no global network of vampire hunters, because each group needs to be small and secretive and there's no feasible way to find other groups and share information with them without compromising themselves.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade has always been a two-way hornet's nest. The Vampires don't want to start anything with humans because, never mind nukes, Tanks and Jets will ruin them. Most of the Humans who know, don't want to know. They don't want to use tanks and jets and endanger countless lives, they want to ride the gravy train that the vampires offer. The overwhelming majority of politicians and government agents want to keep the status quo as is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You underestimate the inherent xenophobia of humans; given the most adept and powerful among them find out there are Others who predate on their own 'prey' - the 99% - they are sure eager to teach the Others not to bite more than they could chew, and would easily band together to achieve just that.<br /> I am not saying Second Inquisition is some heroic stuff to save humanity from nighttime predators. My main point in it doing its best to defeat a competitor and given the scale of the threat, it's coherent enough to succeed.<br /> There is a high possibility that it is being aided or even directed by a group of powerful vampires, too.<br /> Another thing is control. You can control a military industry complex. You cannot control a bloodsucker who wields supernatural powers which deny laws of physics therefore between something you control or can control and understand, and something you cannot, you rather choose the former. Of course the types who prefer individual benefit over common would be present, I am sure we gonna see the downsides and failures of SI in their book; but I wouldn't count on the individual cases of information and security leaks to undermine the effort on such a scale (top world' security services and military complexes working together) - again, for now. Those who fall to vampiric corruption are a nice plot tool - a cracks in the monolith through which the vampires could spread their influence, slowly, nothing in WoD is invincible; but for now, a vampire setting needed a good shakeup. I see no problem with humanity itself providing it - again, they are and were the biggest threat to cainites. I don't make the rules, it's WW idea in the fist place.<br /> <br /> What I'd say the undeniable Vampire's advantage is time. 'Outlive your enemies', as the Book of Nod goes. Humans age; vampires don't. The same way they survived back then - go down and wait for as long as necessary while the most adept of your minions work to slowly spread corruption to undermine the efforts to find and burn you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T04:17:09-07:00","id":1379220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There can be no global network of vampire hunters, because each group needs to be small and secretive and there's no feasible way to find other groups and share information with them without compromising themselves. </div> </div> </div>There ARE global networks of Hunters, though,<br /> <br /> * The Society of Leopold<br /> * The Arcanum<br /> * The NATIONAL SECURITY AGENCY<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T04:25:57-07:00","id":1379224,"title":"","content":"To be honest I do not think Second Inquisition can't do this<br /> <br /> After all, mortals are the greatest and foremost in the WoD. All splats use and fear them. Numerous mortals can overpower all supernaural badass. When a 4th gens like Ur-Shulgi face 100, 1000, or even 10000 soilders euipped with high-tech weapons, he will also be kicked off. That's the World of &quot;Darkness&quot;, all splats must hide deeply or they will be f**ked off<br /> <br /> *And I want to see other supernaural sects are involved in SI, for example, Technoracy, imbueds, garou or even other vampires (Salubris ,Ferox, etc.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379220#post1379220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There ARE global networks of Hunters, though,<br /> <br /> * The Society of Leopold<br /> * The Arcanum<br /> * The NATIONAL SECURITY AGENCY</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters (imbueds) or hunters? Former has the most noted hunter-net but it's a bit loose and uneffective, I don't hear more global organizations, and no more new about them in 20th Anni. Latter, well, are numerous as you say","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-07-2020, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T04:26:14-07:00","id":1379225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition#post1379003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like the Second Inquisition.. It just feels.. so cliche and horrible. From somehow breaking into Schrecknet, then the Vatican getting involved, then this group of mortals just wrecking everything.. Yeah no. The Camarilla nor Sabbat wouldn't be taken out by such a thing in their pre-V5 unnerfed state realistically (even with the whole Beckoning nonsense, lets be real). The worst egress of this Gary-Stu faction was how they somehow <i>bombed</i> the Vienna Chantry- a magic fortress/university basically that has probably existed longer than all the operators within the SI combined and literally can't be comprehended by mortals at all because it always teleports IIRC. Not only that this Gary-Stu faction has cleared out cities with high level Kindred, some Anchillae too who probably weren't compelled by the Beckoning.. somehow... The Second Inquisition.. is horrible.<br /> <br /> What would have been way more compelling was to bring the Imbued in as the primary Human antagonists instead of the SI. More interesting, has clear abilities that would've allowed them to spot Vienna in the first place with True Sight, a clear precedent of their power is known so there is a logical justification for how their KO'ing the Camarilla and the Sabbat (<i>especially the Sabbat</i>), and they would've been generally more compelling. Because I don't understand the fuss about the Second Inquisition, their faction doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do think things would have improved if they introduced the Imbued into the equation, it makes sense, and the Imbued aren't brand new Anymore, they have been around for twenty years some would join a conspiracy like the second inquisition.<br /> <br /> To make it believable you have to take into account they probably had some support in the background by the technocracy, and Vienna was likely sabotaged on the inside. Also True Faith works as kind of the one true kryptonite for Vampires, it nullifies psychic effects from Dominate to Obfuscate, and it burns away Thaumaturgy. And I guess the Vatican has access to True Faith, Sorcery, I would say some Choristers, and type of Numina that would probably be a mix of Sorcery and Faith, and finally Holy Relics. Like Fragments of the True Cross, the Lantern of Constantine, Saint Bones you name it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T04:29:49-07:00","id":1379226,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> also a good point. I think the Second Inquisition uses the information gathered by the NSA to help track down other Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T04:55:48-07:00","id":1379229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379224#post1379224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunters (imbueds) or hunters? Former has the most noted hunter-net but it's a bit loose and uneffective, I don't hear more global organizations, and no more new about them in 20th Anni. Latter, well, are numerous as you say</div> </div> </div> </div>The Hunters Hunted organizations had their own books.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.gr-assets.com/images/S/compressed.photo.goodreads.com/books/1387722890l/168316.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://d1rw89lz12ur5s.cloudfront.net/photo/wildthingsgames/file/4cb1b425ec2a42d3a7332225206d424e/large/70653374_393914158177546_2781412570257424384_n.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/0/0e/03064.jpg/revision/latest/top-crop/width/360/height/450?cb=20061110005504\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T05:03:26-07:00","id":1379231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379229#post1379229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Hunters Hunted organizations had their own books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, and all sleeper hunter books<br /> <br /> Demon Hunter X<br /> Inquisition<br /> The Hunters Hunted I and II<br /> Project Twilight<br /> Halls of Arcanum<br /> Quick and Dead<br /> The Autumn People<br /> The First Contact<br /> Messiahs and Destroyers<br /> <br /> But you say &quot;global&quot;, whcih may need to filter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T05:06:48-07:00","id":1379232,"title":"","content":"Well, this thread blew up in a single day. Honestly, though, not surprised. I swear, every week there's a similar thread about something else. The nossie network, the inquisition, the tremere...<br /> <br /> Reminds me a lot of the old edition wars with D&amp;D.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 04-07-2020, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T05:08:02-07:00","id":1379233,"title":"","content":"Oh I don't remember Messiahs and Destroyers what was that one? Demon?<br /> <br /> Oh and we have Dark Age Inquisition too, but that was the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T05:34:36-07:00","id":1379237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379233#post1379233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh I don't remember Messiahs and Destroyers what was that one? Demon?<br /> <br /> Oh and we have Dark Age Inquisition too, but that was the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah Demon<br /> <br /> And aren't Inquisitors supernaturals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T05:43:43-07:00","id":1379240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379237#post1379237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah Demon<br /> <br /> And aren't Inquisitors supernaturals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who aren't supernaturals now a days am I right?! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Dark Age Inquisitors were mortals that essentially used secret Numina, so it was like they took the concept of Hunters Hunted, put it in sword and sorcery times and make it a more concrete hardcover splat rather then softcover minisplat. I don't know I still need to actually get/read this one myself. :P<br /> <br /> Did Messiahs and Destroyers present new options or new groups? It was dedicated to having Priest and Rabbis and what not channeling faith against the Fallen if I recall, but I never got a copy myself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T07:27:44-07:00","id":1379250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379218#post1379218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You underestimate the inherent xenophobia of humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Xenophobia and racism are, to put it bluntly, poor people problems. The people with actual power very rarely truly care. Which is why, again, hunters work as yokels who fear The Man, Hunters who are dogmatic extremists, but don't work for goverment agencies. Rich people, notably the clever ones, encourage &quot;ISMs&quot; in poor people, but they often don't have those views themselves. It seems disingenuous to have large and interconnected cabals of powerful people who aim to take down vampires. Because while there might be one or two there aren't enough to justify a large scale &quot;second inquisition&quot;. Hell I'd go out on a limb and tell you that someone's willingness to hunt down all the vampires is inversely proportional to competence, if not life expectancy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379220#post1379220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There ARE global networks of Hunters, though,<br /> <br /> * The Society of Leopold<br /> * The Arcanum<br /> * The NATIONAL SECURITY AGENCY</div> </div> </div> </div>*Are dogmatic nutters, have true faith, have tons of false information, aren't really that well connected and operate in a manner I aprove of. <br /> *Not actually a hunter organization. <br /> *National. It's in the freaking name. But more seriously, pre-nerf this is something vampires would easily put their tendrils into the moment they start acting up. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T11:04:19-07:00","id":1379279,"title":"","content":"Imma look that up on DTRPG. Messiahs and Destroyers. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T11:10:00-07:00","id":1379281,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> I agree with you in general, but if the power elite saw a vampire or a group of vampires as a threat to their power base they might feel compelled to act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T11:55:49-07:00","id":1379291,"title":"","content":"Indeed, that might happen on rare occasion, but for the most part they're not a threat to their power base. Infact, I'm pretty sure most times a vampire is a boon to any incumbent person of office. Juicy Financial support, keeping good, righteous and moral people from becoming effective competitors, a great contact for illicit pleasures, possibly blood that keeps one healthy, longlived and strong. Most politicians in the WoD don't do it to make the world better, but because they want lobby money and financial friends. When they retire from politics they want a good possition in a bank granted to them. The Good people are kept out of politics by the establishment, and vampires are a small part of that. In the case where a vampire goes against a corrupt official, it's almost always because some other vampire has been using them against the interloping vampire, and even if a vampire did work against a politician, how does the politician know it's the work of vampires? If the politician did learn that they've been budying up with vampires, how would it benefit them to work against them? (Look at some goverment pedophile scandals for reforence) Having a vampire above you is no different from any other immoral special interest group. <br /> <br /> vampires are more carrot than stick for the elites and those in power.<br /> And, ultimately if common sense fails, Vampires can spot a rogue element and simply use their powers or otherwise get nasty. Many that would be opposed to vampires would be to afraid to ever act on it; They have so much to lose, little chance of victory, and much less to gain.<br /> <br /> Ergo, people that both cling to power and have a hatred of vampires are very, very few, and their days are numbered. There can never reasonably be anything big enough to justify such a threatening global SI. And as these few people are largely either people who have lost everything and who seek personal vengence and dogmatic extremists, they're not going to play well with others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T12:09:52-07:00","id":1379294,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> interesting. I\u2019ll keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> What do you think of ghouling though? No one in that social class is gonna voluntarily drink from a vampire if they know that the Blood Bond will turn them into a virtual slave. Plus, except for a few people who are into goth stuff, most people don\u2019t like drinking blood in the first place. Maybe as an initiation, like for Skull and Bones or one of the Final Clubs...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T12:52:41-07:00","id":1379305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379294#post1379294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> interesting. I\u2019ll keep that in mind.<br /> <br /> What do you think of ghouling though? No one in that social class is gonna voluntarily drink from a vampire if they know that the Blood Bond will turn them into a virtual slave. Plus, except for a few people who are into goth stuff, most people don\u2019t like drinking blood in the first place. Maybe as an initiation, like for Skull and Bones or one of the Final Clubs...</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember you can hide blood in other food and drink. Mysterious Wine or rare meats, or even gelatin or soup.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T12:56:54-07:00","id":1379306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379250#post1379250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But more seriously, pre-nerf this is something <i>vampires would easily put their tendrils into the moment they start acting up</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one of the main reasons the second inquisition happened. The vampires started putting their tendrils everywhere and then got cocky. Cocky enough to start using these agencies to hurt other vampires. Hell, I bet that even after the Inquisition started some vampires still gave out their rivals to them as an easy way to get them out of the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T13:03:35-07:00","id":1379308,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> thanks. Hadn\u2019t thought of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T13:44:49-07:00","id":1379315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackheartz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379306#post1379306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is one of the main reasons the second inquisition happened. The vampires started putting their tendrils everywhere and then got cocky. Cocky enough to start using these agencies to hurt other vampires. Hell, I bet that even after the Inquisition started some vampires still gave out their rivals to them as an easy way to get them out of the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.... It's reasoning, but it's bad reasoning.<br /> <br /> First, The logical and likely resolution for this is a crackdown. The princes start executing people they think have been talking with the authorities (All hail tyranny), forms a clean up team to deal with the agency, and everything becomes hunky-dory. Licks will fear using mortal authorities again. <br /> <br /> Second... This doesn't actually justify a global inquisition. On a small scale? Sure. But getting the secret cell hidden within MI5 to cooperate with the secret hidden cell within Mi6 would be extremely difficult, let alone getting either british agency to co-operate with an alleged secret cell within a french agency, an Iranian agency... The more connections a secret vampire hunting cell makes, the easier it is for vampires to root them out. In the hypotherical scenario where all the inquisitors started working together, it'd take a single night to work out where they all are and a month to clean house, and that's assuming the SI are clever about it. <br /> <br /> I actually can't imagine it gets to that point. Like, I can see my characters pointing yokels or the Society of Leopold at my vampire enemies, but actually using a nation level or global level security agency? To directly go after vampires? It's all fun and games to point out that vampires can be arrogant, but are they that arrogant? How have they lived this long? Whoever wrote this nonsense didn't spend enough time in the shoes of a vampire. I get it, player characters can be morons and pull this kinda nonsense all the time, but PCs are far and away exceptions, not the norm. This reads like a DM feeling good about punishing a player or two, rather than something approaching reasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T14:14:05-07:00","id":1379322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379315#post1379315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This.... It's reasoning, but it's bad reasoning.<br /> <br /> First, The logical and likely resolution for this is a crackdown. The princes start executing people they think have been talking with the authorities (All hail tyranny), forms a clean up team to deal with the agency, and everything becomes hunky-dory. Licks will fear using mortal authorities again.<br /> <br /> Second... This doesn't actually justify a global inquisition. On a small scale? Sure. But getting the secret cell hidden within MI5 to cooperate with the secret hidden cell within Mi6 would be extremely difficult, let alone getting either british agency to co-operate with an alleged secret cell within a french agency, an Iranian agency... The more connections a secret vampire hunting cell makes, the easier it is for vampires to root them out. In the hypotherical scenario where all the inquisitors started working together, it'd take a single night to work out where they all are and a month to clean house, and that's assuming the SI are clever about it.<br /> <br /> I actually can't imagine it gets to that point. Like, I can see my characters pointing yokels or the Society of Leopold at my vampire enemies, but actually using a nation level or global level security agency? To directly go after vampires? It's all fun and games to point out that vampires can be arrogant, but are they that arrogant? How have they lived this long? Whoever wrote this nonsense didn't spend enough time in the shoes of a vampire. I get it, player characters can be morons and pull this kinda nonsense all the time, but PCs are far and away exceptions, not the norm. This reads like a DM feeling good about punishing a player or two, rather than something approaching reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is the prime example of the logic behind the dislike of the SI. Elders are undeniable blood gods who never make mistakes and can outwit any puny human, and they certainly aren't arrogant enough to utilize the government influence that they so carefully curate. They also perfectly understand the forces that they are toying with and would never risk themselves.<br /> <br /> An exaggeration but close enough. It is apparently beyond possibility that intelligence agencies with massive information gathering tools, and technology that elders don't understand (And don't tell me they do when the average person doesn't, and elders have been shown in every edition to take some time to play catch up, let alone stay on the cutting edge) who get used to take out targets might find out about vampires. So you have two groups that know of them, the ones that find out about them indirectly and the pawns who manage to get the information out before they are 'fixed' like they normally would be.<br /> <br /> Vampires haven't exactly been shown to be quick learners. &quot;Oh, the anarch revolt happened because we were oppressing the neonates? Well let's keep doing that with a slightly better veneer.&quot; &quot;Using Humans to hunt vampires lead to the inquisition? Let's keep doing that.&quot; Etc. And these elements weren't introduced in V5 but are from previous editions. Vampires have lived this long because up until recently communication was limited, observation almost always had to be done in person, and data was kept on paper. For the purposes of adapting, I'd argue that vampires and humans haven't ever had to adapt as fast as we have in the recent decades. The industrial revolution? Just made hunting easier for vampires, more crowds to blend in with. Fancy new swords? Still not scary to kindred.<br /> <br /> It has been a theme in almost every edition that elders have been caught off guard by some of the new inventions that have came out of human society, and no. It's not just nukes or missiles.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T14:14:16-07:00","id":1379323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379315#post1379315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This.... It's reasoning, but it's bad reasoning.<br /> <br /> First, The logical and likely resolution for this is a crackdown. The princes start executing people they think have been talking with the authorities (All hail tyranny), forms a clean up team to deal with the agency, and everything becomes hunky-dory. Licks will fear using mortal authorities again.<br /> <br /> Second... This doesn't actually justify a global inquisition. On a small scale? Sure. But getting the secret cell hidden within MI5 to cooperate with the secret hidden cell within Mi6 would be extremely difficult, let alone getting either british agency to co-operate with an alleged secret cell within a french agency, an Iranian agency... The more connections a secret vampire hunting cell makes, the easier it is for vampires to root them out. In the hypotherical scenario where all the inquisitors started working together, it'd take a single night to work out where they all are and a month to clean house, and that's assuming the SI are clever about it.<br /> <br /> I actually can't imagine it gets to that point. Like, I can see my characters pointing yokels or the Society of Leopold at my vampire enemies, but actually using a nation level or global level security agency? To directly go after vampires? It's all fun and games to point out that vampires can be arrogant, but are they that arrogant? How have they lived this long? Whoever wrote this nonsense didn't spend enough time in the shoes of a vampire. I get it, player characters can be morons and pull this kinda nonsense all the time, but PCs are far and away exceptions, not the norm. This reads like a DM feeling good about punishing a player or two, rather than something approaching reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1. The Princes and the upper echelons of the Camarilla CAUSED it. This has been detailed out in threads before. It got out of their hands because of agents who were already in the know.<br /> 2. It's conspiracies within various government orgs, with the biggest being FIRSTLIGHT. When you put enough dots together, people who have seen the implausible will work together; . The majority of it is repurposed assets, along with a couple of actual organizations. It's also not like this happened overnight, this started in 2002 post-9/11 (which, bud, if you don't believe that the government and people in general gets crazy about 'the other' ..).<br /> 3. You keep acting like the Kindred were in control of the entire government. They weren't, haven't been written that way, since 1e/2e. The various books that talk about the government groups like Project Twilight talk about using ghouls and influence, but it's not like they had The President and the Senate blood bound, let alone things like the head of the NSA, FBI, etc. And the books talk about how the SI eventually rooted out the compromised agents.<br /> 4. Vampires are arrogant. They have lived this long by not putting a target on their backs for all of humanity to see (and we round back about to why elders don't lead from the front 99% of the time). But, y'know, Sabbat barely caring about the Masquerade, Camarilla failing to uphold it in places, the Anarchs not giving a care about the Masquerade. There's a breaking point there, especially when vampires are doing terrorist-style shit like 'drive car bombs into buildings'.<br /> 5. Take a single night to work out everything? Wow. I get that you don't like the idea of mortals being a threat to Kindred, but damn man, what kind of insane control do your vampires have? And if this is the case, why even have a Masquerade at all, if they're strong enough to do this they're strong enough in your eyes to openly rule humanity.. The way you describe vampires from your POV, you think your setting would be like the high Vampiric rule ages of the Vampire Hunter D world, if these vampires are such infallible and invincible blood gods that control all aspects of every government ever.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 04-07-2020, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T14:14:58-07:00","id":1379324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379305#post1379305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Remember you can hide blood in other food and drink. Mysterious Wine or rare meats, or even gelatin or soup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can't do that in V5 anymore. Blood bonds must occur directly from the vein.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T14:35:11-07:00","id":1379326,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24893\" data-vbnamecard=\"24893\">Necroticbinder</a> hmmm. That does make it more difficult. Would my idea of drinking the elder\u2019s blood as part of like a club initiation ritual work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:15:18-07:00","id":1379332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379250#post1379250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Xenophobia and racism are, to put it bluntly, poor people problems. The people with actual power very rarely truly care. Which is why, again, hunters work as yokels who fear The Man, Hunters who are dogmatic extremists, but don't work for goverment agencies. Rich people, notably the clever ones, encourage &quot;ISMs&quot; in poor people, but they often don't have those views themselves. It seems disingenuous to have large and interconnected cabals of powerful people who aim to take down vampires. Because while there might be one or two there aren't enough to justify a large scale &quot;second inquisition&quot;. Hell I'd go out on a limb and tell you that someone's willingness to hunt down all the vampires is inversely proportional to competence, if not life expectancy.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I would rather you didn't equate xenophobia and racism. The phenomenon of xenophobia isn't with us because some are poor and that condition forces their racism (it's just a part of the problem). Xenophobia is fear of the other, and a very strong, built-in evolutionary tool (or atavism, from another perspective). Since the first two caves, cavemen in one were wary of the cavemen in the other, and vice versa. The depth and severity of 'wary' can vary greatly, as we've seen throughout human history. Racism is but one facet of it, xenophobia permeates any given group.<br /> <br /> People who are in power can or cannot care about racism, but they do care about other groups competing with them let alone threatening their dominance. Getting up there is no easy fit, and to think of one who accomplished that to forsake the ultimate control of his/her reality in favor of an alliance with a creature which is not simply of another strata or class or skin colour or faith or language or music taste, but of another freaking species wielding unknown powers - is ridiculous.<br /> Since you pretend to know about rich people motivations and habits you would've known there are not so many fools among them willing to take a risk of trying to outwit a supernatural, uncontrollable creature when their own mind and will are at stake.<br /> (Or simply what <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> said)<br /> <br /> Of course if your vampires aren't playing power fantasy and just jedi-mind-trick their way through Masquarade. Seriously, White Wolf should've named the game Vampire: The Dominate then. Whoever ghouls as many yes-men as possible and is the first to get mental Disciplines 5+ powers wins, end of story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:30:38-07:00","id":1379333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379324#post1379324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, you can't do that in V5 anymore. Blood bonds must occur directly from the vein.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh really interesting. Cleans things up. Before revised made a point that you couldn't Embrace unless the blood leaves the sire and enters the childe with no intermediary vessel. They forgot this fact when they described Netchurches experiments embracing with a needle of vitae, and Cappadocius embraced using a sacred grail to contain his vitae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:43:00-07:00","id":1379341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379315#post1379315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually can't imagine it gets to that point. Like, I can see my characters pointing yokels or the Society of Leopold at my vampire enemies, but actually using a nation level or global level security agency? To directly go after vampires? It's all fun and games to point out that vampires can be arrogant, but are they that arrogant? How have they lived this long? Whoever wrote this nonsense didn't spend enough time in the shoes of a vampire. I get it, player characters can be morons and pull this kinda nonsense all the time, but PCs are far and away exceptions, not the norm. This reads like a DM feeling good about punishing a player or two, rather than something approaching reasonable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't this taken from V20 canon, possibly even Revised? The Cam started trying to use the NSA as a weapon against the Sabbat as soon as the PATRIOT act passed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T15:54:32-07:00","id":1379344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379250#post1379250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Xenophobia and racism are, to put it bluntly, poor people problems. The people with actual power very rarely truly care.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is extremely dumb as many dictators follow ethno-nationalist agendas as well as several billionaires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which is why, again, hunters work as yokels who fear The Man, Hunters who are dogmatic extremists, but don't work for goverment agencies. Rich people, notably the clever ones, encourage &quot;ISMs&quot; in poor people, but they often don't have those views themselves. It seems disingenuous to have large and interconnected cabals of powerful people who aim to take down vampires. Because while there might be one or two there aren't enough to justify a large scale &quot;second inquisition&quot;. Hell I'd go out on a limb and tell you that someone's willingness to hunt down all the vampires is inversely proportional to competence, if not life expectancy. </div> </div> </div>Even by this logic, it's much more beneficial to wipe out vampires and take their stuff than make a deal with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> *Are dogmatic nutters, have true faith, have tons of false information, aren't really that well connected and operate in a manner I aprove of.<br /> *Not actually a hunter organization.<br /> *National. It's in the freaking name. But more seriously, pre-nerf this is something vampires would easily put their tendrils into the moment they start acting up. </div> </div> </div>1. The Society of Leopold is a branch of the Catholic Church which, while not the richest institution in the world, is a global society with a billion members.<br /> 2. The Arcanum is a hunter organization as it has an unlimited amount of data on the various supernatural factions in the world that could, at any point, be turned against the Kindred if they became hostile--which they almost certainly would according to the sourcebook on them and were confirmed as doing in THE FALL OF LONDON.<br /> 3. The National Security Agency's reach is not limited to the United States unless you don't understand a single thing about how US intelligence services work or the relationship of intelligence agencies to the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> Also, you do realize we've ALREADY had the National Security Agency described in the World of Darkness. I did a thread re-reading PROJECT: TWILIGHT and it talked about how the undead don't understand the NSA and how it is primarily controlled by the Technocracy but is becoming independent.<br /> <br /> 1. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1351194-wir-project-twilight-a-werewolf-book-now-very-useful-for-vampires\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...l-for-vampires</a><br /> <br /> 2. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1351194-wir-project-twilight-a-werewolf-book-now-very-useful-for-vampires/page5\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...vampires/page5</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T18:53:12-07:00","id":1379370,"title":"","content":"Bottom line: Vampires have allies among the power elite, but they also have enemies. And those enemies have a lot of influence and financial support they can throw behind global hunter organizations like the Second Inquisition (which is already backed by the Vatican and at least certain elements of the United States government). Certainly some hunters are lone wolves or radical extremists, but not all (or even most).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T22:08:44-07:00","id":1379410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379370#post1379370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bottom line: Vampires have allies among the power elite, but they also have enemies. And those enemies have a lot of influence and financial support they can throw behind global hunter organizations like the Second Inquisition (which is already backed by the Vatican and at least certain elements of the United States government). Certainly some hunters are lone wolves or radical extremists, but not all (or even most).</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the big thing is the idea that this IS a new thing for Vampires. They were arrogant about their power and influence but forgot that the World of Darkness has other players inside it.<br /> <br /> And sometimes those players are humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-07T23:35:37-07:00","id":1379418,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think the Second Inquisition make a great antagonist group. They are similar to The Technocracy in Mage, insofar that they are ruthless and coldly scientific in what they do, but aside from somebody who is a vampire and has a vested interest in survival, they actually have a sympathetic point of view at their heart.<br /> <br /> I also like the fact that, in any given scene that is starting to lag or lose interest from the players, I can throw in some random, unannounced attack as the SI pounce. Vampires are usually tough enough to deal with them, but it can spook them, which is cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":". 04-08-2020, 10:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T02:20:44-07:00","id":1379435,"title":"","content":"I really think you guys want a moral argument: The Princes played with fire so they got burned. It sounds right and righteous.<br /> I can see a burn, but I can't see them going up in flames.<br /> <br /> -The Bigger the Organization, the easier it is to infiltrate and take it apart.<br /> -The more secretive the organization, the harder it is for them to make contact with other secretive organizations.<br /> <br /> Even if the prince was the one using alphabet people against their rivals, the standard procedure would be to find scapegoats, dispatch cleaning teams, and if for some bizzare reason the prince went for a global organization (IE the CIA) and didn't have great control over the people they were using (not terribly likely, but possible) They'd merely need to call in a favour of an archon or higher; some international kindred who deals with international problems, who would form teams and....<br /> <br /> Lastly, even if alphabet people found out about vampires... why would they persue? No doubt, the leaders of such organizations are in the pockets of the rich and powerful, which includes no short list of vampires. Vampires in the USA are as threatening to the country as... neoliberalism, and if you've read any theory, these agencies are there to support the status quo of neoliberalism or post-colonialism or whatever, not to make the world a better place. Moreso in the world of darkness, People climb to the heads of these organizations to be powerful and recieve generous goodwill donations, not to be nice people. Why wouldn't they be on the side of vampires? All one needs to do is rekindle friendships with the heads and higher ups of these organizations and get them to clean house. SAD could exist because it was a secretive element that nobody else really knew about. But if you really had the NSA go after vampires, how long would it take for it's senior officers to change their minds after some small convincing? Even if Vampires didn't have supernatural social powers, it wouldn't take all that much to steer the ship back in the right direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T02:26:34-07:00","id":1379436,"title":"","content":"...Agencies are composed of people, and not everyone sold their soul and are so jaded they would ignore evidence to an insanely world-shaking Conspiracy that Vampires exist. The Status quo is always shaky and on the precipice of falling. Yes people are corrupt and that is how the conspiracy lasted so long. But eventually people start finding out about Vampire Evidence. Revised Edition started the idea that portions of the Government discovered Vampires exist and they built machines to detect them along with people possessed by Vampires and ghost. This is twenty years later and that leak that started a small conspiracy blossomed into a Global Reckoning level conspiracy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T03:22:32-07:00","id":1379438,"title":"","content":"They would both need to gather allies and resources and keep their activities secret from their superiors and enemies (and not get any moles in their organization, which is so difficult with pre-nerf dominate) It'd be truly, logistically impossible to get something of the scale of the second inquisition. Again, we're reduced to a few underdogs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T03:31:36-07:00","id":1379439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379438#post1379438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would both need to gather allies and resources and keep their activities secret from their superiors and enemies (and not get any moles in their organization, which is so difficult with pre-nerf dominate) It'd be truly, logistically impossible to get something of the scale of the second inquisition. Again, we're reduced to a few underdogs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Logistically difficult not impossible. This is just the beginning of the Second Inquisition, later they probably would spill out so the world discovers some of it.<br /> <br /> But come on the Week of Nightmares killed over a million people and they covered that up, well the Techies did. <br /> <br /> But we already have so many conspiracies hiding growing and staying secret. This is the inevitable result of the modern world, the Camarilla probably squashed a dozen almost inquisitions eventually one will pop up like this with too much inertia, and once they got Rome on Board they had True Faith Users which does a damn number on Vampire Mind Whammies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T04:36:55-07:00","id":1379446,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> you make some good points, but you have an ideological axe to grind, and I think it blurs your vision when it comes to gaming scenarios. I\u2019m not saying anything about my own personal views, but A LOT of very powerful people support \u201cneoliberalism.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t mean to get personal, but you made your ideology very clear in your previous posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T04:42:19-07:00","id":1379448,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12002_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12002\" data-vbnamecard=\"12002\">CTPhipps</a> very good point. It did happen once before, during the First Inquisition, but a lot of vampires aren\u2019t old enough to remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T04:51:10-07:00","id":1379452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379435#post1379435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really think you guys want a moral argument: The Princes played with fire so they got burned. It sounds right and righteous. I can see a burn, but I can't see them going up in flames.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it going up in flames? The Camarilla hasn't fallen. The Anarchs are more powerful than ever. Only the Sabbat is on the backfoot and that's questionable since they seem to be becoming a bunch of super-vampires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -The Bigger the Organization, the easier it is to infiltrate and take it apart. </div> </div> </div>How does that apply to the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> -The more secretive the organization, the harder it is for them to make contact with other secretive organizations. </div> </div> </div>How does that help the Camarilla?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even if the prince was the one using alphabet people against their rivals, the standard procedure would be to find scapegoats, dispatch cleaning teams, and if for some bizzare reason the prince went for a global organization (IE the CIA) and didn't have great control over the people they were using (not terribly likely, but possible) They'd merely need to call in a favour of an archon or higher; some international kindred who deals with international problems, who would form teams and.... </div> </div> </div>In THE HUNTERS HUNTED and PROJECT: TWILIGHT, Felicity Price was a high ranking member of the National Security Agency who the Camarilla dominated and used to gather information on the Sabbat and Anarchs in order to assist their efforts against them. She was thoroughly conditioned and utterly loyal. In THE CAMARILLA, we found out that her Dominator was Beckoned and thus her mind-control was broken. Being a genius, she gathered all of her data on the Camarilla, Sabbat, and Anarchs before presenting it to the rest of the NSA. This was enough to allow them to gather enough information to break the Masquerade and build the basis for the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> I point out Felicity Price dates back to 1st Edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lastly, even if alphabet people found out about vampires... why would they persue? </div> </div> </div>* Felicity Price was a meat puppet for two decades. So she has an issue. By herself, she possesses access to billions of dollars and the full might of the US intelligence network.<br /> * The Camarilla has access to powers that make it an existential threat to democracy or your corporate overlords. The Sabbat kill a lot of civilians every year. So do the Anarchs.<br /> * When I think of people who react rationally and without anger in a crisis, I think the US intelligence services.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No doubt, the leaders of such organizations are in the pockets of the rich and powerful, which includes no short list of vampires. Vampires in the USA are as threatening to the country as... neoliberalism, and if you've read any theory, these agencies are there to support the status quo of neoliberalism or post-colonialism or whatever, not to make the world a better place. Moreso in the world of darkness, People climb to the heads of these organizations to be powerful and recieve generous goodwill donations, not to be nice people. Why wouldn't they be on the side of vampires? All one needs to do is rekindle friendships with the heads and higher ups of these organizations and get them to clean house. SAD could exist because it was a secretive element that nobody else really knew about. But if you really had the NSA go after vampires, how long would it take for it's senior officers to change their minds after some small convincing? Even if Vampires didn't have supernatural social powers, it wouldn't take all that much to steer the ship back in the right direction. </div> </div> </div>The funny thing is the fact that the Second Inquisition isn't actually that big of a response to the world. According to THE CAMARILLA, they gave the Society of Leopold a billion dollars, a bunch of US military hardware, and helped recruit a couple of thousand new members from Catholic members of Special Forces units over the world. They've also been allowing the Society of Leopold free reign to do their business without interference with law enforcement.<br /> <br /> That by itself probably is responsible for a few thousand vampire deaths.<br /> <br /> Operation: Antigen was the Society of Saint George [Church of England Inquisition], Arcanum, and the London Police Force working with the help of Mithras as well as his massive resources to exterminate all of the vampires in the city that weren't part of his cult. That is basically the TREMERE DID IT explanation everyone assumes that Vienna had but Mithras could have done it without the Inquisition.<br /> <br /> He just used the Inquisition to kill a hundred or more London vampires.<br /> <br /> We know the Harbingers of Skulls and Giovanni Neonates teamed up to wipe out the Mausoleum's Elders.<br /> <br /> And this basically IS the Inquisition's successes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T07:42:41-07:00","id":1379476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379446#post1379446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> you make some good points, but you have an ideological axe to grind, and I think it blurs your vision when it comes to gaming scenarios. I\u2019m not saying anything about my own personal views, but A LOT of very powerful people support \u201cneoliberalism.\u201d<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it does. <br /> Vampires are supported by neoliberals, conservatives, libertarians, fascists, whatever that thing the soviets tried was. Anything with a strong power structure with strong people at the top and weak people below. <br /> <br /> The world of Darkness and Vampire presents a microcosm for which to explore the macrocosm. If you are left leaning, you could point to the Ventrue as a big bad. If you are right leaning, it's the Toreador who are dragging society down. The WoD had clans/tribes/traditions that were analogues for a lot of things, they were exaggerated, and they made a statement about society because to some extent, they were true, they were real. There didn't need to be a political diatribe, the setting simply highlighted things from the real world and exaggerated them. <br /> <br /> That worked when things were true. When the microcosm doesn't line up with the macrocosm, it's wrong. The game is wrong. V5 doesn't give us this exaggerated reality, it gives us someone's wishful thinking. V5 gives us a setting where the people at the top are brought down and weakened, the law is going after the people at the top, and the people have become class concious to the point of the rebel group outsizing the establishment... What here is true? What here is real? V5 does not reflect reality. Vampire society is not a dark mirror of mortal society. Someone really did just make sweeping changes to fill their own wish fulfillment. It's completely out of touch. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379452#post1379452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is it going up in flames? The Camarilla hasn't fallen. The Anarchs are more powerful than ever.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs being larger than ever means the Camarilla has ceased to fulfil one of it's core purposes. Yeah i'd say it's up in flames. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does that apply to the Camarilla?How does that help the Camarilla? </div> </div> </div>I'm talking about the hunters here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I point out Felicity Price dates back to 1st Edition. </div> </div> </div>But the beckoning which enables her here is a 5th edition addition. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T09:43:34-07:00","id":1379486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379476#post1379476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think it does.<br /> Vampires are supported by neoliberals, conservatives, libertarians, fascists, whatever that thing the soviets tried was. Anything with a strong power structure with strong people at the top and weak people below.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Vampires hijack their power structures. They aren't supported by them. The issue is this implies that the people who become aware of vampires don't care because they are the powerful ones at the top. Various ideologies will support the rich and powerful for different reasons, from believing they may one day become one of them, to believing it to be their right to get that rich or one of a multitude of another reasons. Vampires however, are parasites who are often outside of these lines of thinking because guess what. You probably aren't going to become a vampire and it's harder to delude yourself into thinking that, Vampires have mind control powers and have to forcefully assault people to live, and they congregate in a giant suspicious society./<br /> <br /> As you have consistently, and thoroughly ignored because it might break through your cognitive dissonance, the MASQUERADE exists for a reason. V5 merely demonstrates exactly why that is, and it isn't just that the elders want more leeway to abuse people without having eyes on them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The world of Darkness and Vampire presents a microcosm for which to explore the macrocosm. If you are left leaning, you could point to the Ventrue as a big bad. If you are right leaning, it's the Toreador who are dragging society down. The WoD had clans/tribes/traditions that were analogues for a lot of things, they were exaggerated, and they made a statement about society because to some extent, they were true, they were real. There didn't need to be a political diatribe, the setting simply highlighted things from the real world and exaggerated them.<br /> <br /> That worked when things were true. When the microcosm doesn't line up with the macrocosm, it's wrong. The game is wrong. V5 doesn't give us this exaggerated reality, it gives us someone's wishful thinking. V5 gives us a setting where the people at the top are brought down and weakened, the law is going after the people at the top, and the people have become class concious to the point of the rebel group outsizing the establishment... What here is true? What here is real? V5 does not reflect reality. Vampire society is not a dark mirror of mortal society. Someone really did just make sweeping changes to fill their own wish fulfillment. It's completely out of touch. </div> </div> </div>Read: Please ignore this games punk history, it definitely wasn't political. Also, I get to define the terms of reality.<br /> <br /> V5 doesn't require much of an exaggeration because it's not about the people at the top being brought down and weakened, and the rebels outsizing the establishment has been a consistent thing. You know why? It's because we go back to: THIS GAME IS GOTHIC PUNK.<br /> <br /> So first off, there is rampant feelings of xenophobia throughout the world, and guess what vampires represent IN WORLD? The other. That scary, scary other. Terrorists, the boogey man, the shady criminal. Not only that, to get really topical, they represent a highly dangerous and infectious disease. The issue with V5 isn't that it's using wishful thinking, or exaggerated reality, it's giving us quite the opposite. Just a gothic flavored version of the real world, it doesn't need to be darker. But no, there is an axe to grind here and it has to be ground to dust.<br /> <br /> Let's go back to the rebels vs the establishment. Outside of the desire for that happening in places (Like the US) the anarchs may be more numerous, but they are also suffering much higher losses. The establishment is more falling beneath it's own weight and corruption. You know, as happens to organizations after a few hundred years.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Anarchs being larger than ever means the Camarilla has ceased to fulfil one of it's core purposes. Yeah i'd say it's up in flames.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm talking about the hunters here.<br /> <br /> <br /> But the beckoning which enables her here is a 5th edition addition.<br /> </div> </div> </div>Then it's a good thing you've demonstrated no understanding of the setting. Because the Camarilla's core purpose was to protect the elders from the anarchs and enforce the masquerade to the best of their ability. It was never 'be bigger than the anarchs' because it never was, and never would be. The Camarilla enforced strict control over embracing while the average anarch domain didn't care if you had fifteen childer.<br /> <br /> And thank you for the deflection on Ms. Price. It really exemplifies that your arguments are biased and fundamentally flawed. Don't address that her sire dying directly lead to some of the problems that vampires are facing. Instead point out that what killed her sire is an addition of 5e. It could have been anarchs, it could have been a house fire, or a regular group of hunters. The end result would have been her free of her bondage with knowledge of vampire societies capabilities and plenty of their actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>V5 is not VTM</i> </div> </div> </div>Because bias.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>-The Bigger the Organization, the easier it is to infiltrate and take it apart.</i> </div> </div> </div>This is also, ironically, an argument against your own argument. The Camarilla is a much bigger organization, as are the anarchs, and the sabbat than the SI. So it's a lot easier to find information on them and then use it than it would be for the vampires to find the SI.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","user":"Necroticbinder","date":". 04-08-2020, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T10:47:20-07:00","id":1379493,"title":"","content":"Cognitive dissonance? <br /> (Googles just to be absolutely certain) <br /> <br /> Ok. I want you to re-read the post you just made. Do you see any problems with it? Would you be getting so upset if I wasn't challenging you with some sort of truth? <br /> <br /> Now, I can safely dismiss most of it. Vampires are of course, supported by society. They are parasites, sure, but they are supported by society. Society supports landlords, there are people who make a living just from manipulating currency... There are people who make stuff, and there are people who just <i>own </i>stuff. Society works in a hierarchal way so that everyone higher than anyone else needs to support someone better than them. Someone who owns a store might be jealous of a millionaire, who might in turn be jealous of a billionaire, but neither are going to vote left to re-distribute the wealth, because they're both above the average person, and being above half of everyone is attractive. An officer of the law is granted attractive authority from a higher power, that higher power is beholden to influentual constituents, and influentual constituents... <br /> <br /> A vampire isn't really any different from any other human monster in this regard. Since I really should keep the sociology to myself, Let me get Hermes out: <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> &quot;That which is Below corresponds to that which is Above, and that which is Above corresponds to that which is Below, to accomplish the miracle of the One Thing. Thus, whatever happens on any level of reality (physical, emotional, or mental) also happens on every other level.&quot;</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Vampires are parasites, but they've completely integrated into the society of the world of darkness. They are apart of the rich and powerful, not a separate group of interlopers. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Let's move on to something new and actually worth addressing. </span></span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is also, ironically, an argument against your own argument. The Camarilla is a much bigger organization, as are the anarchs, and the sabbat than the SI. So it's a lot easier to find information on them and then use it than it would be for the vampires to find the SI. </div> </div> </div>Except they're not the same, are they? <br /> Pre-nerf, vampires could do some incredible things with Dominate and Auspex. There's a big difference in the capabilities of each to play cat and mouse, and to reap the rewards. If An inquisitor is caught (more likely) he/she will spill everything they know or go back to their comrades and go postal. If a vampire is caught, at best you'll get information on her rivals, at worst she'll trick you into a trap. If an inquisitor is lost, they'll be hard to replace. If a vampire is lost, it's free real estate to embrace. Undead society is incredibly loose; They aren't that well connected. They're city states with an international police force. There's a whole iceberg of reasons why Vampires can do it, and mortals can't. I don't actually care to get into it really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T11:42:00-07:00","id":1379504,"title":"","content":"So. Don't address the points, because it's easier to brush them off while still pretending that vampires are immortal blood gods who don't actually need the masquerade but uphold it because reasons. Also, let's not address that vampires are part of the rich, usually. But are also still an OTHER who has been hunted historically when found out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T14:54:19-07:00","id":1379525,"title":"","content":"I agree. SI are Gary Stu. <br /> <br /> Humanity is a threat to vampires if masquerade fall completely and things get nuclear. If all the humans fight, sure the vampires gonna lose. Now, what we have is a bunch of swat teams going places. <br /> <br /> Black ops cannot assault the fortress of the most powerfull bloodmages in the entire world and kill said bloodmages only because they want. The chantry teleport across dif. locations and have ward against tech that would turn the bombs dropped into harmless metal scrap... <br /> <br /> I don't think any gov. will acept give so much money to one secret org hunt vampires.<br /> I don't think so many countries across the world will gleefull make a deal to share military information (or any info at all).<br /> Neither all of this war gonna be keep secret for any longer.<br /> <br /> SI is solely the writers of NuWW wanting SI very badly be a thing. Hamfisted plotlines. Meta motive to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T15:08:21-07:00","id":1379526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379525#post1379525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. SI are Gary Stu.<br /> <br /> Humanity is a threat to vampires if masquerade fall completely and things get nuclear. If all the humans fight, sure the vampires gonna lose. Now, what we have is a bunch of swat teams going places.<br /> <br /> Black ops cannot assault the fortress of the most powerfull bloodmages in the entire world and kill said bloodmages only because they want. The chantry teleport across dif. locations and have ward against tech that would turn the bombs dropped into harmless metal scrap...<br /> <br /> I don't think any gov. will acept give so much money to one secret org hunt vampires.<br /> I don't think so many countries across the world will gleefull make a deal to share military information (or any info at all).<br /> Neither all of this war gonna be keep secret for any longer.<br /> <br /> SI is solely the writers of NuWW wanting SI very badly be a thing. Hamfisted plotlines. Meta motive to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except. Older editions had vampires afraid of flamethrowers, machine guns, tanks, bombs.<br /> <br /> The chantry doesn't teleport. There've never been 'wards against tech' or anything like that historically.<br /> <br /> Edit: And because those arguing against the SI are holding to the delusion that elders are capable of keeping up with technology. From the V20 core.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although it may seem like the elders have all of the best domains, young Kindred do have a certain advantage They haven\u2019t been dead as long as their elders,and remain closer to the mortals from whom they only recently parted.<br /> This means they still have a connection to mortal trends, and in nights when even children have technology at their disposal, young Kindred do, too. Elders\u2019 age and stasis make them reluctant to engage with these new \u2014 and, frankly, frightening \u2014 technologies. Thus, the speed at which information travels is the neonate\u2019s most valuable asset.<br /> From social media to web-based archives of city history to data clouds that house all of the public records of civic transactions (including the name on the deed of the Tremere chantry\u2026), the ability to seemingly reach into the ether and pluck out vital information is an aptitude that confounds many elders. Consider that a given elder may have once held sway over scriptoria of monks who diligently copied manuscripts by hand over the span of years, or even one who watched the printing press slowly transform the western world. The speed at which information disseminates is a modern horror that can cause even the most stalwart elder to blanch. Flash mob at the graveyard, which just happens to be a craggy old Malkavian\u2019s favored haven? \u201cNo problem,\u201d says the confident young vampire, smartphone in hand. There has even been talk of vampires making their own social network. </div> </div> </div>And guess who has influence over the government and is willing to use that influence? Why the handy dandy elders, who we have, directly from V20, the inability to understand even most modern tech from 20 years ago, let alone again, cutting edge surveillance technology.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Because it's fun quoting the supposedly superior editions to shut down these arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Government agencies also keep an eye on the movements of the undead and even unaffiliated groups have a keen interest in the supernatural occupants of the world they share. </div> </div> </div>So. Even MORE historically arguments in favor of the government slowly getting an eye on what's up.<br /> <br /> Or, you know, the U.S Government section from the antagonist part of the book. Which was almost directly copied from the US Government page from Revised. You know, it's almost like. As I've been saying, editions have been building up and maintaining the threat of humanity. But nope. Muh Vampurs are infallible.<br /> <br /> Edit 3: I'd also like to raise the question. If Vampires are so omniscient and capable of rooting out other conspiracies. Why haven't they taken care of all the large scale hunter groups like the arcanists, or the Society of Leopold, or rogue ghouls, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","user":"Necroticbinder","date":". 04-08-2020, 06:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T15:45:39-07:00","id":1379534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379476#post1379476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs being larger than ever means the Camarilla has ceased to fulfil one of it's core purposes. Yeah i'd say it's up in flames.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Anarchs were growing as a movement massively in V20. As soon as the Kuei-Jin invasion failed, they rebounded. Did you read ANARCHS UNBOUND?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm talking about the hunters here. </div> </div> </div>Your argument applies to the Camarilla, though. Everything you say about conspiracies being easy to discover the larger they are and easier to infiltrate, subvert, or attack applies to the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But the beckoning which enables her here is a 5th edition addition. </div> </div> </div>So your argument is essentially, &quot;It would never work as long as things that are part of the setting in the new edition didn't happen?&quot; Except there were other NSA agents and activities going on in Project: Twilight anyway.<br /> <br /> I'm not putting you down but your argument seems to be, &quot;And under no circumstances could humans ever mobilize to threaten vampires who are so powerful, so efficient, and so intelligent that they would never ever have the Masquerade break to a level that would allow any form of organized resistance against them. Also, no supernatural disaster or event would ever happen that could result in that being effected to the point that they would be vulnerable.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-08T15:49:01-07:00","id":1379535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379525#post1379525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree. SI are Gary Stu.<br /> <br /> Humanity is a threat to vampires if masquerade fall completely and things get nuclear. If all the humans fight, sure the vampires gonna lose. Now, what we have is a bunch of swat teams going places.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, the depiction of the book isn't even a Second Inquisition. It's that the Society of Leopold is now no longer a joke so it's just the First Inquisition. Also, aside from Vienna, London, Montreal, and Venice--the SI doesn't seem to have done much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Black ops cannot assault the fortress of the most powerfull bloodmages in the entire world and kill said bloodmages only because they want. The chantry teleport across dif. locations and have ward against tech that would turn the bombs dropped into harmless metal scrap... </div> </div> </div>I liked it much better with the idea they didn't attack the place on foot but bombed it. I can believe &quot;a hellfire missile blow up the chantry.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't think any gov. will acept give so much money to one secret org hunt vampires.<br /> I don't think so many countries across the world will gleefull make a deal to share military information (or any info at all).<br /> Neither all of this war gonna be keep secret for any longer. </div> </div> </div>I admit, I fully believe they should say the Technocracy is behind the group and/or Marcus Vitel funding it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> SI is solely the writers of NuWW wanting SI very badly be a thing. Hamfisted plotlines. Meta motive to happen. </div> </div> </div>Eh, that's the case in all metaplot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T00:55:12-07:00","id":1379697,"title":"","content":"Just because metaplot is often forced doesn't mean it's ok to write something that very clearly isn't good. Adding more bad things rarely makes something better. <br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with hunters, I like hunters. However, the escalation of the Hunters into the SI doesn't make sense. Logically it doesn't make sense to make Hunters a larger threat than they were in V20 (which yes, had some excellent books) and thats a deal breaker for me; thematically it's a complete inversion of what the World of Darkness is and what it's like to run a Hunter Game. In my opinion, Game wise it's more fun to play hunters as Domestic terrorists than MiB, there's actually another group for MiB, I'd go there if I wanted that kind of game.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't even have to be blood gods to be protected from large scale hunts like this. They're entrenched. Unless there was a public outcry to get rid of the vampires, goverments wouldn't. The scenario of V5 doesn't sociology into account. It doesn't take history or politics into account; It doesn't take Ma Boi Hermes, who probably provided the metaphysical paradigm of the world of darkness, into account; It doesn't even take the literary notion of satire into account. Everything is wrong with the second inquisition. It's like watching new writers take over a show and not know what it's about, only all the examples I can think of don't even come close to the scale of the disconnect V5 has. <br /> <br /> V20 had excellent hunters that made (more) sense and were a joy to run. V5 hunters are the overly emotional reaction of a bad storyteller who got a bit too upset that his players didn't take his game seriously enough. It might actually be great for an individual table to have this scenario, but it really doesn't work for the overall WoD. It's a logistical farce unless you dial it down considerably, and even then you'd be better of just following V20's (wonderful) ideas on hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T01:04:33-07:00","id":1379702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379697#post1379697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're entrenched.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>They</i> are entrenched.....?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T01:09:57-07:00","id":1379704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379697#post1379697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because metaplot is often forced doesn't mean it's ok to write something that very clearly isn't good. Adding more bad things rarely makes something better.<br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with hunters, I like hunters. However, the escalation of the Hunters into the SI doesn't make sense. Logically it doesn't make sense to make Hunters a larger threat than they were in V20 (which yes, had some excellent books) and thats a deal breaker for me; thematically it's a complete inversion of what the World of Darkness is and what it's like to run a Hunter Game.</div> </div> </div> </div>The MIB exist as the Special Affaira Division prior to the Technocracy. I admit, I didn't much care for Hunters Hunted V20 because there was a bias against Hunters. Ever since 1st Edition, Hunters were getting stronger and more deadly but the ones in V20 were dramatically nerfed.<br /> <br /> The SAD and NSA were especially poorly treated in that book.<br /> <br /> At the very least there should be a Task Force: Valkyrie that could come down and destroy any single city of vampires. It should never be less than that.<br /> <br /> V20 treated it as if they were embarrassed that hunters were a reason for Kindred to be afraid of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In my opinion, Game wise it's more fun to play hunters as Domestic terrorists than MiB, there's actually another group for MiB, I'd go there if I wanted that kind of game. </div> </div> </div>I think there should be conspiracies in the government as much as any other group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T01:38:51-07:00","id":1379708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379526#post1379526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except. Older editions had vampires afraid of flamethrowers, machine guns, tanks, bombs.<br /> <br /> The chantry doesn't teleport. There've never been 'wards against tech' or anything like that historically.<br /> <br /> Edit: And because those arguing against the SI are holding to the delusion that elders are capable of keeping up with technology. From the V20 core.<br /> <br /> <br /> And guess who has influence over the government and is willing to use that influence? Why the handy dandy elders, who we have, directly from V20, the inability to understand even most modern tech from 20 years ago, let alone again, cutting edge surveillance technology.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Because it's fun quoting the supposedly superior editions to shut down these arguments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So. Even MORE historically arguments in favor of the government slowly getting an eye on what's up.<br /> <br /> Or, you know, the U.S Government section from the antagonist part of the book. Which was almost directly copied from the US Government page from Revised. You know, it's almost like. As I've been saying, editions have been building up and maintaining the threat of humanity. But nope. Muh Vampurs are infallible.<br /> <br /> Edit 3: I'd also like to raise the question. If Vampires are so omniscient and capable of rooting out other conspiracies. Why haven't they taken care of all the large scale hunter groups like the arcanists, or the Society of Leopold, or rogue ghouls, etc?</div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> Warding Circle versus Technology (Level Five Thaumaturgy Ritual)<br /> This ritual creates a circle of magic centered on the caster, into which technology (i.e. any machine<br /> more complex or advanced than a crossbow) cannot pass without shattering or becoming<br /> defunct. This circle can be made as large and as permanent as the caster<br /> desires, as longe as she is willing to pay the necessary price.<br /> <br /> Level Five Ritual:<br /> Sanctuary.<br /> System: To complet this ritual, the thaumaturge must invest a permanent point<br /> of Willpower into the consecration of the targeted building at the end<br /> of three-night ritual. Once completed, the shroud of sanctuary<br /> completely envelops the boundaries of the targeted building.<br /> All souls, living or orthewise, that are not especifically invited <br /> by the caster cannot enter the building.<br /> Further, those inside the building are protected against all<br /> uses of Animalism, Auspex, Dominate, Dementation and Presente<br /> (and related Disciplines, at Storyteller discretion).<br /> If the building remains consecrated, the magic of this ritual continues for one year per sucess from the activation roll. <br /> Afterward, the caster must either reinvest the Willpower point or allow the sanctuary to dissipate.<br /> <br /> Level Two Ritual: Seal Egress.<br /> Seal egress allows the thaumaturge to mystically seal a room closed to prevent<br /> unwanted trespassers from entering or leaving it until the proper<br /> passcode chosen by the caster is spoken aloud near the entrance.<br /> Some Tremere trap an enemy in a small room and allow him to go mad from hunger.<br /> <br /> <br /> Level Two Ritual: Deny the Intruder<br /> To protect chantries from unwanted observation, Tremere rely not only upon mystic wards, but also upon mortal bureaucracy. <br /> An enemy can hardly drop in if the chantry isn't listed in any directories or real estate paperwork, after all. <br /> Better still, a little judicious paper-shuffling can &quot;lose&quot; records for electrical payments, telephone calls and other incriminating evidence.<br /> <br /> Bonus:<br /> Suspension of Incantation<br /> Apsu Portal; Escape to a True Friend.<br /> Stone Slumber. </div></div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-09T02:44:58-07:00","id":1379712,"title":"","content":"I wonder whether it was True Faith, psychics, modern science, or any of the other resources available to the Second Inquisition that caused these rituals to fail the Tremere.<br /> <br /> The easy answer to me is Tremere the 4th generation/3rd generation wizard brought it low to destroy the Worm but that almost seems like a cop out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:01:11-07:00","id":1380419,"title":"","content":"SI wiped all out is the metaplot, no more \u201cwhy\u201d<br /> <br /> Some thoughts:<br /> 1. Some powers aren\u2019t that common as we think, <br /> <br /> People always consult one power/ritual C in Book Y to debate their splat is the biggest badass, but the fact is, they may be very rare indeed. Maybe Ward versus Tech is not that common, maybe obfuscate rituals are only wielded by experienced kindreds, maybe elder powers are very, very few indeed, not to mention some personal rituals or powers, just like those in Lair of Hidden, they do not represent most kindreds<br /> <br /> 2. Do. Not. Underestimate. Mortals<br /> <br /> Mortals are the greatest and foremost of the whole WoD. They are always cows to vampires, but when uniting and being armed and hunting for the same purpose, they will destroy everything. Mortal wars in history will put the greatest supernatural wars to shame<br /> <br /> When a powerful 4th gens Brujah or Assamite or Tremere faces hundreds or thousands of mortals who may not even have any supernatural power except guns guns guns, they may still realize they will be f**cked off, all methseulah powers are pale when facing true great number of mortals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-11-2020, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:24:06-07:00","id":1380426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380419#post1380419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">SI wiped all out is the metaplot, no more \u201cwhy\u201d<br /> <br /> Some thoughts:<br /> 1. Some powers aren\u2019t that common as we think, <br /> <br /> People always consult one power/ritual C in Book Y to debate their splat is the biggest badass, but the fact is, they may be very rare indeed. Maybe Ward versus Tech is not that common, maybe obfuscate rituals are only wielded by experienced kindreds, maybe elder powers are very, very few indeed, not to mention some personal rituals or powers, just like those in Lair of Hidden, they do not represent most kindreds<br /> <br /> 2. Do. Not. Underestimate. Mortals<br /> <br /> Mortals are the greatest and foremost of the whole WoD. They are always cows to vampires, but when uniting and being armed and hunting for the same purpose, they will destroy everything. Mortal wars in history will put the greatest supernatural wars to shame<br /> <br /> When a powerful 4th gens Brujah or Assamite or Tremere faces hundreds or thousands of mortals who may not even have any supernatural power except guns guns guns, they may still realize they will be f**cked off, all methseulah powers are pale when facing true great number of mortals</div> </div> </div> </div>Dude, it's the council of the seven.<br /> <br /> For real.<br /> <br /> If they dont have those rituals, no one have.<br /> <br /> The mortal, as a whole, are indeed a threat to Kindred.<br /> <br /> Now,<br /> <br /> A bunch of swat teams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:24:31-07:00","id":1380428,"title":"","content":"On a less crazy note I think Vienna was destroyed because the plot there had gotten ridiculous with giant demon worms and magical teleporting buildings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:29:32-07:00","id":1380430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380426#post1380426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, it's the council of the seven.<br /> <br /> For real.<br /> <br /> If they dont have those rituals, no one have.<br /> <br /> The mortal, as a whole, are indeed a threat to Kindred.<br /> <br /> Now,<br /> <br /> A bunch of swat teams?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Humans are a threat to vampires. But. A bunch of humans?&quot;<br /> <br /> Literally what you are saying. If a large group of highly trained operatives backed up by true faith and relics can't take on the Tremere chantry then no one can. Blood magic users should just openly rule the world because at this point the argument is that vampires are literally unbeatable because the only thing that can take them on is nukes and even then. If we go by the old paradigms of magic (Such as revised or V20) the Tremere would have made a 'ward against nukes'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:30:37-07:00","id":1380432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380426#post1380426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, it's the council of the seven.<br /> <br /> For real.<br /> <br /> If they dont have those rituals, no one have.<br /> <br /> The mortal, as a whole, are indeed a threat to Kindred.<br /> <br /> Now,<br /> <br /> A bunch of swat teams?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe these powers are not that effective, or council of seven are not that great. You know many guys who seem to be great usually die of... ridiculous reasons<br /> <br /> Or the whole SI is just a pawn, manipulated by other Ancients or Badass, in WoD sense","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:31:43-07:00","id":1380433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380426#post1380426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dude, it's the council of the seven.<br /> <br /> For real.<br /> <br /> If they dont have those rituals, no one have.<br /> <br /> The mortal, as a whole, are indeed a threat to Kindred.<br /> <br /> Now,<br /> <br /> A bunch of swat teams?</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it made a lot more sense when it was a drone strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T11:37:01-07:00","id":1380435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380430#post1380430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;Humans are a threat to vampires. But. A bunch of humans?&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> Literally what you are saying. If a large group of highly trained operatives backed up by true faith and relics can't take on the Tremere chantry then no one can. Blood magic users should just openly rule the world because at this point the argument is that vampires are literally unbeatable because the only thing that can take them on is nukes and even then. If we go by the old paradigms of magic (Such as revised or V20) the Tremere would have made a 'ward against nukes'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wars. Vs. Every. Thing<br /> <br /> But the fact is more realistic<br /> <br /> And I always think high level powers, elder or meth ones are not that great<br /> <br /> Just the problem of one gun or two or more <br /> <br /> \u201cWell, you can\u2019t take down a 6th gens elder with 5 soilders? No problem, 15 guys arrive. Not enough too? 30 ones!\u201d<br /> <br /> And elder falls, a very pillar collapses<br /> <br /> But soilders can be replaced very fast, much faster than ghouls or mass embrace or anything supernatural","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:00:57-07:00","id":1380453,"title":"","content":"We're doing this? Really? <br /> <br /> As much as a great buzz word -drone strike- is, I really doubt the chantry isn't a fortress that can be taken out by something that wouldn't be extremely noticable and cause massive colatoral damage. You would need a very big payload, to be carried by a very large drone; doing this in a big city like vienna you should consider buzz that would create politically. How wouldn't vampires pick up on this? I think we can safely rule out a drone strike. <br /> And as said, Ward against technology is a thing. The members of the council of seven have auspex and thaumaturgy ratings between 6 and 9. I really, really don't think you could take them by surprise. <br /> <br /> True Faith makes miracles, sure, but you're all getting way too liberal with it. It's not a licence to achieve the impossible whenever you wish. It's rare, and there are limitations. And it would do nothing to guard from the mundane security the Vienna chantry no doubt excels at.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:05:31-07:00","id":1380456,"title":"","content":"The drone strike happened through a pure stroke of bad writing. In actuality the Drone operator would've never pinpointed the Chantry because its literally warded against Tech. Even if their were to send teams on site in an attempt to physically raid it, the Chantry would just disappear for them since it literally teleports. Even if they somehow got in they would've gotten their asses whooped by literally the whole of Tremere with their hard hitters in their central HQ. The council and Tremere clan by itself also have an enormous amount of pull in the city. They'd just organize counter assaults with the city police force against the SI. No way anything that happened with the Vienna chantry would be possible. The SI is a Gary Stu faction.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I noticed I wrote literally alot. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-11-2020, 04:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:18:05-07:00","id":1380461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380456#post1380456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The drone strike happened through a pure stroke of bad writing. In actuality the Drone operator would've never pinpointed the Chantry because its literally warded against Tech. Even if their were to send teams on site in an attempt to physically raid it, the Chantry would just disappear for them since it literally teleports. Even if they somehow got in they would've gotten their asses whooped by literally the whole of Tremere with their hard hitters in their central HQ. The council and Tremere clan by itself also have an enormous amount of pull in the city. They'd just organize counter assaults with the city police force against the SI. No way anything that happened with the Vienna chantry would be possible. The SI is a Gary Stu faction.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I noticed I wrote literally alot. lol</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, which is problematic I think because if an enemy is invincible then it's not terribly interesting. Good writing makes antagonists interesting by their vulnerabilities as well as successes. Basically, all of the descriptions there make the Tremere seem less cool, less interesting, and less entertaining. If they can't actually be defeated because of &quot;handwave&quot; then they aren't interesting. Which is a good reason to take them off the board to begin with.<br /> <br /> The worst villain ever made in any RPG *EVER* was Divis Mal because the writers did their best to make him completely invincible. As such, every player hated him and with good reason.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380453#post1380453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We're doing this? Really?<br /> <br /> As much as a great buzz word -drone strike- is, I really doubt the chantry isn't a fortress that can be taken out by something that wouldn't be extremely noticable and cause massive colatoral damage. You would need a very big payload, to be carried by a very large drone; doing this in a big city like vienna you should consider buzz that would create politically. How wouldn't vampires pick up on this? I think we can safely rule out a drone strike.<br /> And as said, Ward against technology is a thing. The members of the council of seven have auspex and thaumaturgy ratings between 6 and 9. I really, really don't think you could take them by surprise.<br /> <br /> True Faith makes miracles, sure, but you're all getting way too liberal with it. It's not a licence to achieve the impossible whenever you wish. It's rare, and there are limitations. And it would do nothing to guard from the mundane security the Vienna chantry no doubt excels at.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's hard arguing with you because you don't read V5 so when you argue you are actually arguing against things that have been described in the books. The Raid on Vienna happened during the Daytime by the Society of Leopold that used their most sacred relics that stripped away the Chantry's defenses and they proceeded to attack, decapitating many sleeping vampires while stealing away numerous sacred books.<br /> <br /> Then they dropped a bomb on the castle that destroyed it and buried everything underneath it.<br /> <br /> The attack was blamed on ISIS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-11-2020, 04:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:44:22-07:00","id":1380465,"title":"","content":"The Tremere aren't even supposed to be antagonists so I don't understand your angle. Even with that the Tremere obviously aren't invincible, nothing is in WoD. But they damn sure have a plethora of feats gathered over literal centuries where they shouldn't just be gobsmacked by some no name organization at their main HQ no less (which I mentioned before shouldn't have been &quot;droned&quot; in the first place since logically it wouldn't be possible for humans to even see it). It would've been more forgivable if they droned a strategically important but less established Chantry. But no, the main one housing the council somehow gets offed. The writers only pulled that off because they needed a convenience to morph their biases into the Tremere tbh.<br /> <br /> Also the main appeal of the Tremere was that they were Vampiric Sorcerers. They used to have unique abilities mostly abided unto them, but for some reason V5 writers decided to remove that entirely. Even letting THINBOLDS of all things (the subsplat of Vampire thats literally on a plot device and not really to be a focal point of the game) innate ability to do &quot;Thinbold Alchemy&quot;.. as if Thinbolds are meant to be strong or keep up in any matter of Kindred society.. lol","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:45:29-07:00","id":1380466,"title":"","content":"At this point, this thread is only serving to demonstrate that the V5 haters primarily have an irrational bias against it and no matter the explanations backed up by lore from prior editions, no matter how thoroughly explained it was, or even if they wrote entire novels dedicated to nothing but explaining this situation in a 'reasonable' way, that it would still be argued against. Why? Because. Vampires are immortal unbeatable blood gods and unless you are wielding the force of an entire modern nation (Except not even then), the pitiful mortals will be beaten back or because it represents change and advancement. <br /> <br /> The goal posts get shoved or explanations are getting outright ignored, especially if they address the concerns that maybe, just maybe. Elders aren't infalliable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T13:50:01-07:00","id":1380467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380465#post1380465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere aren't even supposed to be antagonists so I don't understand your angle. Even with that the Tremere obviously aren't invincible, nothing is in WoD. But they damn sure have a plethora of feats gathered over literal centuries where they shouldn't just be gobsmacked by some no name organization at their main HQ no less (which I mentioned before shouldn't have been &quot;droned&quot; in the first place since logically it wouldn't be possible for humans to even see it). It would've been more forgivable if they droned a strategically important but less established Chantry. But no, the main one housing the council somehow gets offed. The writers only pulled that off because they needed a convenience to morph their biases into the Tremere tbh.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Council of Seven is certainly a bunch of antagonists because every Tremere character is partially blood bound toward them. So the goal is to get yourself out from under their thumb. But that kind of gets to the heart of the matter in that you describe the &quot;Second Inquisition&quot; as a &quot;no name organization&quot; given that it is meant to be one of the primary antagonists of the 5th Edition. You are basically pointing out why it had to be the Vienna Chantry because the whole point is to show that the most powerful and dangerous Elders of the Camarilla are vulnerable. You may argue that they did a poor job of justifying it (and I agree) but the point is to show that they are vulnerable.<br /> <br /> So how would you as a Storyteller explain why the Second Inquisition did it because the point is that they ARE tough enough to beat the Council of Seven, not that they can't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the main appeal of the Tremere was that they were Vampiric Sorcerers. They used to have unique abilities mostly abided unto them, but for some reason V5 writers decided to remove that entirely. Even letting THINBOLDS of all things (the subsplat of Vampire thats literally on a plot device and not really to be a focal point of the game) innate ability to do &quot;Thinbold Alchemy&quot;.. as if Thinbolds are meant to be strong or keep up in any matter of Kindred society.. lol </div> </div> </div>Thin Bloods actually took a blow, IMHO because they used to be able to have 3 in every Discipline and make their own Disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:01:19-07:00","id":1380471,"title":"","content":"As much as I love bashing the Second Inquisition's implementation... are we really not going to talk, at all, about the other half of the topic of the thread?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:33:36-07:00","id":1380490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380465#post1380465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the main appeal of the Tremere was that they were Vampiric Sorcerers. They used to have unique abilities mostly abided unto them, but for some reason V5 writers decided to remove that entirely. Even letting THINBOLDS of all things (the subsplat of Vampire thats literally on a plot device and not really to be a focal point of the game) innate ability to do &quot;Thinbold Alchemy&quot;.. as if Thinbolds are meant to be strong or keep up in any matter of Kindred society.. lol</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, Sorcery was never unique to the Tremere. Dur-An-Ki, Akhu, Koldunism\u2026<br /> <br /> And in previous editions Thinbloods could create entirely new disciplines ex nihilo. The fact that they can no longer learn any normal disciplines at all (or only one with a specific merit) is a nerf compared to previous editions, where fourteenth-gens could learn up to the fourth dot of anything they wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T14:42:07-07:00","id":1380493,"title":"","content":"Outside of perhaps Al Amut, the Tremere's Vienna Chantry was probably the most well protected fortress in the entire World of Darkness. I understand that the authors wanted it taken out so that they should demonstrate that the Second Inquisition can destroy anyone anywhere and not even the most perfect defenses laid out over hundreds of years can keep you safe, in order to project a feeling of terror out onto the vampires (and players) but it does come off as incredibly hamfisted.<br /> <br /> I could see if the US military did something like dropping a Massive Ordnance Penetrator (Bunker Buster) on the place and basically destroying it (of course an explosion that large would also inflict significant damage to the city of Vienna, kill a ton of other people and there's no way that could just be swept under the rug, and of course they'd probably need the assistance of another supernatural being to help them pinpoint the chantry in the first place), or if there was heavy outside assistance from the Technocracy (Hitmarks and such) but as described with SWAT teams doing room sweeps and whatnot, it just doesn't feel legit and projects a feeling of, &quot;There's no verisimilitude in the World of Darkness because the authors can and will do whatever they want even when it doesn't make a whole lot of sense from within the setting.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 04-11-2020, 05:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T15:03:09-07:00","id":1380501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380471#post1380471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I love bashing the Second Inquisition's implementation... are we really not going to talk, at all, about the other half of the topic of the thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess, I'm wondering how the Imbued have changed in 20 years.<br /> <br /> I admit in my games, I revealed they were all possessed by Redeemer Demons and that turned a lot of them against one another. So there's now only a handful left.<br /> <br /> If the Imbued organized and became a hunting organization I feel they'd lose a lot of their feeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-11-2020, 06:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T20:33:09-07:00","id":1380566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380501#post1380501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I confess, I'm wondering how the Imbued have changed in 20 years.<br /> <br /> I admit in my games, I revealed they were all possessed by Redeemer Demons and that turned a lot of them against one another. So there's now only a handful left.<br /> <br /> If the Imbued organized and became a hunting organization I feel they'd lose a lot of their feeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Few NEW 20th anni materials mention them iirc<br /> <br /> VtM: only a gimpse in the Hunters Hunted iirc<br /> WtA: Gifts in Core and Book of Wyrm has some glimpses. Core also has template but it\u2019s Revised thing<br /> MtA: None. Even the Gods &amp; Monsters don\u2019t have them<br /> WtA: None<br /> CtD: One of kithbooks mention them<br /> <br /> But who knows?<br /> <br /> IMO they may be more famous, organized and greater generally because of nearly 20 years battle, and even knew some relations with Wan Gui (Fallen foremost imbueds)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-12-2020, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T21:00:25-07:00","id":1380572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition#post1379003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like the Second Inquisition.. It just feels.. so cliche and horrible. From somehow breaking into Schrecknet, then the Vatican getting involved, then this group of mortals just wrecking everything.. Yeah no. The Camarilla nor Sabbat wouldn't be taken out by such a thing in their pre-V5 unnerfed state realistically (even with the whole Beckoning nonsense, lets be real). The worst egress of this Gary-Stu faction was how they somehow <i>bombed</i> the Vienna Chantry- a magic fortress/university basically that has probably existed longer than all the operators within the SI combined and literally can't be comprehended by mortals at all because it always teleports IIRC. Not only that this Gary-Stu faction has cleared out cities with high level Kindred, some Anchillae too who probably weren't compelled by the Beckoning.. somehow... The Second Inquisition.. is horrible.<br /> <br /> What would have been way more compelling was to bring the Imbued in as the primary Human antagonists instead of the SI. More interesting, has clear abilities that would've allowed them to spot Vienna in the first place with True Sight, a clear precedent of their power is known so there is a logical justification for how their KO'ing the Camarilla and the Sabbat (<i>especially the Sabbat</i>), and they would've been generally more compelling. Because I don't understand the fuss about the Second Inquisition, their faction doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>They wanted the SI to be The Man, and the vampires to be the Scrappy Underdog. The Imbued don't work as that. The Imbued are the underdogs in a world secretly run by monsters.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-11T23:21:40-07:00","id":1380589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380572#post1380572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wanted the SI to be The Man, and the vampires to be the Scrappy Underdog. The Imbued don't work as that. The Imbued are the underdogs in a world secretly run by monsters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I take it as a commentary on the surveillance state that emerged past 9/11. The government is no longer something that ignorant people view with a conspiratorial eye that more informed people shrug off. The powers, weaponry, technology, and activities of the government have changed to an enormous degree. The Second Inquisition is a creation of the world going from one where the ABC agencies compete against one another to one where they are a united juggernaut.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T00:26:43-07:00","id":1380593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380461#post1380461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the Society of Leopold that used their most sacred relics that stripped away the Chantry's defenses and they proceeded to attack, decapitating many sleeping vampires while stealing away numerous sacred books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacred relics, is that code for Bullshit? But you're also saying they entered the chantry to steal things... and the mundane security did nothing?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then they dropped a bomb on the castle that destroyed it and buried everything underneath it. </div> </div> </div> yes, it must have been a really, really big bomb.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The attack was blamed on ISIS. </div> </div> </div>Because the SoL is happy to be the bad guys now commiting terrorist acts like ISIS and doing tons of collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Just because someone wrote some justifaction, does not mean that the justification was good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T02:05:32-07:00","id":1380603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380593#post1380593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the SoL is happy to be the bad guys now commiting terrorist acts like ISIS and doing tons of collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Just because someone wrote some justifaction, does not mean that the justification was good.</div> </div> </div> </div>SoL (and other hunters) always acted as terrorists, and, hunters were always considered terrorists,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sacred relics, is that code for Bullshit? But you're also saying they entered the chantry to steal things... and the mundane security did nothing? </div> </div> </div>yeah, vampiric or Tremere defenses were always ineffective mechanically speaking,<br /> that was always a big plot hole in all of VtM, and vampires seemed to always get out of trouble thanks to plot armor or plot devices<br /> <br /> as bad as the story was in V5, this is ironically the first time it was realistic mechanics wise<br /> <br /> anyway, I think we should all ignore it, cause if the Tremere are trully gone (regardless of how), good riddance<br /> sadly, blood magic is still a thing, and probably still a mess :/<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T02:52:26-07:00","id":1380607,"title":"","content":"I feel that's the attitude that really caused all the problems of V5 &quot;I really don't like something so I'll get rid of it, it doesn't matter how; if I can do it in a way that completely disrespects the thing I don't like, all the better.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but if the most powerful bloodmages in the world decided to live in a fortress, hire considerable mortal security, and then put down layers upon layers of the very best defensive rituals and wards vampire society has to offer, and then a bunch of bible boys took them out, I really wouldn't be praising V5 for 'realism'. A plot device is not a negative thing, and the Tremere have always used them more than 'plot armour'. Detesting the Tremere for having magic and using it well is like lamenting that people use period-accurate weapons in war movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T02:59:07-07:00","id":1380608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380607#post1380607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel that's the attitude that really caused all the problems of V5 &quot;I really don't like something so I'll get rid of it, it doesn't matter how; if I can do it in a way that completely disrespects the thing I don't like, all the better.&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't know about you, but if the most powerful bloodmages in the world decided to live in a fortress, hire considerable mortal security, and then put down layers upon layers of the very best defensive rituals and wards vampire society has to offer, and then a bunch of bible boys took them out, I really wouldn't be praising V5 for 'realism'. A plot device is not a negative thing, and the Tremere have always used them more than 'plot armour'. Detesting the Tremere for having magic and using it well is like lamenting that people use period-accurate weapons in war movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would love to hear your personal take on who or what and under what circumstances could be capable of taking Vienna chantry out. Caine himself, Maeljin Incarna assault brigade, Vasilisa/Absimiliard?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T03:12:20-07:00","id":1380610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380607#post1380607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Detesting the Tremere for having magic and using it well is like lamenting that people use period-accurate weapons in war movies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dislike Tremere and Magic separately,<br /> magic because the system was bad (well, even the discipline system had problems, but I could tolerate it to some extent),<br /> and magic was used as a convenient plot device to explain everything the devs couldn't explain and advance the plot,<br /> almost nothing happens in VtM without blood magic intervention<br /> <br /> the Tremere were just an invasive presence in the setting,<br /> they don't follow the VtM paradigm,<br /> yet they were everywhere doing everything, and they were made necessary to hold the setting and the Camarilla making you wonder what was the point of all the politicking in the cam/sabbat when the mages/infernalists were the only ones actually contributing in any meaningful way<br /> <br /> I don't necessarily need the Tremere gone, but I'd like them to at least fit in with the rest, and without stealing the show<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel that's the attitude that really caused all the problems of V5 &quot;I really don't like something so I'll get rid of it, it doesn't matter how; if I can do it in a way that completely disrespects the thing I don't like, all the better.&quot; </div> </div> </div>yes, but I don't believe there's a way to fix things that won't be considered disrespectful by someone,<br /> I always wanted the devs to just retcon things, but people will still be mad at retcons, which is why they always avoided retcons and do messy plot advancement,<br /> <br /> rn, I can't thing of any good solution that wouldn't feel radical","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":10998,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","user":"Pleiades","date":". 04-12-2020, 06:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T04:09:11-07:00","id":1380613,"title":"","content":"I'm not saying humans couldn't do it, but it'd look less like a simple terrorist bombing and more like something out of Call of Duty. The Tremere are extremely wealthy, easily in the top four clans, they're the most unified and this is their headquarters. Even if we ignore magic, money would well fortify the Tremere, and then there's influence, and then there's all the rest. Clan Tremere has so many enemies, if their building was really an ordinary building that couldn't take a bomb, they wouldn't have survived this long. You'd need to use a bomb so big that you'd wipe out nearby buildings and kill a lot of innocent people. You can't really smuggle in such a bomb on a person. And when you do bomb it, does that mean you hit the inner circle? These vampires survived WWII, and Vienna got hit by bombing pretty badly during the war. Just dropping a bomb on the place won't cut it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T04:20:03-07:00","id":1380615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380608#post1380608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to hear your personal take on who or what and under what circumstances could be capable of taking Vienna chantry out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The question supposes something rather off from the perspective of what the WoD is supposed to be about.<br /> <br /> The important question to any such effort is less about &quot;how,&quot; and more about, &quot;at what cost.&quot; The setting certainly tiers costs such that there are threats that have costs far beyond PCs in anything but epic long games with huge piles of XP and plot gained goodies, but nonetheless the question of was the cost worth it is what permeates the WoD's themes.<br /> <br /> This is what the main issue with taking out the Vienna Chantry as written really comes down to: The Second Inquisition didn't pay a cost. They weren't exposed to the world. Their supposed weaknesses didn't get easier for vampires to exploit. They didn't sacrifice a plot device they could only use once. They didn't lose a vital irreplaceable Inquisitor that will take decades of their best to train in the hopes of recovering the faith and skills lost. Etc. <br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition didn't pay a cost commensurate with the narrative challenge the Vienna Chantry represented. <br /> <br /> This is also the biggest issue with trying to change things to the Imbued. The Imbued, as they stand with their core themes, aren't up to pay those sorts of costs. Advancing them to the point where they could even try is radically changing Reckoning from it's intended themes into something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T04:35:09-07:00","id":1380617,"title":"","content":"Deleted ra ra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","user":"Trippy","date":".  Can\u2019t be bothered with it. 04-12-2020, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T05:06:42-07:00","id":1380620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380615#post1380615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The question supposes something rather off from the perspective of what the WoD is supposed to be about.</div> </div> </div> </div>My comment was meant to highlight the absurdity of the whole discussion and the reasons which led to it. Please don't think too much into it. The very fact we have to ruminate on &quot;power levels&quot; of certain forces and capabilities of &quot;this or that taking this or that out&quot; indicates that there were things in WoD and VtM which gone seriously wrong.<br /> <br /> I agree the whole solution was heavy-handed and the build-up was really non-existent, a missed opportunity. A rushed decision. But the whole 'Fall from grace' thing was inevitable for Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T05:15:51-07:00","id":1380621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380593#post1380593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sacred relics, is that code for Bullshit? But you're also saying they entered the chantry to steal things... and the mundane security did nothing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls still die when shot.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> yes, it must have been a really, really big bomb. </div> </div> </div>Probably. Except the chantry isn't in the city according to the description but was apparently in the countryside outside of Vienna.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because the SoL is happy to be the bad guys now commiting terrorist acts like ISIS and doing tons of collateral damage. </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't know how many innocents die in the destruction of the isolated castle.<br /> <br /> But yes, I think the Inquisition would burn down an apartment of 200 people to kill one vampire.<br /> <br /> Because they're the INQUISITION.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because someone wrote some justifaction, does not mean that the justification was good. </div> </div> </div>I agree, I think they should have not invaded the place. I would have had the Chantry found by combining intelligence and then using psychic technology of NSA to find it then bomb it.<br /> <br /> In my games, I had the Camarilla (with the help of the Assamites) slip the US Military in Syria the location of the true Alamut and had them carpet bomb the place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T05:31:51-07:00","id":1380625,"title":"","content":"If anything, this discussion also helped me understand the problem with both sides. The pre-V5 WoD, which I prefer slightly more over the new one, was too overcrowded with supernatural superpowers. Not only VtM splat, any of them - after reading on all splats, just the corebooks, I had a feeling of the world overstuffed with supernatural, and not too many of them were subtle enough to make their existence a believable part of a &quot;darker reflection of our world&quot;. <br /> Sub-cults inside cults inside sects inside armies inside factions inside supernatural species. Archmages, methuselahs, werewolf elders, incarna, bodhisattvas, spectres running all over the place and wrecking stuff making the world tremble were too much to believe the mortals would never notice or dismiss it and go back to everydays business. The feeling of the setting was departing from gothic novella to a grimdark comicbook. It all certainly needed an update, but a careful one, a believable one, involving build up and proper connections between crucial story point which could certainly help explain the shift in the mood.<br /> <br /> And that's where the new guard failed, to my mind. They took the whole update and amplified it up to eleven in a very 'in your face' manner; with BJD being the only thing connecting all the dots. While BJD is an amazing read and easily one of my favorite WW books ever, it's not enough to justify such a drastic turnaround. After reading V5 corebook, I had a feeling of the new direction being taken with too much of a zeal, like the authors almost overtly telling me in my face &quot;If you want your methuselahs, sect wars, city gangrel commandos and tremere orbital strikes then go back play v20/revised/2ed vampions; this is a game for grown-ups now! Feeding, hunger, beast, personal drama, everynight needs. Focus please, you are not some superhero/supervillain with fangs.&quot;<br /> <br /> I honestly hope that the authors could find a middle ground between the two extremeties some day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T05:40:05-07:00","id":1380626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380621#post1380621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, I think they should have not invaded the place. I would have had the Chantry found by combining intelligence and then using psychic technology of NSA to find it then bomb it.<br /> <br /> In my games, I had the Camarilla (with the help of the Assamites) slip the US Military in Syria the location of the true Alamut and had them carpet bomb the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>always so subtle, ey Phipps?<br /> <br /> VtM plot has a problem with bombs, how do we fix this?...more bombs!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T06:03:30-07:00","id":1380631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380626#post1380626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> always so subtle, ey Phipps?<br /> <br /> VtM plot has a problem with bombs, how do we fix this?...more bombs!</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like Alamut would have been a much better target than Vienna to be honest because the US dropping massive amounts of ordinance there is less likely to be noticed.<br /> <br /> Also, bluntly, I hate Ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> I like military hardware trumping Blood Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T06:05:02-07:00","id":1380634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1379697#post1379697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 hunters are the overly emotional reaction of a bad storyteller who got a bit too upset that his players didn't take his game seriously enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>AMEN. TO. THAT.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:03:34-07:00","id":1380653,"title":"","content":"I think my biggest problem with V5 is that the Sabbat still haven't been detailed. I think they needed to be scaled back but essentially existing them from the game is like, &quot;And Pentex is now gone from Werewolf.&quot; The Second Inquisition vs. Camarilla vs. Anarchs vs. Sabbat is better than just the first three.<br /> <br /> If the Sabbat were still around we could have vampires deciding that the SI justifies going even more extreme and extra effort needing to be kept to show vampires don't exist/are a myth. We could also set up Sabbat vs. Anarchs fights every bit as hard as Sabbat vs. Camarilla fights. Plus the SI vs. Sabbat could be the most interesting &quot;Who should we root for?&quot; conflict.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I do think the Wan kuei should be exised until they can come up with something better and am okay with the Ravnos being extinct except for player characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-12-2020, 11:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T08:32:41-07:00","id":1380655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380653#post1380653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think my biggest problem with V5 is that the Sabbat still haven't been detailed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Knowing your vision of the sect, I guess it's for the best.<br /> <br /> I say that as long time Sabbat/Paths player. If authors went at least close to where you see Sabbat it would bury V5 for me.<br /> <br /> Even leaving them as mysterious bogeymen would be a more respectful approach than downgrading them into Belial's brood you see them as.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, I do think the Wan kuei should be exised until they can come up with something better and am okay with the Ravnos being extinct except for player characters. </div> </div> </div>Wan Kuei concepts were amazing. To some, including me, a whole next level after the indivudalistic approach of Vampire. I'd rather spread Gui Ren 'awakenings' across the planet instead of being limited to one region as well as opening said region to cainites.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-12-2020, 11:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:09:08-07:00","id":1380687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380603#post1380603\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> yeah, vampiric or Tremere defenses were always ineffective mechanically speaking,<br /> that was always a big plot hole in all of VtM, and vampires seemed to always get out of trouble thanks to plot armor or plot devices<br /> <br /> as bad as the story was in V5, this is ironically the first time it was realistic mechanics wise<br /> <br /> anyway, I think we should all ignore it, cause if the Tremere are trully gone (regardless of how), good riddance<br /> sadly, blood magic is still a thing, and probably still a mess :/</div> </div> </div> </div>What? V5 wasn't realistic at all in the context of the WoD universe. It was a pure asspull. The Tremere have worked and established their defenses for centuries. Off the bat they invoked alot of enemies just to get to the level of Vampirism. Not only from other Kindred, but from Hermes too- y'know an Awakened faction (who may I remind are OP reality warpers) to a standstill? The Tremere didn't have plot armor. Plot Armor is a device for a particular character or organization just have immunity to certain things just 'cuz. Tremere have legitimate feats and lore to back up why their <b>HEADQUARTERS</b> of all places should be one of the most defended possible from what they scrounged up over literal centuries. They shouldn't be finessed by the SI at all.<br /> <br /> Nothing about what went down with the SI was even half-baked good, its horrible and not realistic at all. Also what they did isn't even backed by mechanics at all, don't know what your talking about. They were just written for that feat against the Tremere as a convenience to take them down and (mostlikely) advance the asinine Rudi plot. I can see the writers mentality in you- taking out or sabotaging a staple clan because of a weird bias against them. Tremere definitely fit in the setting of oWoD. Just because you don't like something doesn't mean its a &quot;mess&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-12-2020, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:17:15-07:00","id":1380691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380655#post1380655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd rather spread Gui Ren 'awakenings' across the planet instead of being limited to one region as well as opening said region to cainites.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is possible in the time of V5<br /> <br /> In fact the Yomi has spread abroad during the revised (Broken Mirror in Killing the Streets implies this), and that\u2019s 20 years ago. I can believe wan gui has become more international today, if they still exist. But they may be more infernal and darker","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-12-2020, 01:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:33:54-07:00","id":1380698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380687#post1380687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What? V5 wasn't realistic at all in the context of the WoD universe. It was a pure asspull. The Tremere have worked and established their defenses for centuries. Off the bat they invoked alot of enemies just to get to the level of Vampirism. Not only from other Kindred, but from Hermes too- y'know an Awakened faction (who may I remind are OP reality warpers) to a standstill?</div> </div> </div> </div>yeah, that's actually one of the examples of Tremere having plot armor,<br /> realistically, they wouldn't have survived their first decade...or even their first year...yet they did,<br /> the Tremere standing up against all their enemies was, to use your phrasing, an asspull<br /> <br /> imo, the only 'realistic' explanation people have come up with was that they had antideluvian backing (or kupala or something),<br /> and even that was a stretch into plot device territory<br /> <br /> people seem to be doing the same with the SI destroying Vienna...another antideluvian intervention,<br /> but I honestly don't think we need to go that far for it to be believable,<br /> vampires were always the squishy bugs of the WoD,<br /> Tremere might be a bit less squishy, but squishy nonetheless<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>-</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10998-pleiades","name":"Pleiades","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10998_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1844"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:48:07-07:00","id":1380701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380687#post1380687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off the bat they invoked alot of enemies just to get to the level of Vampirism. Not only from other Kindred, but from Hermes too- y'know an Awakened faction (who may I remind are OP reality warpers) to a standstill? The Tremere didn't have plot armor. Plot Armor is a device for a particular character or organization just have immunity to certain things just 'cuz. Tremere have legitimate feats and lore to back up why their <b>HEADQUARTERS</b> of all places should be one of the most defended possible from what they scrounged up over literal centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>How is it <i>not</i> plot armor that a minor splinter group, starting out with no magic (because they'd just utterly destroyed their Avatars and hadn't developed Thaum yet), hated by most of the Order of Hermes, Clan Tzimisce, and many others, survived everything and came out with super awesome magic that's better than anyone else's because they're so cool?<br /> <br /> People here love talking about how House Carna shouldn't have been able to exist for more than a week because the greater organization of the Tremere would have instantly annihilated them. Shouldn't the same have applied when the Tremere first turned themselves into vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:48:40-07:00","id":1380702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380698#post1380698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, that's actually one of the examples of Tremere having plot armor,</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere represents how WW love the magicians, they are Bad Bad Evil Gary Stu<br /> <br /> They have the most extended blood magic (and discipline), which is so versatile that can be compared to Magick<br /> <br /> Their history is full of badass, achieving a lot and almost unbelievable, just a glimpse:<br /> As you say, survive wars with many vampire factions which are much older than the Order of Hermes <br /> Become the most powerful mordern clan <br /> Attain something which worth centuries of effects of other clans","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T10:58:03-07:00","id":1380704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380691#post1380691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But they may be more infernal and darker</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean because of the Yomi spread? Possibly. That could be a start of them; however, as soon as they get 'educated' on their first steps on their Dharmas, they could break the infernal mold. Another question would be, who starts educating them and where from they get initial support and guidance? Maybe we could see the nascent Gui Ren courts of Eu and NA in not-so-distant future, for that purpose. Instead of a racist GLO, they perform educational missions on behalf of the most wise and strategic-minded Asian Gui Ren who see this worldwide spread of 'awakenings' both as an opportunity and as a sign of the next Age coming and feeling it's their sacred duty to lend a hand and avoid the newly reborn filling akuma ranks which is an inevitable outcome for those reborn in the west w/o proper guidance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:03:11-07:00","id":1380705,"title":"","content":"The Tremere's build up was gradual. They had to fight tooth to limb to get through all their trials. They lost alot to justify their gains. Their gradual ascension isn't an asspull, its backed by feats and lore. SI doesn't have that. Its just a faction that formed because somehow Shrecknet was breached just 'cuz. They aren't comparable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:07:40-07:00","id":1380707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pleiades</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380698#post1380698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> yeah, that's actually one of the examples of Tremere having plot armor,<br /> realistically, they wouldn't have survived their first decade...or even their first year...yet they did,<br /> the Tremere standing up against all their enemies was, to use your phrasing, an asspull<br /> <br /> imo, the only 'realistic' explanation people have come up with was that they had antideluvian backing (or kupala or something),<br /> and even that was a stretch into plot device territory<br /> <br /> people seem to be doing the same with the SI destroying Vienna...another antideluvian intervention,<br /> but I honestly don't think we need to go that far for it to be believable,<br /> vampires were always the squishy bugs of the WoD,<br /> Tremere might be a bit less squishy, but squishy nonetheless</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> The whole Tremere thing was importantly, blatantly OP from any perspective - vampion, 'serious roleplaying' tm, metaplot etc. Sabbat being somehow capable to defeat Camarilla strongholds with Chantires in them utilizing shovelheads, blood brothers, vozhd and black hand kamuts is another example of the necessity of new plot armor countering the previous one.<br /> <br /> Recalling the Dark ages; they simply cheated from the very start. Now, the retribution came to them. Don't forget how thoroughly the Carna/White Worm/Goratrix stuff shook up the whole Pyramid. That's a nice reprimand for their blatant OPedness throughout millenia and especially at the start.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing, on a more personal, joking level: guys, you made a huge, HUGE freaking mistake messing with the Tzimisce at the very start of your brilliant but inevitably doomed career.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:08:53-07:00","id":1380708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380704#post1380704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean because of the Yomi spread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I originally mean, compare their states in Blood &amp; Silk and Core, you\u2019ll find they become more depraved as the Age passes, the wickedness of world is growing. Spread of Yomi may also contribute to this<br /> <br /> Their curse is stronger, and they become weaker,<br /> More and more people fall into Yomi<br /> P\u2019o is 3 in modern, not 1<br /> Negative soul situations are harder to resist<br /> Sunlight is more lethal to them<br /> Many powers change, become darker (Shintais for example), or simply disappeared (Most Rites in that book)<br /> Their enlightenment become harder (remember, Dharma 5 in B&amp;S is equal to Dharma 6 in the power term)<br /> ...<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s 20 years ago, today they will fall deeper","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-12-2020, 02:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:17:27-07:00","id":1380709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380708#post1380708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I originally mean, compare their states in Blood &amp; Silk and Core, you\u2019ll find they become more depraved as the Age passes, the wickedness of world is growing. Spread of Yomi may also contribute to this<br /> <br /> Their curse is stronger, and they become weaker,<br /> More and more people fall into Yomi<br /> P\u2019o is 3 in modern, not 1<br /> Negative soul situations are harder to resist<br /> Sunlight is more lethal to them<br /> Many powers change, become darker (Shintais for example), or simply disappeared (Most Rites in that book)<br /> Their enlightenment become harder (remember, Dharma 5 in B&amp;S is equal to Dharma 6 in the power term)<br /> ...<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s 20 years ago, today they will fall deeper</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply in terms of the ages, there are centuries between Blood&amp;Silk and KotE 1998-2004; now, it's just 20 years. Even if the situation worsens (that's a nice hint, I like it to amplify grimdark), it's not as nasty as for newly awakened Gui Ren instantly fall to P'o. Maybe it'll be even more arduous for the new Chih-mei to remain mentally intact than it was before; but then again, guess how many karmically indebted people would start 'awakening' as Yomi Wan extends to the rest of the world?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:29:39-07:00","id":1380710,"title":"","content":"The Tremere are OP at face value, but really, it makes sense when you look at it critically. <br /> <br /> Unlike their vampire enemies, they are highly organized and provide a very vaulable service for which to gain favour. Thaumaturgy is like the tech sector of prestation: Little investment, lots of gains. Even with the Noble Roads being popular about this time, the Tremere have a big advantage in their early nights against their devided enemies. And Cities are smaller during this time so once the Tremere really establish themselves in a place, they've basically got the whole area covered. <br /> <br /> Unlike the order of Hermes, The Tremere can recruit very, very quickly and low level vampires&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;&gt;low level mages. In an attrition war, of course they'd win. But the biggest thing about this is that these wars, the Omen war (Does that apply to the Hermetic war or just the inter-vampire stuff?) was a protracted struggle that lasted for hundreds of years. The Tremere as a clan might have constantly been fighting, but on a local level they only fought occasionally. <br /> <br /> The Tremere never had plot armour, they were just what would happen if a very organized faction of intellegent bloodmages emerged among the vampires. They're not a Mary sue faction, because they're known to be agressive and untrustworthy and, as intelligent as they all are, bloodmagic is not a calling for social butterflies; They've certainly made mistakes. Consider this: You guys who don't like the Tremere have fallen for the same reasons the people in universe don't like the Tremere. That's some brilliant literary work right there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:30:43-07:00","id":1380711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380709#post1380709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply in terms of the ages, there are centuries between Blood&amp;Silk and KotE 1998-2004; now, it's just 20 years. Even if the situation worsens (that's a nice hint, I like it to amplify grimdark), it's not as nasty as for newly awakened Gui Ren instantly fall to P'o.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is uncertain<br /> <br /> W20 is also 20 years later, but the situation is worse, obviously. Gauntlet is harder. Gaia is dying, more. The related system is fixed a bit if you compare both. And I think it is not impossible for wan gui to fall deeper<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380709#post1380709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> guess how many karmically indebted people would start 'awakening' as Yomi Wan extends to the rest of the world?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a thought: More foreigner-looking kanbujian will rise, not limited to asian features <br /> <br /> and most of them can\u2019t be educated well, becoming chin-mei or akuma or scorpion eater (it\u2019s a nasty dharma, but has much potential, sadly). And more wan gui will rise generally","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:38:26-07:00","id":1380714,"title":"","content":"So much Tremere fanboyism I can't even. People forget that simple fact of the whole Vampire setting: nothing happens of good will. There are no individuals or groups who achieve great results through sheer grit, skill and perseverance. On a PC level, probably. On a Antediluvian-metaplot level - not a chance.<br /> <br /> Tremere are a result of Jyhad machinations, nothing more. A tool of (at least) two Antediluvians + one Earthbound. The rest is left to ST's and players' imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:44:47-07:00","id":1380716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380714#post1380714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So much Tremere fanboyism I can't even. People forget that simple fact of the whole Vampire setting: nothing happens of good will. There are no individuals or groups who achieve great results through sheer grit, skill and perseverance. On a PC level, probably. On a Antediluvian-metaplot level - not a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s World of Darkness, a low fantasy world. That\u2019s also the reason why there\u2019s no really powerful individuals or organizations which devote to true \u201crighteous\u201d goal: Purge the evil, Protect the humanity, just like those in Anime: Alucard, Vampire Hunter D... which is very, very romantic and even ridiculous in VtM","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:49:45-07:00","id":1380719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380711#post1380711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a thought: More foreigner-looking kanbujian will rise, not limited to asian features</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's not just my thought, it's my whole idea. Karmic indebtment should not be limited to race, blood, origin etc. Imagine the very concept of Karma becoming applicable to the humankind as whole (as it should be from the start, imho). How many wan gui start 'awakening'. Even if most of them turn akuma or scorpion-eaters, the general number of wan gui who somehow get past or are guided to get past the chih-mei state successfully would rise drastically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and most of them can\u2019t be educated well, becoming chin-mei or akuma or scorpion eater (it\u2019s a nasty dharma, but has much potential, sadly). And more wan gui will rise generally </div> </div> </div>Yepp, that;s somewhere close where I see it. The situation is even more dire than it was 20 years ago but the hope remains.<br /> Scorpion-eaters are truly a tough 'dharma' to play. but as NPCs they would be amazing (not just simply as enemies).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:53:17-07:00","id":1380721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380711#post1380711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is uncertain<br /> <br /> W20 is also 20 years later, but the situation is worse, obviously. Gauntlet is harder. Gaia is dying, more. The related system is fixed a bit if you compare both. And I think it is not impossible for wan gui to fall deeper<br /> <br /> <br /> Just a thought: More foreigner-looking kanbujian will rise, not limited to asian features<br /> <br /> and most of them can\u2019t be educated well, becoming chin-mei or akuma or scorpion eater (it\u2019s a nasty dharma, but has much potential, sadly). And more wan gui will rise generally</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That checks out with how the Wicked City ended up uncomfortably close to the CyberRealm in Umbra Revised (coinciding with Malfeas moving from the Deep to the Near Umbra).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T11:56:15-07:00","id":1380723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380705#post1380705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Tremere's build up was gradual. They had to fight tooth to limb to get through all their trials. They lost alot to justify their gains. Their gradual ascension isn't an asspull, its backed by feats and lore. SI doesn't have that. Its just a faction that formed because somehow Shrecknet was breached just 'cuz. They aren't comparable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fucking what?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Tremere's build up was gradual&quot; Right. Right. See, again. Absolute shenanigans here. Remember kids. The Tremere lore was always justified and definitely didn't have to be built up over multiple books, but the SI? Again. Even with it being explained and walked through, that isn't justification enough. We just need to make a sect of Tremere where they run everything because that's what all the tremere-stans clearly want. Tremere supremacy, maybe they'll write a book where the Tremere decide to finish what they started and go enslave the Order of Hermes because it has been 'backed by feats and lore'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24893-necroticbinder","name":"Necroticbinder","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:01:41-07:00","id":1380724,"title":"","content":"Gonna throw it out there; Hypertech is the bees knees and they Cyberrealm and wicked city are cool, those glass walkers that went nuts and did sick things in the name of cybernetics are metal as hell, and the WoD would only benefit from more Hypertech. If Hunters and vampires alike had better access to cybernetics, the world of darkness would be a better place (Still horrific for the residents, but more fun to play with) . Cyborgs&gt;Imbued (Though I do like &quot;MISSION FROM GOD&quot; characters quite a bit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:07:09-07:00","id":1380727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Necroticbinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380723#post1380723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fucking what?<br /> <br /> &quot;The Tremere's build up was gradual&quot; Right. Right. See, again. Absolute shenanigans here. Remember kids. The Tremere lore was always justified and definitely didn't have to be built up over multiple books, but the SI? Again. Even with it being explained and walked through, that isn't justification enough. We just need to make a sect of Tremere where they run everything because that's what all the tremere-stans clearly want. Tremere supremacy, maybe they'll write a book where the Tremere decide to finish what they started and go enslave the Order of Hermes because it has been 'backed by feats and lore'.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So, if I rephrased this a little to be less mad, it'd make a great unironic argument.<br /> Yeah, the Tremere had hundreds of years and used universal metaphysics (magic) to their advantage. They were the merchants in a time of fuedalism, and like the merchants they eventually won out for the renaissance.<br /> The SI exist because the elders disapeared, vital disciplines got nerfed, everyone in the camarilla is incompetent, and all the hidden, isolated groups of vampire hunters discovered eachother on facebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:09:00-07:00","id":1380728,"title":"","content":"I'm not a Tremere-&quot;stan&quot; at all. I'm just arguing that the Second Inquisition is just a bad piece that should've never been incorporated. Their droning of the main HQ of the Tremere that wards tech, can't be seen by humans because its disguised, and a place that always teleports doesn't make sense. The SI just somehow droning Italy without their advance knowledge is ridiculous. The SI is just going to snowball doing more ridiculous things, Tremere was just starting point. Thats why I suggested the Imbued over the Inquisiton. They are more sensible in regards to how such an OP Hunting faction would work.<br /> <br /> Actually the Imbued aren't a faction, but a loose federation. They would've been the better &quot;Hunter Faction&quot; because while disorganized and not very connected, they have the most logical reason to take down wide swathes of Vampire society. Edges, with the fact they are also gifted with Second Sight. They still definitely would've been the &quot;underdogs&quot; (which I never even considered them that in the first place) while having reasons to BTFO the Cam, Sabbat, and most of Vampire society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:11:42-07:00","id":1380730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rock113</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380716#post1380716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s World of Darkness, a low fantasy world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. The main theme and mood of WoD and VtM in particular has one omnipresent shtick: nothing lasts. Everything rots. Organizations get betrayes in their ranks; personal vampiric agenda and passions always, ALWAYS prevail over common goals. Initiatives getting compromised by individual failures; fractionism, intrigue and infighting undermine seemingly well-going campaigns. Tremere were rid of all of that for centures; why? for people who love them, that's rule of the cool - look at their arguments. for those who see them as a part of WoD, they were an anomaly hidden by plot armour at worst; Saulot/Tzimisce/Kupala Jyhad trump card at best.<br /> <br /> The whole Vampire is about personal in the first place. Look at the relationships at the top of the Pyramid: do you see men of great personal integrity who respect and treat each other with mutual earnestness and put personal things aside working towards common success? Lmao.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> organizations which devote to true \u201crighteous\u201d goal: Purge the evil, Protect the humanity, just like those in Anime: Alucard, Vampire Hunter D... which is very, very romantic and even ridiculous in VtM </div> </div> </div>Well, among dozens upon dozens of sects, cults, factions and organizations, there was one in Dark Ages... but turned into Surveillance state in modern days. *sad trombone*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-12-2020, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:13:00-07:00","id":1380732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380724#post1380724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gonna throw it out there; Hypertech is the bees knees and they Cyberrealm and wicked city are cool, those glass walkers that went nuts and did sick things in the name of cybernetics are metal as hell, and the WoD would only benefit from more Hypertech. If Hunters and vampires alike had better access to cybernetics, the world of darkness would be a better place (Still horrific for the residents, but more fun to play with) . Cyborgs&gt;Imbued (Though I do like &quot;MISSION FROM GOD&quot; characters quite a bit)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hypertech is a Mage concept. Unless you're playing Mage, you won't use it, as other games don't assume that reality needs a bunch of humans to clap their hands and accept next gen batteries and laser systems into their beliefs. In Book of the Weaver, for example, all of the advanced, vaguely near sci-fi stuff is a Device, and Paradox is nowhere to be found. Unless, you know, you view maintenance and repairs as Paradox, but if you take that far enough, living beings needing to drink water is a result of Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:28:49-07:00","id":1380738,"title":"","content":"When I say hypertech, I just mean Technology that isn't purely tech and needs magic to function; Jetpacks, Laser rifles, Cybernetics that exceed human performance, Nanites. I don't care if it's filled with quintessence, houses a spirit, got enchanted by normal means or was installed by a Tzmisce and uses Vitae to function. A hunter faction with this stuff would rock, and a vampire faction moreso. But it's not a truism. It doesn't reflect our reality; so we can't have them actually make huge metaplot defining moves like blowing up Vienna. At best they can kill a prince of chicago. Maybe in twenty years we can justify it better, no? <br /> <br /> V5s large scale inquisition feels like a farce<br /> Because in reality, is the goverment cracking down on the rich? Are they all getting globalized to fight international white collar crime? Are the elites being persecuted by the system they've created? <br /> No<br /> They're not. <br /> Beyond vocal outcry from a few young people without real power, the rich are only getting richer and the system is supporting them. Vampires, as analogues of these elites, really aren't supposed to be hunted around now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:57:55-07:00","id":1380746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380701#post1380701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How is it <i>not</i> plot armor that a minor splinter group, starting out with no magic (because they'd just utterly destroyed their Avatars and hadn't developed Thaum yet), hated by most of the Order of Hermes, Clan Tzimisce, and many others, survived everything and came out with super awesome magic that's better than anyone else's because they're so cool?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How did the small (but higly militarized) state of Prussia stand 7 years against the combined forces of France, the Holy Roman Empire and Russia and rose to became one of the major superpower of continental europe?<br /> <br /> <br /> Or how did the small nomadic civilization of the Khamag Mongols step out of anarchy and internal strife to unite all the tribes of Mongolia under one banner and create the greatest empire ever seen? Crushing under their feet bigger empires and more complex civilizations like the Chinese Empire, Khwarzemia and Kievan Rus?<br /> <br /> And how did the people of France take power from the Monarchy and survived a war against ALL of Europe, and later conquered most of it for a time?<br /> <br /> Or how did the small revolutionary group like the Bolsheviks take power in Russia, a weak nation at the start of the XX\u00b0 century, and turned it in the second super-power in the world?<br /> <br /> Time,good generals, charismatic leaders, wise diplomacy, and a lot of luck.<br /> It doesn't happen often, but sometimes it does happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-12-2020, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:08:19-07:00","id":1380748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380746#post1380746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time,good generals, charismatic leaders, wise diplomacy, and a lot of luck.<br /> It doesn't happen often, but sometimes it does happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>My issue is, the Tremere didn't do it through diplomacy or making allies (at least not initially). Their initial strategy seems to have just involved making more and more enemies, until they finally figured out a way to use blood magic and had some ability to fight back.<br /> <br /> Like, at the beginning they had no magic, no Gargoyles, no shock troops, no military force, against the Tzimisce who had magic, had vozhd, had szlachta, and had military force. And also the Order of Hermes, pretty much the largest unified organization of Awakened mages at the time, wanted them destroyed. And yet somehow the Tremere won that fight, because the plot required it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:20:24-07:00","id":1380751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380748#post1380748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My issue is, the Tremere didn't do it through diplomacy or making allies (at least not initially). Their initial strategy seems to have just involved making more and more enemies, until they finally figured out a way to use blood magic and had some ability to fight back.<br /> <br /> Like, at the beginning they had no magic, no Gargoyles, no shock troops, no military force, against the Tzimisce who had magic, had vozhd, had szlachta, and had military force. And also the Order of Hermes, pretty much the largest unified organization of Awakened mages at the time, wanted them destroyed. And yet somehow the Tremere won that fight, because the plot required it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually in their beginning they did it through subtlety. It's not like the Seven became vampire and the day after every one knew. It was slow. The Order took almost a century to understand what was happening inside House Tremere.<br /> Tremere and Etrius started immediately the study of a new form of magic, which is easier to develop if one of you is one of 12 founding archmages of the Order of Hermes.<br /> <br /> Having previous magic knowledge has always been quite the edge for great thaumaturgists. Al-Ashrad was a powerful mage, Baba Yaga was a witch, and so on. How did they become such powerful blood mages? Because they already knew most of the rules.<br /> <br /> They pushed for diplomacy almost immediatly, as they allied with the Eastern Lords of Jurgen against the Voivodate and sent emissaries in every vampiric court, just think about Goratrix who became a major player in Paris.<br /> <br /> Even more, their enemies were scattered and weak. Tzimisce had magic, Vozhd and so on... but every Voivode was for himself and the Tzimisce were plagued by infightings: Noriz tried to conquer Yorak power, Rustovich lacked support from the other voivodes, Byelobog played deaf and the Carpathian Tzimisce had quarrels with the Obertus. The main Tzimisce strategy was opening their gates to the Tatars and the Mongols, in the hope that the horde would crush the Tremere.<br /> As for the Nosferatu and the Gangrel they lacked clan structure to push against the Ventrue-Tremere alliance.<br /> <br /> <br /> Most important thing: when the war with the Tzimisce started most of the Tremere were still mages, with True Magic. Most of the Clan was embraced much later<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> He turned his fury to the war against the Tzimisce,<br /> whose ghoul armies once again stepped up their attacks.<br /> These assaults waxed and waned over the ensuing decades.<br /> The night creatures would ravage the outlying<br /> chantries, come howling to the very gate of Ceoris, and<br /> lay siege to it. Then the desperate magi would marshal<br /> their dwindling power, blast the creatures with a terrible<br /> working, and send them yelping back to their havens<br /> in northern Transylvania. At first I had hopes that the<br /> war would change things, but as the cycle repeated, I<br /> saw in it only tedium and perhaps a cryptic joke of destiny.<br /> Perhaps you are fond of dates, Bitiurges, so I will<br /> list the years of the worst fighting: 1040, 1046, 1062,<br /> 1066, 1086, and 1105. I do not entirely understand the<br /> long pauses between assaults, for I claim no insight into<br /> the Tzimisce mind. <b>At any rate, the magi, during the<br /> periods from 1047 to 1061 and from 1067 to 1085, were<br /> able to erect wards to keep night creatures from even<br /> approaching our holdings. They rebuilt the outlying<br /> chantries during these times, frantically stockpiling vis<br /> for future use. Then the wards failed, the enemy armies<br /> once more descended, and the magi fled back to their<br /> chantry of chantries.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Many who dwell within these walls were Embraced<br /> during this time.</b> You know blade-tongued Malgorzata.<br /> Did you know she is not a noble, but a young<br /> local Goratrix purchased from field-worker parents?<br /> He made her his apprentice, sheltering her from his<br /> rivals. As is so often the case with apprentices, she<br /> became a coarser, less subtle version of her master,<br /> emulating and exaggerating his most blatant traits.<br /> Her boldness and quick rise won few friends but won<br /> the admiration of other apprentices. Five years after<br /> her own Embrace, she brought her most wet-lipped<br /> admirer, Jervais, into the Cainite fold.<br /> A great Tzimisce offensive came in 1105. It crushed<br /> all of the Transylvanian chantries outside Ceoris. Goratrix<br /> struggled against the call of the blood oath, wishing<br /> to Embrace all of Ceoris\u2019 magi at once to better enlist<br /> them in the war. Although he Embraced a few individuals<br /> then, he could not break with Tremere\u2019s </div> </div> </div><br /> In 1125 Goratrix had the army gargoyle ready, that's the moment the tides of war turned<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In 1121, Goratrix unveiled the first of this remade<br /> race. The first Gargoyle was named Chaundice. It was<br /> to become typical of its kind, with a demonic visage,<br /> stony skin, fearsome claws and bat-like wings. But Goratrix,<br /> Malgorzata and Virstania spawned many other<br /> types of Gargoyles, ultimately less successful in design,<br /> during these years.<br /> <b>By 1125, they\u2019d created enough of these fearsome<br /> servants to turn them loose on their foes. The Gargoyles<br /> turned the tide of war against the Tzimisce. They flew<br /> out over the battlefield, homing in on the few vampires<br /> among the throng of blood-crazed ghouls and terrified<br /> mortal warriors. They swooped down and plucked them<br /> up, bearing them to Ceoris, where they too would become<br /> raw material for new Gargoyles</b>. </div> </div> </div>Thaumaturgy was researched between the 1037 and the 1121<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Tremere and Etrius were not idle during this<br /> near-century of bloodshed. <b>From 1037 to 1121, they<br /> traveled from one chantry to the next, conducting the<br /> secret experiments that spawned their vampiric art of<br /> Thaumaturgy. They had begun such work in Ceoris and<br /> now continued it abroad. It converted the spells and<br /> incantations of hermetic magic to a system of power<br /> dependent not on vis, but on the supernatural potency<br /> of blood as converted and stored by the vampire\u2019s body.<br /> The two appeared at Ceoris only to exchange their<br /> resulting insights with those pearled from Goratrix\u2019s<br /> Gargoyle project. Much of the first seven decades of<br /> their inquiries consisted of theoretical work. Practical<br /> breakthroughs were apparently slow in coming and I<br /> watched Goratrix use the addictive properties of his<br /> blood to enslave several magi to serve as his proxy in<br /> the Gargoyle project and other matters.</b><br /> Tremere and Etrius expended the final twenty years<br /> finding specific hermetic spells and rituals amenable<br /> to blood magic conversion and translating them into<br /> thaumaturgic formulae. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> For the first century of fight the Tzimisce fought against a house of mages, with true magic. So no, no &quot;magical plot armor&quot;, but &quot;armor by magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> After the first century...Gargoyle and Thaumaturgy closed the gap.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mortal Magi<br /> The blood-made mages\u2019 humor cannot be improved<br /> by the need to treat mortal mages as their equals. Do<br /> not mistake me for a member of Goratrix\u2019s faction. I do<br /> not claim that they should all be Embraced forthwith.<br /> And I avow that I have no easy deception with which<br /> to convince the unaware mortals to accept the sudden<br /> elevation of the blooded above them. Still, everything<br /> about our former peers grates upon my senses, though I<br /> be but the most mild of our hidden cabal. The longer<br /> they accept our deception, the more foolish they seem<br /> and the more trying it becomes to countenance their<br /> blind arrogance. We never appear by day. Our pallor<br /> exceeds even that of the typical scholar, for whom<br /> sunlight is but a reminder that he\u2019s strayed too far from<br /> his library carrel. We speak in a code in front of them,<br /> exchanging meaningful glances and furtive gestures.<br /> Indeed, we did have to behead Jacobus last year when<br /> he stumbled upon a feeding. But the others \u2014 they were<br /> too occupied trying to wring the last drams of vis from<br /> the land to take notice of the flaws in our hastily-constructed<br /> tale of his demise. I should not be infuriated<br /> that our plan effects itself so well upon them, but by the<br /> tears of Croesus, I am! I once thought these fools to be<br /> my peers in learning, cunning and ambition! Magi of<br /> House Tremere, masters in the making of the Order of<br /> Hermes! That they be fooled so easily galls me. And as<br /> I said, I am the mildest among us.<br /> The paradox doubles in upon itself when you consider<br /> that the mortal mages are infinitely more pliant and<br /> obedient than their secret masters. They greatly fear the<br /> vampires hammering at our gates, especially as the power<br /> of vis drains away from them. We blooded are nothing if<br /> not cocksure, and they instinctively defer to our sense of<br /> assurance. They accept me as castellan, as your eyes and<br /> ears, and follow my commands with as little argument as<br /> can be expected. Malgorzata awakens in them their primal<br /> instincts to submit, as if they see in her the incarnation<br /> of some primordial and capricious bog-goddess. They see<br /> Virstania as their savior for making the Gargoyles. They<br /> do not ask themselves how she came upon the vampiric<br /> secrets needed to construct them.<br /> Therein lies the truth, I judge. It is not so much that<br /> we are fooling them as they are allowing themselves to<br /> be fooled. They smell the coppery tang of blood in the<br /> air. They see what drips from the walls when the moon<br /> is wrong. The screams from below do not escape their<br /> ears. But they fear to broach the subject, comprehending<br /> that their fate is entirely in our hands. </div> </div> </div><br /> It was not unitl 1202 that the Order of Hermes understood that House Tremere was ruled by vampires. 176 years after the ritual of Goratrix.<br /> At that point, it was already too late.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-12-2020, 04:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:01:31-07:00","id":1380761,"title":"","content":"From guide to the low clans<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> Very shortly after the Experiment, the Seven had<br /> infected a number of the score or so of chantries in<br /> Eastern Europe with the Embrace. This was a course few<br /> of them actually thought wise, except perhaps Goratrix,<br /> but Tremere insisted. He pointed out that the strength<br /> of the Tremere had always been their ability to work<br /> in concert; more Cainite magi meant more research<br /> into the adaptation of Hermetic theory to vampiric<br /> capabilities. More likely, he simply had no intention<br /> of giving up the house he had founded so long ago, his<br /> proudest achievement. If he had fallen into damnation,<br /> it would just have to come along with him.<b> He<br /> discovered to his chagrin that chantries of vampire<br /> magi fell to Tzimisce assault far more quickly than the<br /> mortal sort. The Fiends knew much more about fighting<br /> Cainites than wizards, after all, and the vampire magi<br /> were all but helpless in any case, stripped of their old<br /> powers and unacquainted with the new.</b><br /> <br /> Over Goratrix\u2019s protests and much to Etrius\u2019<br /> relief, <b>Tremere decided that the ultimate conversion<br /> of House Tremere would have to proceed gradually,<br /> and so it did. Mortal Tremere did the greater part of<br /> the work in repelling Tzimisce depredations \u2014 unwittingly<br /> protecting the creatures that skulked behind<br /> them (and in a very few cases among them), while<br /> the vampires relearned the Art in a new form and<br /> awaited the right time to bring the entire House over<br /> the threshold. The Tzimisce withdrew to lick their<br /> wounds, rethink their strategy and blame each others\u2019<br /> patriarchs and matriarchs for their failure. This<br /> sequence was repeated on larger and larger scale over<br /> the next two centuries. Thinking back to the koldun<br /> auguries that started it all and appalled by what they<br /> found in the chantries they vanquished, the younger<br /> Tzimisce who laid most of the actual sieges took<br /> to calling their crusade the \u201cwar of omens.\u201d But in<br /> truth, the real war had yet to be joined because the<br /> Tremere remained on the defensive.</b> That, of course,<br /> would change. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T16:41:32-07:00","id":1380788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380738#post1380738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I say hypertech, I just mean Technology that isn't purely tech and needs magic to function; Jetpacks, Laser rifles, Cybernetics that exceed human performance, Nanites. I don't care if it's filled with quintessence, houses a spirit, got enchanted by normal means or was installed by a Tzmisce and uses Vitae to function. A hunter faction with this stuff would rock, and a vampire faction moreso. But it's not a truism. It doesn't reflect our reality; so we can't have them actually make huge metaplot defining moves like blowing up Vienna. At best they can kill a prince of chicago. Maybe in twenty years we can justify it better, no?<br /> <br /> V5s large scale inquisition feels like a farce<br /> Because in reality, is the goverment cracking down on the rich? Are they all getting globalized to fight international white collar crime? Are the elites being persecuted by the system they've created?<br /> No<br /> They're not.<br /> Beyond vocal outcry from a few young people without real power, the rich are only getting richer and the system is supporting them. Vampires, as analogues of these elites, really aren't supposed to be hunted around now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cybernetics as presented in BotWe don't require magical energy of any kind to function, and neither do a lot of the other material that would count as a &quot;wonder&quot; under Mage. That's what I mean when I said that Hypertech wasn't necessary to import over as a concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T16:44:13-07:00","id":1380789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380655#post1380655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Knowing your vision of the sect, I guess it's for the best.</div> </div> </div> </div>May I ask what you think is my vision for the sect?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I say that as long time Sabbat/Paths player. If authors went at least close to where you see Sabbat it would bury V5 for me. </div> </div> </div>Broken up into feuding factions ala Beckett's Jyhad Diary?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Even leaving them as mysterious bogeymen would be a more respectful approach than downgrading them into Belial's brood you see them as. </div> </div> </div>That's actually where they are in THE CHICAGO FOLIOS. I think that isn't a very good use for them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Wan Kuei concepts were amazing. To some, including me, a whole next level after the indivudalistic approach of Vampire. I'd rather spread Gui Ren 'awakenings' across the planet instead of being limited to one region as well as opening said region to cainites. </div> </div> </div>I think that you either should have vampires who create or vampires who come from the ground but not both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T16:53:15-07:00","id":1380791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380789#post1380789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I think that you either should have vampires who create or vampires who come from the ground but not both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't Dracula originally a vampire that rose from his grave and then turned others?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:28:58-07:00","id":1380799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380791#post1380791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wasn't Dracula originally a vampire that rose from his grave and then turned others?</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I know, Dracula's origins are never explained.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T17:44:38-07:00","id":1380805,"title":"","content":"By the way it seems clear to me that a lot of people really never studied the Tremere.<br /> It's clear that people just read the Tremere entry in the Corebook, say &quot;Oh shit evil Wiza' who broke the setting!&quot; and after that never ever read a Tremere sourcebook.<br /> I didn't took some mystical an forgotten developer commentary found in a secret archive, those are entries from House of Tremere and Player Guide to the Low Clans.<br /> <br /> <br /> Because while it is true that Blood Magic was overpowered and needed a lot of balance (no doubt, but still... this is a common problem with linear magic and magic in general), the Tremere were quite far from being a really overpowered Clan (unless obviously your storyteller was a lazy dude who never opened one of their sourcebooks).<br /> <br /> What they gained in terms of magic power and cohesion was balanced by the distrust and the internal power plays. Tremere are hated, and distrusted, this is clear from pretty much every sourcebook. Most vampires in the Camarilla just think that the Tremere are evil wizards plotting something. Do you remember D.C. By Night? Probably the most powerful clan in town, and yet they were incapable of ousting Vitel because no one trusted them and most vampire prefered Vitel to Peter Dorfman.<br /> And outside the Camarilla? Well, it's not like the Tzimisce have forgot, and when sieges and crusades start, the Tremere Chantry is the first place that gets nuked.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even more Clan Tremere, just like the Order of Hermes, is built for internal conflict. Since the original Clanbook Clan Tremere is plenty of factions that fight against each other. The main fight was between Traditionalist and Transitionalist, plus several minor factions like the Human League, the Guardians of Traditions or the Elite. What a Tremere gains in terms of protection against rival clans a Tremere lose in terms of trust inside his own. The worst enemy of a Tremere is not a Brujah or a Ventrue who fight against his dominion: it's his own apprentice, or his Regent, or his best friend that was coopted by one of the secret societies inside the Clan.<br /> <br /> This was true also in Dark Ages where the fight was between Etrius' faction and Goratrix. House of Tremere is a whole sourcebook about the inner fightings inside Ceoris, with plenty of factions, distrust, plots and daggers in the shadows...<br /> <br /> Which is consistent with the Tremere concept.<br /> It is just like the Order of Hermes,They have more men, more artifacts, a better political structure, and the most powerful Chantry in the world, and people like Caeron Mustai and Sao Cristavao who had too much power, and used it badly. The Hermetic had several edges that put them far ahead the other Traditions (which is a point that is often treated in the metaplot, several books in mage tell us that the other Traditions distrust the Order of Hermes and its power).<br /> And just like the Tremere your worst enemy is not the Man in Black from the NWO, but the brother from another House. It's the mage from House Janissaries that will spy on you and use you in the game of the Order, is the Quaesitor who will judge you for you errors, or the Tytalus who will challenge you for power and dominance. Doissetep was a nest of vipers, that collapsed for the internal strife between Porthos and Mustai.<br /> <br /> Now, I understand that probably many storyellers are lazy, and make things easy for Tremere players by not offering a correct picture of the inner treachery of the clan and strife for power between clan mates, but this is not a problem of Clan Tremere, is a problem with lazy storytellers and lazy players who do not study sourcebooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-12-2020, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T18:51:00-07:00","id":1380820,"title":"","content":"Just a last note: The problem with Vienna's bombing is not that Vienna got bombed and the Tremere had a major advancement in meta-plot: the problem is that Vienna's bombing is bad writing. Period.<br /> <br /> There were tons of tools to destroy the Vienna's Chantry and reach the same end. When people try to put up theories about the worm, or a spy in the inner council and so on, it's because there is no problem with Vienna being crushed in one of the eternal moves of the Jyhad. The problem is that doing that with SWAT teams and drone strikes is dumb and stupid and lazy.<br /> <br /> I will use again Mage, given the deep link that it has with the Tremere: no one complains because Doissetep was nuked, or because the Technocracy ravaged Horizon, and no one cries over the fate of Mistridge or the defection of the House of Helekar. And believe me, the fall of Doissetep and the fall of Horizon were FAR more important in terms of metaplot and consequences.<br /> <br /> BUT... they made sense, they were good writing. Yeah, it does make sense that internal strife between Porthos, Hortemone and Mustai would have lead to the fall of Doissetep, it's one of the basic premise of the Book of Chantries, no one can complain about that. And yeah, it does make sense that Horizon was sacked and destroyed by the the powerful Technocracy, with the help of a traitor from the Hollow Ones and the shock from Doissetep collapse. It does work.<br /> On the other hand, if you told me that Horizon was sacked thanks to a drone strike and SWAT teams... I would laugh. The end would be the same, the credibility would not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 04-13-2020, 07:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T19:31:09-07:00","id":1380828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380789#post1380789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> May I ask what you think is my vision for the sect?</div> </div> </div> </div>As you said yourself, breaking Sabbat apart with the most 'common', mainstream, devoted Sabbat proper - Gehenna Crusaders - to be turned into montycovened satanic locusts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Broken up into feuding factions ala Beckett's Jyhad Diary? </div> </div> </div>BJD only implies it can be done, depending on who becomes the Regent. The new Regent choice will also define the outcome of the 4th civil war of the sect.<br /> There is no true 100% direction mandated. At least six possible outcomes presented as suggestions to the ST. The 'canon' Regent is non-existent although it says Polonia is probably the strongest claimant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's actually where they are in THE CHICAGO FOLIOS. I think that isn't a very good use for them. </div> </div> </div>Didn't get my hands on those, so can't comment. I still think V5 books just present Sabbat as in the 1ed - nothing but vague speculations and an amplified aura of 'booo scary' for Anarch kids. In the corebook, they even added another alias of the sect - Black Church. Lol, seriously? What's next, Spooky Castle?<br /> <br /> I've read the post on your vision and could agree only on loyalists going into anarchs, making them more violent overall. I partially agree Moderates' elders going Camarilla or Oradea league or independent. However, after reading BJD and V5 corebook, I think we can safely say the authors articulated their idea pretty well: the most of Sabbat slowly but steadily has migrated to MENA and other warzones. 'Sabbat cities emptying out' is a pretty straightforward statement which leaves almost no room for interpretations. That also means the crusaders will become the core line of the sect, regardless if or when the Crusade ends.<br /> <br /> Now, here is where yours and my visions go the opposite ways. Your playable Sabbat is the back-up Sabbat - those who stayed, for whatever reason. Orthodoxy theologists mixed with some Inquisition mixed with some particularly devoted Loyalists and some particularly devoted Moderate researchers and scientists. The role of Belial brood in your version is left to crusaders who - most obviously in canon too - will form the bulk of the sect, with your playable 'sedated Sabbat' numbers-wise being nothing more than a handful of undercover agents and covens scattered across both Americas and Europe.<br /> <br /> My version makes the Sabbat cut out the ones who left or defected and leave the returning crusaders as playable. I would like to have them as a militant Tal'Mahe'Ra but with an opposite ideology and goals, being led by the Inquisition - False Hand either compromises itself completely (their ties with Ancients' worshippers cult got publicly exposed, for example) and was disbanded or put the goals of the sect first and merges with the Inquisition in order to avoid political infighting in the times of war. The Focus will shift from Cam-Sabbat war to Methuselahs-Tal-Mahe-Ra-Ancients-Infernalists, with Camarilla or Anarchs becoming targets of second or even third (after Second Inquisition) priority; Anarchs will be facing Sabbat only when the circumstances demand it from the latter (no more overt war on all fronts with everyone who's not Sabbat, I'd rather have such lunatics perish first under elders' fangs in the crusade. War is a harsh but very effective teacher).<br /> <br /> Rise of Inquisition is also heavily implied by BJD. As a long time Sabbat player, I noticed this trend in V20, when RotB introduced the Orthodox faction and their rites. Then we had BJD where Black Hand - the Revised's Sabbat champions who even got their own awesome book Caine's Chosen back in 2003 - were depicted as fallen from grace and eviscerated across Mexico City by Inquisition packs as the new civil war erupts. At the same time, Inquisition glows up from being a small club of 20 or so cainites in Revised to a heavyweight political player - Lucita as Regent will likely support Inquisition instead of Hand, and then Sandoza herself is presented as a possible Regent candidacy. That shift in the mood could indicate a crucial role Inquisition might play in the new Sabbat. One of their new primary goals would be the pruning of the new-Sabbat ranks from 'montycovened locusts' who lost their minds after gorging on elder blood.<br /> <br /> I really loved BH (Zillah's tribe) in revised and thought of them as an example of where I see the sect but writers went out of their way in V20/BJD to depict how irreversibly deep the Tal'Mahe'Ra infiltration goes. At this point, I don't believe False Hand can go on waging war on Ancients when there are the ancients' defenders among their very ranks. Sabbat got their suspicions voiced in 2004, I believe they'll manage to clear it all up by 2020 or whenever Sabbat is back as playable. I am also sure the Inquisition will probably do a much better job at educating younger Cainites embraced before and during the war in Paths; they are more into occult than Black Hand too, the very blob dedicated to the sect in V5 corebook says 'occultation of the Sabbat'. Obviously, I'm trying to connect all the dots here.<br /> <br /> Yes, I am pretty sure the Paths are crucial to the Sabbat, especially after going through hell of a war trying to fulfill their purpose and destiny as a sect; after supernatural horrors and atrocities they witnessed and committed 'over there', I doubt Humanity could hold any single one of them sane, let alone the newly embraced ones who will likely be the PCs. Paths were almost always either a central theme of my own Sab chronicles or of extreme importance.<br /> <br /> The main themes and moods would be post-human relationships; the price of war on human and post-human mind; the search for redemption in the face of atrocities both witnessed and committed; the consequences of indoctrination; and most of all, trauma and a quest for spirituality, camaraderie and brotherhood in the face of the worst the Vampire can put you against - your Beast, maddened by years of relentless global conflict against powers you can barely comprehend. How do you deal with it, where do you look for a moral compass and a backbone to carry on when the cosy familiar human-centric set of values (Humanity) is gone and your inner darkness is pressing down on you, who is beside you in these darkest moments and how it feels to see them meeting Final Death. I always felt the war or rather post-war themes present a unique opportunity for the most emotionally powerful Sabbat chronicles; the gehenna war and it's consequences are just that.<br /> <br /> I digress heavily from the thread's matter and I'd rather have a separate thread on Sabbat since it's my favorite part of VtM; I'd rather stop at this point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that you either should have vampires who create or vampires who come from the ground but not both. </div> </div> </div>I think otherwise. I see no problem with having both or even more. Also the downgrading the concept of Wan Guei to 'vampires who come from the ground' is a nice example why I found KotE more appealing and cannot understand their haters' POV. Not everything should be dubbed as 'bloodsucker from beyond the grave' especially if in it's origin it is not.<br /> Power through enlightenment and spirituality is a far more appealing concept to me than power through blood and generation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","user":"Val_Nir","date":". 04-12-2020, 11:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T20:37:02-07:00","id":1380843,"title":"","content":"I recommend checking out THE CHICAGO FOLIOS because it gives a lot of information beyond what would normally be available in a book that just deals with Chicago on both THE SABBAT and RAVNOS, which I didn't think would have information in both.<br /> <br /> On Page 78 and 79 of the book, they talk about the breakup of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <br /> <b>The Seven Fires</b><br /> <br /> Chicago, for all its corruption and horrors, understands though it may wallow in degradation, it has nothing on the empire of perpeturbation that is the Sabbat. Th city has had many horrific encounters with the fanatical sect, most recent being the dread nights of 1993. Little is known about the fringe and alien sect. What is known is the Sabbat relinquished control over its holdings and threw itself into a purported &quot;Gehenna War.&quot; With the advent of the Lasombra defection, there have been whispers of concern about what the Sabbat will do in retaliation. To help the Lasombra in their quest to join the Camarilla is to potentially put a target for the Sabbat on your back.<br /> <br /> The Chicago Sabbat have become a cell organization, perpetuating atrocities by some byzantine design. These cells have become known as &quot;The Seven Fires&quot;&lt; the surviving cells not called off to the Gehenna War, destroyed by Edward Neally, or killed by the defecting Lasombra. This is likely a name given to them due to their ferocity, related to their brutal &quot;ritae&quot;, often connected to fire, their appalling &quot;games&quot;, or something to do with their numbers of operatives or groups known as packs.<br /> <br /> The Seven Fires leave nothing but carnage and perplexing propaganda in their wake. In their graffiti, their trail of mutilated bodies, and arcane scrawl, they reference the story of Peter Pan, possibly an allusion to the Lasombra defection and &quot;losing their shadow.&quot; These Cainites are appearing close and closer to Chicago border, emerging in more run down or economically suburbs. </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>What Happened</b><br /> <br /> What befell the Sabbat in the United States is still broadly a mystery. Packs disappeared, the hierarchy dissolved, and many of the Cainites remaining in place lost their grip on reality and stability as their purpose disappeared. </div> </div> </div>I really like what they're alluding to with the changes to the Sabbat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T20:45:32-07:00","id":1380847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380843#post1380843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I recommend checking out THE CHICAGO FOLIOS because it gives a lot of information beyond what would normally be available in a book that just deals with Chicago on both THE SABBAT and RAVNOS, which I didn't think would have information in both.<br /> <br /> On Page 78 and 79 of the book, they talk about the breakup of the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> I really like what they're alluding to with the changes to the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>And what would that be?<br /> <br /> Thank you for the info from the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25988-val_nir","name":"Val_Nir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25988_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T20:46:25-07:00","id":1380848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Val_Nir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1380847#post1380847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And what would that be?<br /> <br /> Thank you for the info from the book.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380845-v5-the-sabbat-in-v5\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380845-v5-the-sabbat-in-v5\"> [V5] The Sabbat in V5 - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380845-v5-the-sabbat-in-v5\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1380845-v5-the-sabbat-in-v5 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> How would you handle the Sabbat in V5. This was posted in another thread and really interesting. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Made a thread for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:36:35-07:00","id":1381015,"title":"","content":"V5 and Tremere hate aside and back o topic. The reason is numbers. The imbued are not numerous enough to wage a full-scale war on the supernatural, but the alphabet agencies have the numbers and resources. How they fully discover the existence of vampires is up to the storyteller.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T10:55:36-07:00","id":1381021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kael03</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381015#post1381015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason is numbers. The imbued are not numerous enough to wage a full-scale war on the supernatural,</div> </div> </div> </div>This, many guys used to say imbueds are much weaker but more than their ancestor Wan Xian... Well, the truth is... they are neither greater nor more than their ancestors, in fact they may be one of the smallest splats<br /> <br /> Some used to count imbueds according to the statistics of Hunternet\u2019s online users, and they are no more than 600(I can\u2019t remember this sorry). Don\u2019t know how many of them today, but IMO won\u2019t be much more, in WoD sense<br /> <br /> The imbued is weaker in all aspects. If their patrons can return all original power to them, that\u2019s another thing","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-13-2020, 02:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:00:07-07:00","id":1381023,"title":"","content":"Imbueds is very contradictory in some ways. They\u2019re invested so few power that can\u2019t be corrupted directly, but they also can\u2019t complete their mission, and Earthbounds will indirectly corrupt them by offering equal power... <br /> <br /> If they are invested much power which is equal to their ancestors\u2019, they will be proud, paranoid and finally corrupted, just like Wan Xian","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24560,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","user":"Rock113","date":". 04-13-2020, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T14:46:04-07:00","id":1381101,"title":"","content":"I really have no problem with what the SI has done. Just how fast they did it. The speed of their learning curve totally breaks suspension of disbelief for me. They need to have some kind of supernatural backing, like Tremere, Vitel, or similar. They knew too much too soon for anything else. The first Inquisition got going with kindred using it against their enemies, and mortals gathering information and it snowballing out of control. That kindred just couldn't stay away from using hunters against each other works.<br /> <br /> Because yes, the stuff they've done so far is bad writing. It is a recurring problem in the writing of VtM. They build up the ancients into chtonic blood gods and then suddenly try to dispose of them like they are nothing, and claim it shows something. And then there is blowback and people asking &quot;What were you thinking?&quot;<br /> <br /> It happened when they disposed of Vitel the first time, Rayzeel, Boukephos, probably others I've forgotten. That these sudden whiplashes in the supposed danger level of the ancients destroys immersion is something that seems to need to be learned over and over again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2471-trollroot","name":"Trollroot","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T03:52:27-07:00","id":1381256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trollroot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381101#post1381101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really have no problem with what the SI has done. Just how fast they did it. The speed of their learning curve totally breaks suspension of disbelief for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>One oddity is the fact they're not really the Second Inquisition but the first. The Fall of London also has them be the Arcanum (or at least the London Branch).<br /> <br /> So they're not actually a learning curve. These people have been around for centuries.<br /> <br /> The Inquisition knows everything about vampires after all, they just don't care about most details. &quot;Yeah, yeah, 13 Clans. Spawn of Caine. These guys are harder to kill than most and can control minds. That's useful.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T05:34:46-07:00","id":1381291,"title":"","content":"I think a big thing that bothered me was the way they're using tech against vampires. <br /> Chaoscopes are fine. Thermal imaging is great though I believe vampires could use tech to get around it. <br /> <br /> But using the NSA to listen to phones and calls and stuff? It's more difficult to pick up on vampires than you'd think. Very little of vampire communication would reasonably have key words that would tip anyone off about vampires, and for the few that do, you could easily substitute a few words. It's not the prince, it's &quot;The Boss&quot; or &quot;Big P&quot; , Bloodhunt becomes &quot;They're out for your blood&quot; or &quot;They want your head&quot;, Elysium becomes &quot;The usual hangout&quot; or &quot;The Gig&quot; or something. It doesn't take a lot of imagination to wash the lexicon clean of incriminating vocabulary. <br /> <br /> I'm incredibly disapointed that they're not following the Technomancy route. It seemed like new and exciting rituals would be released to match technological advancement and further aid the masquerade. I can imagine very simple level 1 and 2 rituals confounding cameras, bugs, attempts to listen in to calls or read texts, wifi connections.... You can even joke that internet works perfectly all the time, and connection issues are entirely the work of vampires, mages and werewolves. <br /> <br /> A lot of squandered potential due to some shortsightedness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T08:28:59-07:00","id":1381328,"title":"","content":"There will always be a learning curve. As evidenced by some of the chat write ups, not everyone is completely concerned or 100% perfect about not using the code words. As the targets change their code words, the SI would be changing their algorithms to find them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24641-sarcasticjazzhands","name":"SarcasticJazzHands","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T08:57:16-07:00","id":1381334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381291#post1381291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a big thing that bothered me was the way they're using tech against vampires.<br /> Chaoscopes are fine. Thermal imaging is great though I believe vampires could use tech to get around it.<br /> <br /> But using the NSA to listen to phones and calls and stuff? It's more difficult to pick up on vampires than you'd think. Very little of vampire communication would reasonably have key words that would tip anyone off about vampires, and for the few that do, you could easily substitute a few words. It's not the prince, it's &quot;The Boss&quot; or &quot;Big P&quot; , Bloodhunt becomes &quot;They're out for your blood&quot; or &quot;They want your head&quot;, Elysium becomes &quot;The usual hangout&quot; or &quot;The Gig&quot; or something. It doesn't take a lot of imagination to wash the lexicon clean of incriminating vocabulary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the irony is that all of what you're describing is what is introduced AFTER the Second Inquisition. I.e they speak in mob speak NOW but didn't before.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm incredibly disapointed that they're not following the Technomancy route. It seemed like new and exciting rituals would be released to match technological advancement and further aid the masquerade. I can imagine very simple level 1 and 2 rituals confounding cameras, bugs, attempts to listen in to calls or read texts, wifi connections.... You can even joke that internet works perfectly all the time, and connection issues are entirely the work of vampires, mages and werewolves.<br /> <br /> A lot of squandered potential due to some shortsightedness. </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I'm curious if the Technocracy will exist in M20 or whether it's going to be destroyed and divided into factions. They seem to be playing with a lot of shakeups that way and M20 indicates the lower level Technocrats have discovered their leadership has all been eaten by the Nephandi.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be adverse to the Second Inquisition retconned as the people who killed Ravnos. I wouldn't mind if it was the Indian government working with Indian Hunters that dropped the bomb.<br /> <br /> It would explain why no one is particularly concerned about a nuke in the middle of a hurricane. Albeit, yes, I believe the Union could cover it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-14-2020, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T10:12:18-07:00","id":1381357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381334#post1381334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would explain why no one is particularly concerned about a nuke in the middle of a hurricane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Covering up a nuke in a populated area, with how big deal these things are to world goverments, it's the kind of things that really need &quot;a wizard did it&quot; to explain.<br /> <br /> There's no way a conspiration within alphabet agencies can cover *that* kind of ambiental catastrophe w/o literaly everyone with a sliver of power in the world being involved in the cover up (and, to be fair, even then it would be impossible. If everyone from Trump to the pope *was* in it, that just adds weak links to a chain that would inevitably break).<br /> <br /> It's easier to believe god-vampires and nuke-summoning wizards exist in the real life, and are being covered by the goverment, than to swallow that alphabet agencies can <b>nuke countries</b> w/o consequence. SI it's already straining belief with covering terrorist attacks on major cities, let's not put more strain on that camel by pretending they can do *that*, please.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-14-2020, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T10:28:33-07:00","id":1381362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381357#post1381357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Covering up a nuke in a populated area, with how big deal these things are to world goverments, it's the kind of things that really need &quot;a wizard did it&quot; to explain.<br /> <br /> There's no way a conspiration within alphabet agencies can cover *that* kind of ambiental catastrophe w/o literaly everyone with a sliver of power in the world being involved in the cover up (and, to be fair, even then it would be impossible. If everyone from Trump to the pope *was* in it, that just adds weak links to a chain that would inevitably break).<br /> <br /> It's easier to believe god-vampires and nuke-summoning wizards exist in the real life, and are being covered by the goverment, than to swallow that alphabet agencies can <b>nuke countries</b> w/o consequence. SI it's already straining belief with covering terrorist attacks on major cities, let's not put more strain on that camel by pretending they can do *that*, please.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, my argument would be India's government [which is nuclear capable] would do it with their vampire hunters.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition isn't limited to America's intelligence agencies.<br /> <br /> Each nation has their own variants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T11:09:56-07:00","id":1381377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381362#post1381362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each nation has their own variants.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an extreme viewpoint. There's a few rare nations where I'm on the fence; where corruption is minimal and enforcement agencies feel obligated to the people, I can imagine they'd go after vampires. In nations like the USA or Britain, The goverments are far too beholden to money, special interest groups, and the people are too invested in class hierarchies for a goverment institution to turn against vampires; Why bite the hand that feeds you, and how insanely hard would it be to organize resistance in a group that doesn't want to. But of course, a good deal of nations are even worse than that. As great as the inquisition might be in the country, I don't see an italian goverment stepping in to doing shit to vampires, they'd almost undoubtably side with the vampires (yep, that includes the so-called christian party) Let's not even get into... The Vast majority of nations; especially when you throw in the WoD filter. There are places in the world where average people trust organized crime more than they trust police. Whoever decided upon international vampire-hunting alphabet agencies is really ignorant of the ways of the world.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> think the irony is that all of what you're describing is what is introduced AFTER the Second Inquisition. I.e they speak in mob speak NOW but didn't before. </div> </div> </div>I don't imagine this is the case in all seriousness. I think it'd be common for elders to source people who are good with the technology they aren't, and I think many vampires would happily share suspect texts from their rivals with a sherrif or prince as proof of contempt for the masquerade, possibly leading to execution if the text was brazen enough. </span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T11:26:27-07:00","id":1381381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381334#post1381334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think the irony is that all of what you're describing is what is introduced AFTER the Second Inquisition. I.e they speak in mob speak NOW but didn't before.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We were doing this in Larp in 2000, before the whole NSA/MI5/bla-bla-bla were listening in. only truely dumb kindred would be using Masquerade threatening language. And to head off any &quot;elders don't get it&quot; talk, any of those elders wouldn't be using the tech to be able to make those kind of slip ups anyway. We had a little laugh a while ago, i texted the contact number of a Setite elder to try and arrange a meeting, the said &quot;ok, while i wait for her to commune with the Idol of Nokia and get back to me...&quot; If an elder barely understands a phone, they'll be getting someone else to do it for them who does, and they'll know enough about the Masquerade to not fuck up. If they didn't then the hunters would have risen within about a year of mobile phones getting popular...<br /> <br /> If there was widespread use of Kindred language as a justification of 2nd Inquisition, then that's just another idiot ball the setting has made the Kindred juggle","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T11:54:57-07:00","id":1381387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381362#post1381362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, my argument would be India's government [which is nuclear capable] would do it with their vampire hunters.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition isn't limited to America's intelligence agencies.<br /> <br /> Each nation has their own variants.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter which govement does it. It's impossible to cover up for this.<br /> <br /> 1\u00b0 You can't hide the fact that a major city it's now a Hiroshima-like nuclear wasteland w/o serious magic<br /> <br /> 2\u00b0 You would need the WHOLE power structure of India to be on it to even try such a cover up. Otherwise the *other* areas of the goverment that aren't *in the know* (army, justice, rescue people..wathever) would discover that it was a nuke. And in that case everyone knows about vampires, and it would leak. You can't keep the SI as a conspiration <i>within</i> the goverment if *everyone* knows<br /> <br /> You would need to admit, at least, that a nuke was lauched into the territory eventually. It's reason to go to <b>nuclear war</b>. It *will* topple the goverment if it's discovered that <i>they </i>did it. I find very hard to believe India can just nuke it's own people w/o consequence.<br /> <br /> SI cannot be at once omnipotent/omnipresent and yet a hidden section of the goverment that most don't know about. It's exactly that kind of nonsense what people complains about what they say the SI it's poorly written. Even you, when you ask yourself how this whole operation would keep being funded w/o people noticing...this is worse than that<br /> <br /> Even the Technocracy, with their magick, would be stetching belief if they pull such a massive, yet subtle, people manipulation: What they *could* do it's to help their subtle manipulations with some reality warping in the &quot;scene of the crime&quot; to make the nuke scenario seem less of an inevitable conclussion everyone with some knowledge will make before the army enters Bangladesh in full force. This is something humans simply can't do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-14-2020, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T12:06:21-07:00","id":1381389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381377#post1381377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's an extreme viewpoint. There's a few rare nations where I'm on the fence; where corruption is minimal and enforcement agencies feel obligated to the people, I can imagine they'd go after vampires. In nations like the USA or Britain, The goverments are far too beholden to money, special interest groups, and the people are too invested in class hierarchies for a goverment institution to turn against vampires;</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with this argument is you're describing why the government wouldn't destroy the Camarilla's High Clans when 90% of vampires don't have money and the Camarilla would want the Second Inquisition to wipe out those.<br /> <br /> Note: in-universe, the Camarilla separated from the Anarchs is suffering the least from the Second Inquisition.<br /> <br /> And the Camarilla's biggest mistake is the fact that they are using the Second Inquisition this way because a huge chunk of the Hunters are NOT cynical government spooks but fanatical religious zealots used and paid by them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T12:10:53-07:00","id":1381392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381387#post1381387\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't matter which govement does it. It's impossible to cover up for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking less nuclear explosion than, &quot;There was a huge explosion in this area. No it wasn't nuclear. That's silly.&quot;<br /> <br /> Mind you, you're acting like anyone is still alive in that region.<br /> <br /> The awakening of the Antediluvian killed everyone for a massive area around it and drove the rest gibbering insane. Wasn't it something like 2 million dead? At that point we're in &quot;Doctor Who ignores flying saucers crashing into Big Ben.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:39:33-07:00","id":1381426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381392#post1381392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was thinking less nuclear explosion than, &amp;quot;There was a huge explosion in this area. No it wasn't nuclear. That's silly.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>One could say the Indian government, or even the american government, deployed a MOAB strike in the region. Either via testing or an &quot;anti-terrorist strike&quot;. MOABs are basically nukes without the nuke. We've seen the devastation one can bring in 2017 when the US basically leveled a mountain and caused damage to buildings 1.5 miles away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T13:46:55-07:00","id":1381427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381389#post1381389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem with this argument is you're describing why the government wouldn't destroy the Camarilla's High Clans when 90% of vampires don't have money and the Camarilla would want the Second Inquisition to wipe out those.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>If &quot;Not having money&quot; means 2 to 4 dots of resources... Are you serious right now? You've been playing the game this long and you think 90% of vampires are poor? Unless you're taking Gangrel survivalism way too seriously or you're a delusional fool that wants humanity 10, only the freshest of fledglings don't have some kind of money source under their thumb. 10% of vampires are poor, the rest are loaded and don't work for a living. You are playing a parasite, it doesn't matter what sect you're in. Anarchs aren't socialist, they're libertarians. They don't like favours so much so often use millions of dollars for services instead. While you can't just dominate someone to give you their business, even the laziest and least competent of kindred can blood bond a weak mortal or two and mooch off them, living without discomfort. Even humble kindred, spending so little, can amass a good amount of wealth over time. And over their long lives they will be exposed to much better ways of making easy money without working, like currency manipulation, stock trading, or if they really don't want to learn anything good they can just become a landlord. Any vampire can easily become middle class, most can make it into being an elite. Now, yeah, you as a player might want to play with someone relatable (poor) or someone who actually works, but most neonates are going to pick up a few dots of finances or at least find a good retainer before they reach ancillae. <br /> There's no great reason for the SI to pick on the middle class. The WoD alphabet organizations should cement the hierarchy of society, not attack it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T14:10:50-07:00","id":1381434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381291#post1381291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a big thing that bothered me was the way they're using tech against vampires.<br /> Chaoscopes are fine. Thermal imaging is great though I believe vampires could use tech to get around it.<br /> <br /> But using the NSA to listen to phones and calls and stuff? It's more difficult to pick up on vampires than you'd think. Very little of vampire communication would reasonably have key words that would tip anyone off about vampires, and for the few that do, you could easily substitute a few words. It's not the prince, it's &quot;The Boss&quot; or &quot;Big P&quot; , Bloodhunt becomes &quot;They're out for your blood&quot; or &quot;They want your head&quot;, Elysium becomes &quot;The usual hangout&quot; or &quot;The Gig&quot; or something. It doesn't take a lot of imagination to wash the lexicon clean of incriminating vocabulary.<br /> <br /> I'm incredibly disapointed that they're not following the Technomancy route. It seemed like new and exciting rituals would be released to match technological advancement and further aid the masquerade. I can imagine very simple level 1 and 2 rituals confounding cameras, bugs, attempts to listen in to calls or read texts, wifi connections.... You can even joke that internet works perfectly all the time, and connection issues are entirely the work of vampires, mages and werewolves.<br /> <br /> A lot of squandered potential due to some shortsightedness.</div> </div> </div> </div>For once, I actually agree with you. I don't think vampires would get caught because they're saying overtly Masquerade-breaching things, most of the time; I find it more likely that hunters dug through activity records for a particular city (London perhaps? I haven't actually read FoL, I don't know how they handled that), discovered a bunch of cell phones only used between sunset and sunrise, and used cell tower data to find the location of Elysium. It was a bloodbath, with heavy losses on both sides; some parts of the Camarilla then declared a blanket ban on cell phones to avoid that happening again, which doesn't really work and isn't really enforceable but that's nothing new (look at how well mortal lawmakers tend to understand tech issues).<br /> <br /> Hopefully the planned SI book will come out at some point with a canon explanation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T14:31:48-07:00","id":1381437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381427#post1381427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If &quot;Not having money&quot; means 2 to 4 dots of resources... Are you serious right now? You've been playing the game this long and you think 90% of vampires are poor? Unless you're taking Gangrel survivalism way too seriously or you're a delusional fool that wants humanity 10, only the freshest of fledglings don't have some kind of money source under their thumb. 10% of vampires are poor, the rest are loaded and don't work for a living. You are playing a parasite, it doesn't matter what sect you're in. Anarchs aren't socialist, they're libertarians. They don't like favours so much so often use millions of dollars for services instead. While you can't just dominate someone to give you their business, even the laziest and least competent of kindred can blood bond a weak mortal or two and mooch off them, living without discomfort. Even humble kindred, spending so little, can amass a good amount of wealth over time. And over their long lives they will be exposed to much better ways of making easy money without working, like currency manipulation, stock trading, or if they really don't want to learn anything good they can just become a landlord. Any vampire can easily become middle class, most can make it into being an elite. Now, yeah, you as a player might want to play with someone relatable (poor) or someone who actually works, but most neonates are going to pick up a few dots of finances or at least find a good retainer before they reach ancillae.<br /> There's no great reason for the SI to pick on the middle class. The WoD alphabet organizations should cement the hierarchy of society, not attack it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only a few vampires are rich, that's kind of the point of the Anarch vs. Camarilla conflict. Using Chicago by Night demographics, only a small handful of vampires have pull and wealth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no great reason for the SI to pick on the middle class. The WoD alphabet organizations should cement the hierarchy of society, not attack it. </div> </div> </div>They'd pick on them because they're a bunch of dangerous fanatics and xenophobes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T14:49:01-07:00","id":1381444,"title":"","content":"We're also forgetting the fact that the reason the first inquisition happened was because elder kindred started using well trained mortals to hunt and kill their kindred enemies during the day. It backfired. The Second inquisition was the same exact thing but only worse. Ancients and elders using members of human governments to send in task forces and drone strikes all over the world to remove the sabbat. that attack on the sabbat cities was because kindred fueled the inquisition's knowledge on how best to attack them and only land strikes in their weak points. Which is what they did and after they realized that the people who hired them, shared alot of similar qualities. The V5 camarilla book even hints to the destruction of tremere chantry was because of the Banu Haqim. Their elders scoped it out for decades if not longer and then leaked the info that blook sucking monsters lived there, and here's the way in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26094-thatoneguy","name":"ThatOneGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-14T15:34:40-07:00","id":1381455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381434#post1381434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For once, I actually agree with you. I don't think vampires would get caught because they're saying overtly Masquerade-breaching things, most of the time; I find it more likely that hunters dug through activity records for a particular city (London perhaps? I haven't actually read FoL, I don't know how they handled that), discovered a bunch of cell phones only used between sunset and sunrise, and used cell tower data to find the location of Elysium. It was a bloodbath, with heavy losses on both sides; some parts of the Camarilla then declared a blanket ban on cell phones to avoid that happening again, which doesn't really work and isn't really enforceable but that's nothing new (look at how well mortal lawmakers tend to understand tech issues).<br /> <br /> Hopefully the planned SI book will come out at some point with a canon explanation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would agree with you on the phone thing, if the fiction actually didn't have vampires talking about vampire shit on the phone, in emails, etc. all the time. If that wasn't a thing in almost every bit of vampire fiction from the WoD, I might buy that. But it's not. It's a logical extrapolation of what would be done, based on what has been written before.<br /> <br /> for. In real life we have government spooks that spend their days looking through phones, emails, etc. for terrorist information. This is no different. And once the SI had identified things, it's not hard to feed some of that into the various organzations the SI agents truly work for, covering it with various terrorism-related falsehoods about the word salad, and get all that added to the terrorist threat assessments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:07:43-07:00","id":1381581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381437#post1381437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only a few vampires are rich, that's kind of the point of the Anarch vs. Camarilla conflict. Using Chicago by Night demographics, only a small handful of vampires have pull and wealth.</div> </div> </div> </div> I raise to your Chicago by night and give you <i>Bloodlines</i>. Checkmate, athiest.<br /> <br /> Really, I had a long ass post, but it disappeared on me, so I'll give you the abridged version.<br /> <br /> I love myself some class conflict, I love rich vs poor stories, but that's not realistic when dealing with vampires. Your average anarch isn't a communist, they're a libertarian. They have the money, they just don't have the influence as they're competing in a two party system against conservatives and neoliberals. (or Theocrats and Monarchists). The class conflict is more like '4 dots of resources VS 6 dots of resources&quot; or, in keeping with the Libertarian theme &quot;<i>Against the Cam, A Four or Five dot resources-Anarch embraces childer, indoctrinates them into hating the Authority of the Cam, equips them, and sends them into &quot;battle&quot;. Should they survive and he takes a liking to them, he may gift them a financial asset</i>&quot;.<br /> <br /> The issue isn't money, it's influence. Money is easy for kindred, but if you're competing, influence is hard. A city where Anarchs are in control is fine, a city with the Cam? Hmm, Yeah, that might be difficult. Ordinarily, Anarchs, besides the fledglings and those that are just adverse to money, are rich enough to have some soft status and are typically the targets that government organizations would turn a blind eye to. Just not-being-poor gives anarchs some leeway; If Anarchs had kids who did drugs they wouldn't be 'junkies' they'd be 'troubled'. It's only when the camarilla uses their influence against the anarchs that big hunter groups might actually go after them, but as said previously, I think Vampires overwhelmingly prefer to push smaller hunter organizations and religious nutters and don't want to tangle with the government monoliths.<br /> <br /> Yeah,this is way messier than what I had before, but let's continue.<br /> It's really easy for vampires to make money. I'll say it again; I love the themes of rich vs poor, but Vampires aren't the 99%. They're literally the 0.001%. With what vampires have, they can only be poor by choice or extremely unfortunate in terms of supernatural curses. The Poor characters in <i>Bloodlines</i> are the thinbloods, the serial killer, the gargoyle, relatively speaking maybe the folks in the last round just live comfortably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:15:53-07:00","id":1381584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381581#post1381581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I raise to your Chicago by night and give you <i>Bloodlines</i>. Checkmate, athiest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whose an atheist?<br /> <br /> Rich Vampires: Isaac Abrams, Sebastian La Croix, Strauss, Graut, Therese, Octavio Giovanni, Ash, Vivi [questionably], Andrei<br /> <br /> Poor Vampires: Skelter, Nines, Damsel, The Nosferatu living under Hollywood, Jeanette, The Thin Bloods, Smiling Jack, The Shovelheads<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love myself some class conflict, I love rich vs poor stories, but that's not realistic when dealing with vampires. Your average anarch isn't a communist, they're a libertarian. They have the money, they just don't have the influence as they're competing in a two party system against conservatives and neoliberals. (or Theocrats and Monarchists). The class conflict is more like '4 dots of resources VS 6 dots of resources&quot; or, in keeping with the Libertarian theme &quot;<i>Against the Cam, A Four or Five dot resources-Anarch embraces childer, indoctrinates them into hating the Authority of the Cam, equips them, and sends them into &quot;battle&quot;. Should they survive and he takes a liking to them, he may gift them a financial asset</i>&quot; </div> </div> </div>Going again with Bloodlines as an example, the Thin Bloods on the beach of Santa Monica are not only penniless but homeless. Lily, E, Rosa, and that crazy guy muttering to himself are people living in terror of being killed by the system that they barely understand. The Anarchs are living working class existences in a bar that doesn't show any signs of wealth and power. Isaac Abrams certainly has both as a Hollywood mogul but he and Therese are exceptions not the rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The issue isn't money, it's influence. Money is easy for kindred, but if you're competing, influence is hard. A city where Anarchs are in control is fine, a city with the Cam? Hmm, Yeah, that might be difficult. Ordinarily, Anarchs, besides the fledglings and those that are just adverse to money, are rich enough to have some soft status and are typically the targets that government organizations would turn a blind eye to. Just not-being-poor gives anarchs some leeway; If Anarchs had kids who did drugs they wouldn't be 'junkies' they'd be 'troubled'. It's only when the camarilla uses their influence against the anarchs that big hunter groups might actually go after them, but as said previously, I think Vampires overwhelmingly prefer to push smaller hunter organizations and religious nutters and don't want to tangle with the government monoliths. </div> </div> </div>Uh huh, may I ask where you got the impression of the anarchs as rich vampires? Their inspirations are NEAR DARK and THE LOST BOYS of which are as far from aristocrat rich vampires as possible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah,this is way messier than what I had before, but let's continue. It's really easy for vampires to make money. I'll say it again; I love the themes of rich vs poor, but Vampires aren't the 99%. They're literally the 0.001%. With what vampires have, they can only be poor by choice or extremely unfortunate in terms of supernatural curses. The Poor characters in <i>Bloodlines</i> are the thinbloods, the serial killer, the gargoyle, relatively speaking maybe nines </div> </div> </div>Vampires with Presence and Dominate can make a lot of money very rapidly. As can someone who ghouls someone. However, if you're not going to use ghouldom to enslave someone, you're not going to be rich, which is a large chunk of Anarchs. Not everyone has the Toreador, Tremere, or Ventrue power set either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:34:22-07:00","id":1381589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381584#post1381584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Uh huh, may I ask where you got the impression of the anarchs as rich vampires? Their inspirations are NEAR DARK and THE LOST BOYS of which are as far from aristocrat rich vampires as possible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Vampires with Presence and Dominate can make a lot of money very rapidly. As can someone who ghouls someone. However, if you're not going to use ghouldom to enslave someone, you're not going to be rich, which is a large chunk of Anarchs. Not everyone has the Toreador, Tremere, or Ventrue power set either.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are blantently Sabbat, not Anarchs.<br /> <br /> But, yeah, i kind of agree, only Kindred who don't want money won't have it. Which makes it all the more puzzling. The vast majority of people like having money, it makes their life more comfortable, easier, why would Kindred be any different. In the world of Darkness, really, Kindred should be more willing to take what they need.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T03:54:15-07:00","id":1381596,"title":"","content":"The Anarchs conflict with the Camarilla has nothing to do with class or money. Its simply they want to oust the Camarilla until its nothing but Final Death ash. Never have I heard class was the reason they wanted to have conflict with the Camarilla. Also the Thin-Bloods in bloodlines were factionless, they had nothing to do with the Anarchs.They would be dead weight. Also speaking of Bloodlines <a href=\"https://vtmb.fandom.com/wiki/Isaac_Abrams\" target=\"_blank\">Isaac Abramas</a> wasn't hurting for at all for cash and he was literally the Baron of Hollywood. Its actually nonsensical to think the Anarchs who politic themselves to Baron status would be poor resourceless Kindred anyway.<br /> <br /> Another thing- just because the Anarchs had one of their main bases in an old Bar doesn't mean all the members were poor at all. The mere fact that they <b>own</b> a Bar property in California pretty much relates to them not hurting for cash. Even with this all said in done Vampires as an almost principle have extensive black market trade networks across Sect lines. Only the most secluded Gangrel from the mortal economy is without cash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 04-15-2020, 06:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T06:46:53-07:00","id":1381634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381392#post1381392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking less nuclear explosion than, &quot;There was a huge explosion in this area. No it wasn't nuclear. That's silly.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You were thinking to retcon <i>the nuking itself</i>, or you think that's a good explanation for the whole place being transformed into a nuclear wasteland? Because these are two very different scenarios.<br /> <br /> If nukes obliterating the area weren't used to stop the Ante, then <i>maybe </i>it could be easier to hide the fact. It all depends on how it's done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mind you, you're acting like anyone is still alive in that region. </div> </div> </div>If New York City disappears in a big explosion, there would be no one left alive in that region either. Still it would be kind of a big deal, don't you think?<br /> <br /> The people left alive there doesn't matter as much as the people elsewhere that may care about the fact. That there's none with that body count it's 2ed &quot;Sabbat makes cities disappear&quot; levels of silly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The awakening of the Antediluvian killed everyone for a massive area around it and drove the rest gibbering insane. Wasn't it something like 2 million dead? At that point we're in &quot;Doctor Who ignores flying saucers crashing into Big Ben.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Not saying that's not the case, but &quot;two wrongs don't make a right&quot; it's starting to become the moto of V5 criticism.<br /> <br /> &quot;A wizard did it&quot; may be a lazy narrative, but it's less lazy than having no explanation at all. At least during the fact there was an impossible climatic effect impeding anyone to reach into the area, and after the fact we can presume other magics were used to hide the fact.<br /> <br /> Forcing the SI, that it's supposed to be &quot;badass normal&quot; with mostly human capabilities, into this already crazy shit *<i>as it is</i>*...would be making no favors to the SI image.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 04-15-2020, 09:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T07:37:51-07:00","id":1381645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381589#post1381589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those are blantently Sabbat, not Anarchs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that they're the inspiration for the Anarchs according to Mark Rein Hagen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But, yeah, i kind of agree, only Kindred who don't want money won't have it. Which makes it all the more puzzling. The vast majority of people like having money, it makes their life more comfortable, easier, why would Kindred be any different. In the world of Darkness, really, Kindred should be more willing to take what they need. </div> </div> </div>Yes, which is why everyone in the world is a drug dealer or slaver. That doesn't track at all.<br /> <br /> That's a very, &quot;The poor don't have money because they're lazy&quot; argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381596#post1381596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Anarchs conflict with the Camarilla has nothing to do with class or money. Its simply they want to oust the Camarilla until its nothing but Final Death ash.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read GUIDE TO THE ANARCHS or ANARCHS UNBOUND. The reason Anarchs hate the Camarilla is because they lack domain and the ability to sire. Also general oppression.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Never have I heard class was the reason they wanted to have conflict with the Camarilla. Also the Thin-Bloods in bloodlines were factionless, they had nothing to do with the Anarchs. </div> </div> </div>The question is whether any vampires in Bloodlines were poor not rich.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They would be dead weight. Also speaking of Bloodlines <a href=\"https://vtmb.fandom.com/wiki/Isaac_Abrams\" target=\"_blank\">Isaac Abramas</a> wasn't hurting for at all for cash and he was literally the Baron of Hollywood. Its actually nonsensical to think the Anarchs who politic themselves to Baron status would be poor resourceless Kindred anyway. </div> </div> </div>The question is whether any vampires in Bloodlines were poor not rich.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Another thing- just because the Anarchs had one of their main bases in an old Bar doesn't mean all the members were poor at all. The mere fact that they <b>own</b> a Bar property in California pretty much relates to them not hurting for cash. Even with this all said in done Vampires as an almost principle have extensive black market trade networks across Sect lines. Only the most secluded Gangrel from the mortal economy is without cash. </div> </div> </div>That is explictly not the case given there's a Resources background that vampires don't automatically have dots in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2020, 10:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T09:26:03-07:00","id":1381665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381645#post1381645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that they're the inspiration for the Anarchs according to Mark Rein Hagen.</div> </div> </div> </div>... I'm sorry, what? The Anarchs are meant to be roving packs of mass murderers?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381645#post1381645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, which is why everyone in the world is a drug dealer or slaver. That doesn't track at all.<br /> <br /> That's a very, &quot;The poor don't have money because they're lazy&quot; argument.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If all you have to do is feed someone some blood, then yes, if they're poor, then it's through their own choice.<br /> <br /> It's like having actual money in your veins and complaining that it's too much effort to prick your finger.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T09:53:57-07:00","id":1381672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jamiemalk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381665#post1381665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... I'm sorry, what? The Anarchs are meant to be roving packs of mass murderers?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same way that Toreador are meant to be murderers like Lestat and Ventrue are meant to be Dracula-esque mannered murderers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If all you have to do is feed someone some blood, then yes, if they're poor, then it's through their own choice. </div> </div> </div>Leaving them an addicted braindead shell of a human being.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's like having actual money in your veins and complaining that it's too much effort to prick your finger. </div> </div> </div>It depends on what you think slavery and theft is justified by. Turning a rich person into a ghoul is an easy way of making money but any person who does it will see that person rapidly degenerate. Also, making a person into a ghoul is sometimes forbidden by a Prince unless that person is part of your domain (domain being what Anarchs are chiefly fighting over) or owned by another Kindred. Sometimes ghouls are things Princes demand permission to create as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2020, 12:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:03:51-07:00","id":1381675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381584#post1381584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rich Vampires: Isaac Abrams, Sebastian La Croix, Strauss, Graut, Therese, Octavio Giovanni, Ash, Vivi [questionably], Andrei<br /> <br /> Poor Vampires: Skelter, Nines, Damsel, The Nosferatu living under Hollywood, Jeanette, The Thin Bloods, Smiling Jack, The Shovelheads<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>You really didn't look into this much, did you? This is more a list of obviously rich vampires versus vampires who aren't displaying their wealth. Let's try this again. <br /> <br /> Rich Vampires. <br /> Isaac Abrams, Sebastian La Croix, Strauss, Graut, Therese <i>and </i>Jeanette, Octavio Giovanni, Ash, Vivi, Andrei, Smiling jack, The Nosferatu except for maybe Imalia, The brotherhood of the Ninth circle, Pisha (she'd need quite the contact network) Presumably the other primogen. Becket. <br /> <br /> Comfortable/Questionable: <br /> Skelter (guy knows how to manage things, probably a petty bourgiouse, I'd guess 2-3 resources) , Nines (Too class concious, wouldn't be surprised if he was voluntarily poor, but he does have expensive equipment) Damsel (Acts like she's never been poor, does she own the LR?) Imalia (as a cleopatra, she lacks a good connection to the clan and marketable skills, but she can give you spy cams so...) The Reeve and the Sherrif. <br /> <br /> Poverty Vampires<br /> The Gargoyle, The thin bloods, the shovelheads. The Serial killer (presumably) <br /> <br /> We know absolutely nothing about the folks who come after you during the bloodhunt/endgame. The shovelheads as fledglings are too fresh to really be put into consideration. But, rough count for a conservative estimate:<br /> <br /> <b>Rich</b>:18<br /> <b>Comfortable</b>: 7+ A lot of unammed characters (However many additional Nosferatu/Tremere you think are hiding under holywood/In the chantry? They would be at <i>least </i>comfortable and well protected by elders. (This count of 7 is assuming that in groups like the 9thC and the underground nos, there's one rich person buying the expensive things for others, rather than them all being wealthy, which isn't so realistic) <br /> <b>Poverty</b>- Six (Not counting fledglings) and I remind you; Four of these are thinbloods, they shouldn't count. They're not real vampires and can't even ghoul. The Gargoyle has a curse or two to blame, it's only the serial killer who is actually a normal vampire and yet remains in poverty. <br /> <br /> I would guess it's even more lopsided than that. But even if we discuss whether we count 3 dots of resources as 'rich' or just comfortable, it doesn't really matter; People with three dots of resources aren't generally looking for economic class conflict. Having three dots of resources is enough to put you in the top 20% of income earning, and a vampire can have two dots of resources easily without really working. It doesn't matter if they have 1 dot of resources or 8, most vampires aren't labouring, they just own stuff. They have no right to an economic class conflict because they're all in the class of owners. <br /> <br /> Most vampires are rich, the rare ones that aren't usually have friends that are. What matters is influence, and money only doesn't buy influence when someone's either outbidding you or you're against a favoured customer. But the point being, unless another vampire is actively trying to screw you and direct bad things your way, you are part of the protected class and the goverment has no interest in coming down on you. When a poor kid does drugs, he's a junkie sent to prison. When a rich kid does drugs, he's 'Troubled' and let off. When a poor pedaphile is accused, his face goes everywhere and he's beaten to death in prison. When a rich pedophile is accused, it's 'slander' and a lawsuit occurs for damages. If a rich person murders someone, it doesn't matter if they drained the blood or not: Justice seeks to condemn the poor and enable the rich, moreso in the world of Darkness. Vampires take prestation so seriously because that's how elites in real world society actually work. The Heads of the Alphabet agents are thinking &quot;If I don't hunt them, I'll get favours from them&quot; (But also they'll destroy my family if I actually do hunt them so...) and that goes for Anarchs as well as Camarilla (not that the alphabet agents can really tell the difference)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:05:20-07:00","id":1381678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381675#post1381675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You really didn't look into this much, did you? This is more a list of obviously rich vampires versus vampires who aren't displaying their wealth. Let's try this again.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> No it's not.<br /> <br /> Large portions of vampires are poor, which is part of the game's premise. The first campaign is in Gary, Indiana after all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:13:35-07:00","id":1381684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381672#post1381672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The same way that Toreador are meant to be murderers like Lestat and Ventrue are meant to be Dracula-esque mannered murderers.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, i've never gotten that impression from any of the books. Those are Antitribu, and why the Sabbat was a thing, from a meta perspective<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381672#post1381672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leaving them an addicted braindead shell of a human being.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure where you're getting braindead from, unless you're talking about conditioning them into being useless. If that was the only thing that Ghouling did, it would be less than pointless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381672#post1381672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depends on what you think slavery and theft is justified by. Turning a rich person into a ghoul is an easy way of making money but any person who does it will see that person rapidly degenerate. Also, making a person into a ghoul is sometimes forbidden by a Prince unless that person is part of your domain (domain being what Anarchs are chiefly fighting over) or owned by another Kindred. Sometimes ghouls are things Princes demand permission to create as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, now you're describing the insanely stupid kinds of princes that you seem to think are commonplace. Princes that want useful and competent subjects don't do that, or the Kindred would just leave. Also would require an insane amount of surveillance or mandatory telepathy and dominate sessions for everyone who came to elysium. Getting a ghoul, &quot;off the books&quot; is also really easy, just go somewhere that isn't someones claimed domain.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Prone to being a Classic Curmudgeon, goshdarned whippersnappers...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1037-jamiemalk","name":"jamiemalk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1037_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:20:56-07:00","id":1381689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381678#post1381678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Large portions of vampires are poor, which is part of the game's premise. The first campaign is in Gary, Indiana after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like preconcieved notions of yours are really colouring your perspecitve. You've listed the same malk in both rich and poor sections of your list, Vivi isn't really debatable when her holdings are 4-dot territory. You've also listed the game's nosferatu as poor, which is hilarious. The vast majority of named vampires in Bloodlines possess between 3 and five dots of resources. Moving on from Bloodlines... How rich are you in real life? What do you consider poor? If you keep your players constantly moving with a narrative driven game I guess it's conceivable that players who want money don't end up gaining more than 2 dots of resources, but if they actually want money, you'd have to either beat them down with unreasonably unyielding domain restrictions or houserule them to death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:27:54-07:00","id":1381691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381689#post1381689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like preconcieved notions of yours are really colouring your perspecitve. You've listed the same malk in both rich and poor sections of your list, Vivi isn't really debatable when her holdings are 4-dot territory. You've also listed the game's nosferatu as poor, which is hilarious. The vast majority of named vampires in Bloodlines possess between 3 and five dots of resources. Moving on from Bloodlines... How rich are you in real life? What do you consider poor? If you keep your players constantly moving with a narrative driven game I guess it's conceivable that players who want money don't end up gaining more than 2 dots of resources, but if they actually want money, you'd have to either beat them down with unreasonably unyielding domain restrictions or houserule them to death.</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Uh, yes, because Jeanette doesn't have access to the resources that Therese has.<br /> <br /> 2. It depends on how much money you think a decent strip club makes.<br /> <br /> 3. Yes, Nosferatu don't have Resources. They live underground and squat.<br /> <br /> 4. I strongly disagree.<br /> <br /> For me, vampire is a game about playing urban predators and some of those are going to live in condemned buildings and ratty apartments while others live in skyscrapers.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://lparchive.org/Vampire-The-Masquerade-Bloodlines-(by-gatz-and-TheMcD)/Update%2004/2-ibRunt0ZR7ucK.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:58:05-07:00","id":1381704,"title":"","content":"1. If a socialite does no work but has an exceedingly rich spouse and lives in a mansion, are they poor? <br /> 2. I uhh... Did research on this for a game. If someone of VV's league dances, that'd make 3 dots of resources on it's own. The place appears to be popular, It's a cash business and good for laundering money, only overheads can really drag the place down. <br /> 3.And yet, all those nosferatu computers, all that up to date tech, all those wide networks of informants, all that snooping, oh, and all that unreasonable sewer level with giant gates. <br /> Nosferatu have the money, they just choose not to live in palaces. <br /> 4. Elaborate please. The facts point to one thing and your feelings point to another. Hardly an argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T10:59:40-07:00","id":1381705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381704#post1381704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. If a socialite does no work but has an exceedingly rich spouse and lives in a mansion, are they poor?<br /> 2. I uhh... Did research on this for a game. If someone of VV's league dances, that'd make 3 dots of resources on it's own. The place appears to be popular, It's a cash business and good for laundering money, only overheads can really drag the place down.<br /> 3.And yet, all those nosferatu computers, all that up to date tech, all those wide networks of informants, all that snooping, oh, and all that unreasonable sewer level with giant gates.<br /> Nosferatu have the money, they just choose not to live in palaces.<br /> 4. Elaborate please. The facts point to one thing and your feelings point to another. Hardly an argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Nosferatu stealing internet and devices while squatting in the sewers is a cool lair but I don't see that as a way to have vast influence as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T12:23:54-07:00","id":1381732,"title":"","content":"Hogwash. <br /> They've got the details to all your accounts, evidence of your secrets, they own businesses on the sly, A million politicians know them by ten million faces. You honestly believe this clan poor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T14:07:20-07:00","id":1381762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381732#post1381732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hogwash. <br /> They've got the details to all your accounts, evidence of your secrets, they own businesses on the sly, A million politicians know them by ten million faces. You honestly believe this clan poor?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Tech is not cheap.<br /> <br /> And they will become even richer considering that they no longer need to hide inside the sewers as now by the rules they are not required to be fugly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24832,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","user":"blailton","date":". 04-15-2020, 06:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T15:13:30-07:00","id":1381775,"title":"","content":"And this why I still believe the Anarchs are a basic faction compared to the Sabbat if we take CTPhipps take on &quot;what the Anarchs&quot; are. Their reasoning for conflict against the Camarilla is just ultimately stupid and temporal. If the fight between the Anarchs and Camarilla is just about finances then its a pure garbage faction, there is no reason why it should've been raised from underdog middle-man to the forefront of the setting compared to the Camarilla and Sabbat. The Sabbat actually have a more interesting reason for conflict against the Camarilla, it also isn't about petty things mortals would worry about long past their undead ages already. There is really no justification for the reason the Anarchs to become a main faction, but again, there reasonings for conflict isn't compelling for the setting. <br /> <br /> Sabbat and Camarilla were the perfect dualistic extremes duking it out on the effect of Vampirism should be handled. Anarchs are just uppity babies who want to fight the Camarilla just 'cuz (maybe because the Anarchs are red while the Camarilla is blue? idk lol).<br /> <br /> And to even take your arguments seriously (which is admittedly hard), Anarchs obviously aren't poor at all. If they were, they would've never have survived against the Camarilla long enough at all. Class warfare shouldn't be a main stay theme of VTM and its why it is worsening. VTM is about supernatural bloodsucking entities that are virtually immortal, human political ideologues shouldn't be a focus. Money is just a backdrop for the undead parasites to continue on their unlife.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T15:28:00-07:00","id":1381779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381775#post1381775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this why I still believe the Anarchs are a basic faction compared to the Sabbat if we take CTPhipps take on &quot;what the Anarchs&quot; are. Their reasoning for conflict against the Camarilla is just ultimately stupid and temporal. If the fight between the Anarchs and Camarilla is just about finances then its a pure garbage faction, there is no reason why it should've been raised from underdog middle-man to the forefront of the setting compared to the Camarilla and Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for running me down and my opinion on what makes a good game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Sabbat actually have a more interesting reason for conflict against the Camarilla, it also isn't about petty things mortals would worry about long past their undead ages already. There is really no justification for the reason the Anarchs to become a main faction, but again, there reasonings for conflict isn't compelling for the setting. </div> </div> </div>The Sabbat's motivation for fighting the Camarilla is the same one as the Anarchs: domain and resources. The whole idea they're fighting for any other reason is a trick of the Elders. The shovelheads and Neonates are used by the Elders as cannon fodder to see who can control the most.<br /> <br /> You don't actually believe the Sabbat and Camarilla are DIFFERENT do you? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Mind you, it's partially why I accepted the Lasombra defection because I've never thought the Lasombra actually BELIEVED in the religion they taught the Neonates and were horrified by the Gehenna Crusade because it was the &quot;let's all drink the Kool-Aid&quot; moment that made them realize they'd lost control of their cult and possibly were, even worse, teaching about something REAL.<br /> <br /> It's how I differentiate the Lasombra and Followers of Set really. The Followers of Set BELIEVE while the Lasombra have always viewed Noddism as an opiate of the masses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sabbat and Camarilla were the perfect dualistic extremes duking it out on the effect of Vampirism should be handled. Anarchs are just uppity babies who want to fight the Camarilla just 'cuz (maybe because the Anarchs are red while the Camarilla is blue? idk lol). </div> </div> </div>They're dualistic in the sense of being the exact same coin.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to even take your arguments seriously (which is admittedly hard), Anarchs obviously aren't poor at all. If they were, they would've never have survived against the Camarilla long enough at all. Class warfare shouldn't be a main stay theme of VTM and its why it is worsening. VTM is about supernatural bloodsucking entities that are virtually immortal, human political ideologues shouldn't be a focus. Money is just a backdrop for the undead parasites to continue on their unlife. </div> </div> </div>It's not financial resources, though the Anarchs are clearly the underdogs there, it's Domain which is a far more important thing.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2019/06/the-social-satire-of-vampire-masquerade.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://unitedfederationofcharles.blo...asquerade.html</a><br /> <br /> Here's an essay I wrote on the Social Satire of Vampire: The Masquerade, though if you want to read it.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if you want the Anarchs to be a group that isn't a boots on the ground conflict of the poor and disenfranchised against the rich and powerful then MAYBE you aren't someone who should be playing the Anarchs vs. the Camarilla. The Anarchs are always revolutionaries of the peasant class (with the occassional defector ala Louis Fortier) fighting the landowning rulership class. This is why the Anarchs have been always on the backfoot in their conflict against the Camarilla as they control domain, influence, herds, and mortal allies to a far greater extent than the Anarchs. The ones who have abandoned themselves to the Beast and corruption are the Sabbat and of course they're now identical as an exploitative corrupt sect that misuses its young and sends them on suicide missions exactly like their Elders in the Dark Ages: they have become what the Anarchs once fought.<br /> <br /> That is the interesting part of the Anarchs in the fact that they can maybe make progress against the Camarilla by becoming more vicious, more evil, and exploiting mortals as weapons against the Ivory Tower as well as the Black Hand but they run the risk of becoming exactly what they hate. V5 promises the Anarchs will gain great power as well as influence by taking in Elders of the Gangrel and Brujah plus the Ministry but the former Followers of Set will almost certainly warp their interior ideology to something darker as well a more malevolent. Is it possible the Anarchs will be turned into the Sabbat 2.0?<br /> <br /> Yes, that's a real possibility. It's a tragedy V5 has set up as the old Sabbat is collapsing while a new one is emerging from the idealists fighting against an evil empire. These sort of full circle revolutions are a mainstay of history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2020, 06:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T15:34:50-07:00","id":1381780,"title":"","content":"Or, in simpler terms, the Sabbat ARE Anarchs. They're just the ones who have become what they once despised.<br /> <br /> The other Anarchs became Camarilla sellouts.<br /> <br /> Because tragedy.<br /> <br /> Now are the Anarchs going to do a repeat of history?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T15:36:13-07:00","id":1381781,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat are ludicrously different from the Camarilla, what do you mean? One group literally accepts and revels in their vampirism, while one understands their condition but tries to level it off abiding by human viewpoints and morality (even at the cost of it degrading as they age further and further). They literally are specifically written as far apart from eachother as possible, unlike the Anarchs who just Camarilla-lite with a few steps taken out the way- they are the different side of the coin for the Camarilla. Obviously the Sabbat and Camarilla fight for domain/resources, but thats only a backdrop for their real motivations of supernatural conflict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T15:38:52-07:00","id":1381782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381781#post1381781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sabbat are ludicrously different from the Camarilla, what do you mean? One group literally accepts and revels in their vampirism, while one understands their condition but tries to level it off abiding by human viewpoints and morality (even at the cost of it degrading as they age further and further). They literally are specifically written as far apart from eachother as possible, unlike the Anarchs who just Camarilla-lite with a few steps taken out the way- they are the different side of the coin for the Camarilla.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Camarilla's Elders are every bit as inhuman and evil as the Sabbat's elders. They only pretend to be human. It's even a joke in the game that 90% of the Sabbat's titles are just different names for the Camarilla's equivalent. The big difference?<br /> <br /> The Sabbat: Well we follow all the same Traditions but we WOULDN'T if not for the Camarilla holding us back. Until then, we hold the Masquerade because of those jerks.<br /> <br /> Gross hypocrisy.<br /> <br /> Mind you, part of what I love about the setting is the fact Barons are just Princes and they're forming into the exact same patterm. Anarchs struggle to make a real change and are unable to escape the trap their predecessors in the First Anarch Revolt fell into.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Obviously the Sabbat and Camarilla fight for domain/resources, but thats only a backdrop for their real motivations of supernatural conflict. </div> </div> </div>See, I see the exact opposite. Very few Sabbat leaders actually believe in the apocalypse. It's all a scam to increase their own power and keep the neonates in line.<br /> <br /> The War of Ages, Anarch vs. Elder, is the central conflict.<br /> <br /> It's just that you don't even have to be an Anarch to fight it. It's in every sect and every level of their society.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-15-2020, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T15:52:32-07:00","id":1381786,"title":"","content":"Mind you, it might be different at your table.<br /> <br /> There's a million individual canons.<br /> <br /> What works for me may not work for you.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T18:46:10-07:00","id":1381842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blailton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381762#post1381762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Yes. Tech is not cheap.<br /> <br /> And they will become even richer considering that they no longer need to hide inside the sewers as now by the rules they are not required to be fugly.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> THey are still required to be fugly. They have to take a required Flaw that represents it and take social penalties because of it. They just aren't 'OH GOD THAT IS A VAMPIRE OR SOMETHING OBVIOUSLY SUPERNATURAL'.<br /> <br /> But nice hyperbole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-15T22:11:17-07:00","id":1381859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381779#post1381779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's how I differentiate the Lasombra and Followers of Set really. The Followers of Set BELIEVE while the Lasombra have always viewed Noddism as an opiate of the masses.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't differentiate them by their wildly different belief systems and philosophies, but instead by how cynical they are? I feel this thread has become a real eye opener.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not financial resources, though the Anarchs are clearly the underdogs there, it's Domain which is a far more important thing.<br /> <br /> Frankly, if you want the Anarchs to be a group that isn't a boots on the ground conflict of the poor and disenfranchised against the rich and powerful then MAYBE you aren't someone who should be playing the Anarchs vs. the Camarilla. The Anarchs are always revolutionaries of the peasant class (with the occassional defector ala Louis Fortier) fighting the landowning rulership class. This is why the Anarchs have been always on the backfoot in their conflict against the Camarilla as they control domain, influence, herds, and mortal allies to a far greater extent than the Anarchs.<br /> <br /> . </div> </div> </div>Anarchs are 'poor and disenfranchised' only in Vampire society. Among mortals, things are very different. Being an Anarch is not being a peasant during fuedalism, it's more akin to being a merchant in a class system that doesn't like them. or being 'New money' in today's society. There are many, many historical examples of the wealthy merchant class being 'oppressed' by the law-making Aristocracy who were wary of them gaining power, and honestly now that i think about it; holding the Anarchs as analogues to the Merchant class really rounds them out well with the Aristocratic Camarilla and the Theocratic Sabbat (The peasants toiling in the fields are, of course, ghouls and kine!) Regardless, someone easily making 2-3 dots of resources is only disenfranchised within the circles of the uber elite, not society in general.<br /> <br /> Hunters are meant to be the disenfranchised. They are meant to be the angry peasants. But you know, in history, people often treated peasants nicely, and then they didn't rebel. Any number of useful methods could be used for dealing with peasants, namely targeting the influentual...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T01:51:07-07:00","id":1381871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381842#post1381842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They are still required to be fugly. They have to take a required Flaw that represents it and take social penalties because of it. They just aren't 'OH GOD THAT IS A VAMPIRE OR SOMETHING OBVIOUSLY SUPERNATURAL'.<br /> <br /> But nice hyperbole.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, it's flat out not true for any of the Nosferatu in Chicago by Night 5E. They're some of the most freakish and Masquerade breaking looking ones in the series history if you go by the art.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://vignette.wikia.nocookie.net/whitewolf/images/d/df/Nathaniel_from_Chicago_by_Night_-_V5.png/revision/latest/top-crop/width/360/height/360?cb=20190727091749\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Coteries of New York was different.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://66.media.tumblr.com/546a1a20dbec10c6a85a1ac9d1a72948/51879e1e6a35c54b-43/s250x400/c471dc3e1ec2fcaf6b6fb2be79c589d89ffe3bed.gifv\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T02:12:30-07:00","id":1381873,"title":"","content":"D'Angelo can pass for a human who has a birth-defect, or suffered some mutilating injury like a car-wreck. I got the vibe that they were going with the idea that Nos, at least Nos with low blood potence, are fugly in ways that don't break the Masquerade, allowing you to play them without perpetually being obfuscated.<br /> <br /> That Chicago Nos is a walking Masquerade breach, though. I wonder if I misread their new policy, or one art team just didn't get the memo?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T02:24:14-07:00","id":1381874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381873#post1381873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">D'Angelo can pass for a human who has a birth-defect, or suffered some mutilating injury like a car-wreck. I got the vibe that they were going with the idea that Nos, at least Nos with low blood potence, are fugly in ways that don't break the Masquerade, allowing you to play them without perpetually being obfuscated.<br /> <br /> That Chicago Nos is a walking Masquerade breach, though. I wonder if I misread their new policy, or one art team just didn't get the memo?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't be surprised if the utterly fugly vampires are now going to get a flaw. Sort of like what they did with the Nagaraja.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Cults of the Blood Gods ones don't <i><b>have </b></i>to eat human flesh...but some do!&quot;<br /> <br /> We also have the traditional Nosferatu weakness in some Thin Bloods in Bloodlines 2:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/D_hWx1QXkAEOL0K.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-16-2020, 05:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T02:37:48-07:00","id":1381877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381859#post1381859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't differentiate them by their wildly different belief systems and philosophies, but instead by how cynical they are? I feel this thread has become a real eye opener.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your way of arguing is pretty bizarre. Everytime I talk about something you abruptly switch topics and it makes your argument fall apart because we're suddenly discussing something else. Yes, the Lasombra and the Setites have a fundamentally different view of RELIGION when discussing RELIGION. The Lasombra treat religion as a tool that they use and that affects their relationship with the people they control, their use of rhetoric, and their philosophies vs. the Setites. This is notably important in the time of the original Inquisition when the Lasombra's misuse and infiltration of the Church helped create the original Masquerade breach (or &quot;Silence of the Blood&quot;) and caused the Inquisition. That and Goratrix fucking with the Knights Templar in France if you believe the Transylvania Chronicles.<br /> <br /> I admit, I feel like the Tremere being responsible for the Church finding out about Kindred feels kind of dumb and anti-Tremere but it's canon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Anarchs are 'poor and disenfranchised' only in Vampire society. Among mortals, things are very different. Being an Anarch is not being a peasant during fuedalism, it's more akin to being a merchant in a class system that doesn't like them. or being 'New money' in today's society. There are many, many historical examples of the wealthy merchant class being 'oppressed' by the law-making Aristocracy who were wary of them gaining power, and honestly now that i think about it; holding the Anarchs as analogues to the Merchant class really rounds them out well with the Aristocratic Camarilla and the Theocratic Sabbat (The peasants toiling in the fields are, of course, ghouls and kine!) Regardless, someone easily making 2-3 dots of resources is only disenfranchised within the circles of the uber elite, not society in general.<br /> <br /> Hunters are meant to be the disenfranchised. They are meant to be the angry peasants. But you know, in history, people often treated peasants nicely, and then they didn't rebel. Any number of useful methods could be used for dealing with peasants, namely targeting the influentual... </div> </div> </div>Vampires have a bunch of incredible privileges over human beings that they acquire when being transformed into monsters. Disciplines, immortality, blah, blah, blah. They also have the weaknesses of losing activity during the daytime, the Beast, and so on.<br /> <br /> One of the things I always struggled with despite my fondness of the sect was the Anarch books rarely articulated is &quot;WHY do the Anarchs rebel?&quot; It was why I was pleased with Anarchs Unbound in V20 that it explained a good chunk of that is Domain. For the majority of vampires, unless you have a herd or regular feeding pattern, it is a night to night struggle for survival. Territory is one of the most important things that any vampire can have as feeding is the primary concern of every vampire. Before you can work to accumulate wealth, you need to be able to satisfy the basic needs of your Kindred nature: blood.<br /> <br /> One of the things that the V5 game worked very well for highlighting is the Camarilla does not recognize Anarch claim to any domain [and usually just leaves some area for Anarchs to feed in] while sending the Sheriff and Hounds or Scourge to destroy any Kindred who feeds in other Kindred's domain. COTERIES OF NEW YORK has Prince Panhard stake an Anarch for feeding in Central Park and decapitated because he dared &quot;claim&quot; it as his feeding grounds.<br /> <br /> Indeed, that is a major reason why the Camarilla exists. It not only exists to protect the Masquerade but to divy up the territory and domain of Kindred so that only those &quot;authorized&quot; to feed are allowed to do so. This makes a certain amount of sense as if you are cultivating the Dallas Cowboys cheerleaders as your herd, you are going to get pissed if someone drinks three of them dry. The conflict over domain is an easy one to articulate because the Camarilla wishes to force vampires that don't fit their system or government to the margins of society or outright destroy them. They practice Malthusian economics (i.e &quot;Overpopulation is bad, so speaks Thanos!&quot;) and do their best to control who is Embraced and who is forgiven or killed.<br /> <br /> Yes, some vampires can and do accumulate great power or wealth in their territory. Many Barons like Isaac Abrams, Louis Fortier, or Jeremy MacNeil can have the same power as Princes. Indeed, you need to have that if you want to cover up the Masquerade but the portrayal of your typical Anarch in the Free States (and this is where they RULE) is that Anarchs share domains and are mostly living night to night rather than building up vast power blocks.<br /> <br /> They either lack the Disciplines to do so or don't have the mindsets to create ghouls of Bill and Melinda Gates [who are probably controlled by the Camarilla, Technocracy, or Pentex anyway] instead of just their local bar owners.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T06:59:39-07:00","id":1381908,"title":"","content":"You're the one who keeps changing topic. I just threw pointed something out because I couldn't leave it alone, but I did it in a single line and then moved on. <br /> <br /> Vampires are rich people (Mostly) or subordinates of fabulously rich people. <br /> Rich people control the government by giving key people nice things.<br /> <b>The Government does not go after rich people</b><br /> Ergo, The second inquisition, as it is, is a bit of an incongruity .<br /> <br /> Vampire hunting is dangerous and stupid. <br /> Most intellegent people would realise it's not worth it. Those in power realise they can gain some benefit from rich vampire buddies<br /> Only someone crazy, or with a very serious personal grudge, or someone stupid, would do it.<br /> The quantity of quality vampire hunters cannot be so high. <br /> <br /> Vampires have many fantastic means at their disposal. <br /> If a big, threatening organization that wasn't a deeply underground terrorist oranization divided into loose cells started making serious moves towards vampire (Yeah, the Society of Leopold isn't this thing) Then the more powerful people of the global vampire conspiracy would find access to key figures in this organization and make them more reasonable or replace them. On a local level the princes can enact political purges and organize cleaning teams. If they With their abilities, if they can catch one, they can catch them all. <br /> The Camarilla was created for two purposes: First, to appease anarchs whilst keeping the power structures intact. Second, the masquerade. While it is argued in some books that the masquerade is self sustaining and exists to that princes and elders just use it as an excuse to exert power over others (That earlier part is important) the fact is it's a core directive, and it's utterly unreasonable to assume that the Camarilla really hasn't put any effort into monitoring and lubricating the big organizations. Nor is it reasonable to assume that someone had one important thrall in one of the largest alphabet organizations, nobody else had anyone there, and when the one guy disappeared there was absolutely nothing in place to stop her from a crusade. That implies some serious ineptitude from paranoid creatures that live for hundreds of years. <br /> <br /> Ultimately, 'the masquerade' isn't about a few people knowing, it's about everybody knowing. People have always known, and they have almst always been willfully ignorant because humans aren't selfless creatures that want to sacrifice themselves to be rid of an evil that doesn't immediately threaten them. How many people do you know have turned into eco-terrorists or political extremists in order to fight where democracy fails? Were they brilliant people? <br /> <br /> Imbued fit in perfectly with the Yokels and Faith hunters that have hunted vampires for millenia. &quot;The Man&quot; doesn't fit at all. Vampires aren't meant to be wrongly persecuted for being different, they're elites struggling in a cycle of jealousy, domination and paranoia. A just and righteous goverment does not belong in the world of darkness, and this big sweeping change that doesn't reflect reality really takes away from the potential of timelessness that VTM could have by remaining neutral and remaining objective (I realise that's not something past editions did consciously or particularly well at times, especially 1st edition, but the more the metaplot is inline with the real world, the better, and V5 is obstensibly worse for this given the inquisition) <br /> <br /> <b>Way better SI</b><br /> -After a disaster killing many of the old guard, The Society of Leopold modernizes as it's demographics shift. <br /> -A few groups of Islamic extremists really want to rid the world of vampires, but also want to take down the godless society they've corrupted. They formed an agreement with the SoL and in turn Protestant and Jewish groups have made contact, because for the most part destroying devils is more important to this group than prophet of choice. For novelty, we'll call them Abrahamic vampire hunters United (AHU) The AHU is by no means a perfect partnership. In some ways this does more harm than good, as the media is very keen to differentiate bombings by race and faith. But in terms of doing a lot of damage fast in a city, having more groups converge on a location at once, or having Christians do the inconceivable spying for a Muslim attack, the effectiveness of hunter groups has tripled, and all groups have become more willing to arm and direct yokels who don't share their prophet of choice. Supply chains and recruitment have improved considerably all-round. <br /> -AHU discovers the imbued, and begins to actively recruit. <br /> -Parts of the AHU are recieving indirect support from lupines who don't wish to war directly with vampires, mob groups who are afraid of vampire influence within their organization, a hand's worth theocratic mages exist within the ranks (at least one nephandi, of course) and of course vampires are still underestimating these groups and are largely unaware of their connections and are pushing them towards rivals. The one downside is that, given the increased number of connections, increased recruitment, and so on, the number of compromised teams have gone up and the body count increase isn't one-way. <br /> <br /> You can kinda take out the<b> Vienna prime </b>with this if you really wanted to? I wouldn't use the SoL here, enough of them would be known and watched. I'd use an Islamic group. I'd use a small group of gunmen and waves upon waves of suicide bombers. Start with a truckbomb for shock and awe and to open an entrance, gun down the outside survivors, Send the first man in. When he encounters the first major obstacle, he blows himself up, hopefully disrupting wards and such for the next man to move in who in turn blows himself up when it gets difficult. At least three teams of three will head below ground with rifles and bombs, in an attempt to fight their way to the sleeping elders in their bunkers, each team has their explosives rigged to go if they fail No attempt can be made to recover the repositories of information the vampires have here; The mission is to destroy the head vampires that lead the international vampire conspiracy, and they must escape the Austrian police and military who are no doubt under the control of vampires (in the minds of the SI) and who will no doubt overwhelm the teams who stayed on the surface to fend them off before long. There is no escape plan. Every man on this mission isn't just ready to die; they expect to die. They are Martyrs, Each of their names is written upon a tablet, to cherished by their order. None have families; they are orphans and survivors. Even the man on the edge, who pulls the trigger of the final remote detonator for the additional explosives the basement team have weaved throughout the bunker, has left an explosive device with himself for that moment.<br /> <br /> <br /> I'd say you'd need to drown the vampires in your own blood but then I remembered what vampires are. The point being you need a massive sacrifice to take out the most powerful vampire fortress in the world, or you'd need a modern military's might. You can't just say &quot;It was bombed, job done, look how powerful our protagonists are&quot; because that's not what hunters are meant to be. A human can't eat a four-course meal in one easy bite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T07:18:28-07:00","id":1381918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381908#post1381908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're the one who keeps changing topic. I just threw pointed something out because I couldn't leave it alone, but I did it in a single line and then moved on.</div> </div> </div> </div>My apologies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires are rich people (Mostly) or subordinates of fabulously rich people.<br /> Rich people control the government by giving key people nice things.<br /> <b>The Government does not go after rich people</b><br /> Ergo, The second inquisition, as it is, is a bit of an incongruity . </div> </div> </div>They do if they're brown, gay, or a threat to the supremacy of the system. The Sabbat and the Anarchs are certainly a bunch of brown as well as questionably rich people, certainly not as rich as the Camarilla. The vampires are also an &quot;other&quot; that can be the subject of government purges.<br /> <br /> In the SAD section of Project: Twilight, it says that the FBI goes after werewolves involved in civil rights and hates the Anarchs for their deviant behavior as well as ties to social justice or civil rights movements. This is canon, BTW, not my interpretation.<br /> <br /> Given the Sabbat are a religious terrorist organization that's killed hundreds if not thousands of Americans, I'd think that they'd be used.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire hunting is dangerous and stupid.<br /> Most intellegent people would realise it's not worth it. Those in power realise they can gain some benefit from rich vampire buddies<br /> Only someone crazy, or with a very serious personal grudge, or someone stupid, would do it.<br /> The quantity of quality vampire hunters cannot be so high. </div> </div> </div>Probably the same sort of thrill-seeking, dangerous, headstrong people who become Special Forces and SWAT members. Not to mention those hunters who are already part of the Society of Leopold or are recruited by them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires have many fantastic means at their disposal. If a big, threatening organization that wasn't a deeply underground terrorist oranization divided into loose cells started making serious moves towards vampire (Yeah, the Society of Leopold isn't this thing) Then the more powerful people of the global vampire conspiracy would find access to key figures in this organization and make them more reasonable or replace them. On a local level the princes can enact political purges and organize cleaning teams. If they With their abilities, if they can catch one, they can catch them all. </div> </div> </div>Which fails immediately with the fact that the Camarilla is going to support the Second Inquisition against the Sabbat and Anarchs for as long as they can. Its stated that they helped create the Second Inquisition by misusing government resources to fight its enemies. However, your argument also depends on the Camarilla being perfectly competent when recent years shows that government leaders can be complete morons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla was created for two purposes: First, to appease anarchs whilst keeping the power structures intact. Second, the masquerade. While it is argued in some books that the masquerade is self sustaining and exists to that princes and elders just use it as an excuse to exert power over others (That earlier part is important) the fact is it's a core directive, and it's utterly unreasonable to assume that the Camarilla really hasn't put any effort into monitoring and lubricating the big organizations. Nor is it reasonable to assume that someone had one important thrall in one of the largest alphabet organizations, nobody else had anyone there, and when the one guy disappeared there was absolutely nothing in place to stop her from a crusade. That implies some serious ineptitude from paranoid creatures that live for hundreds of years. </div> </div> </div>Yes, repairing the Masquerade after its horrific breach and the creation of the Second Inquisition is a top priority of V5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ultimately, 'the masquerade' isn't about a few people knowing, it's about everybody knowing. People have always known, and they have almst always been willfully ignorant because humans aren't selfless creatures that want to sacrifice themselves to be rid of an evil that doesn't immediately threaten them. How many people do you know have turned into eco-terrorists or political extremists in order to fight where democracy fails? Were they brilliant people? </div> </div> </div>Yes, if everyone knew the game would be over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imbued fit in perfectly with the Yokels and Faith hunters that have hunted vampires for millenia. &quot;The Man&quot; doesn't fit at all. Vampires aren't meant to be wrongly persecuted for being different, they're elites struggling in a cycle of jealousy, domination and paranoia. </div> </div> </div>That would be the Camarilla, yes. You are in fact describing the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A just and righteous goverment does not belong in the world of darkness, and this big sweeping change that doesn't reflect reality really takes away from the potential of timelessness that VTM could have by remaining neutral and remaining objective (I realise that's not something past editions did consciously or particularly well at times, especially 1st edition, but the more the metaplot is inline with the real world, the better, and V5 is obstensibly worse for this given the inquisition) </div> </div> </div>What makes you think the Second Inquisition is righteous? It's another form of evil fighting the Camarilla. Just because they're humans doesn't mean they're not monsters.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Way better SI</b><br /> -After a disaster killing many of the old guard, The Society of Leopold modernizes as it's demographics shift.<br /> -A few groups of Islamic extremists really want to rid the world of vampires, but also want to take down the godless society they've corrupted. They formed an agreement with the SoL and in turn Protestant and Jewish groups have made contact, because for the most part destroying devils is more important to this group than prophet of choice. For novelty, we'll call them Abrahamic vampire hunters United (AHU) The AHU is by no means a perfect partnership. In some ways this does more harm than good, as the media is very keen to differentiate bombings by race and faith. But in terms of doing a lot of damage fast in a city, having more groups converge on a location at once, or having Christians do the inconceivable spying for a Muslim attack, the effectiveness of hunter groups has tripled, and all groups have become more willing to arm and direct yokels who don't share their prophet of choice. Supply chains and recruitment have improved considerably all-round.<br /> -AHU discovers the imbued, and begins to actively recruit.<br /> -Parts of the AHU are recieving indirect support from lupines who don't wish to war directly with vampires, mob groups who are afraid of vampire influence within their organization, a hand's worth theocratic mages exist within the ranks (at least one nephandi, of course) and of course vampires are still underestimating these groups and are largely unaware of their connections and are pushing them towards rivals. The one downside is that, given the increased number of connections, increased recruitment, and so on, the number of compromised teams have gone up and the body count increase isn't one-way. </div> </div> </div>Aside from the Lupines and Mages, most of this happened. A big part of the Second Inquisition is the government outfitting, funding, and helping the SOL recruit to go from a few hundred hunters to several thousand and then give them intelligence as well as clearance to eliminate vampires as they see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T10:07:06-07:00","id":1381941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381908#post1381908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're the one who keeps changing topic. I just threw pointed something out because I couldn't leave it alone, but I did it in a single line and then moved on.<br /> <br /> Vampires are rich people (Mostly) or subordinates of fabulously rich people.<br /> Rich people control the government by giving key people nice things.<br /> <b>The Government does not go after rich people</b><br /> Ergo, The second inquisition, as it is, is a bit of an incongruity .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, and all vampires are legit, legal, wealthy donors whose money is tied up in temporal dollars, not backed by jewels, art, gold, property, etc. <br /> THey all pay their taxes and are a real part of the 1% of rich in the world that have bought the government. <br /> <br /> Except, y'know, they're largely not. But it seems like you have a lot of preconceived real world notions that you're carrying over into the game, which the fiction of the WoD historically does not support. In fact, the WoD has minimized a lot of this in the past editions, to the detriment of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T10:17:46-07:00","id":1381943,"title":"","content":"Part of why I like the Camarilla/Anarch split is the fact that it does nicely make one the slobs (Anarchs) and the other the snobs (Camarilla).<br /> <br /> I never understood why the Camarilla would include the Illuminati/Eyes Wide Shut types with the dirty hillbilly vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T13:08:26-07:00","id":1381965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381941#post1381941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, and all vampires are legit, legal, wealthy donors whose money is tied up in temporal dollars, not backed by jewels, art, gold, property, etc.<br /> THey all pay their taxes and are a real part of the 1% of rich in the world that have bought the government.<br /> <br /> Except, y'know, they're largely not. But it seems like you have a lot of preconceived real world notions that you're carrying over into the game, which the fiction of the WoD historically does not support. In fact, the WoD has minimized a lot of this in the past editions, to the detriment of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Firstly, do you believe real multi-millionaires and billionaires are paying their taxes? Lets say you need to pay 20 million in tax every year. You can pay an accountant 30k to pull some tricks with your money and an influentual politician 1 million to ensure that, not only is tax low, tax codes remain a mess so your accountant can do more things with it, oh, and you can donate 5 million to charity to write some money off. you only need to pay 5 million now in tax. You're ten million better off than you'd be if you just paid up honestly. That isn't even going into options like claiming you actually made no money because of patents your tax-haven subsidiary owns... <br /> <br /> You don't pay taxes, you make 'generous contributions'. Bruce Wayne can spend millions on orphanedges to avoid tenfold taxes. The FBI isn't mad at vampires because they aren't funded by vampire tax, as they undoubtedly recieve many magnanimous donations from pale parasites. <br /> Obviously, I'm exaggerating here (Am I?) I realise I'm looking a bit like a rabid supporter of an ideology. But I can assure you I don't let it colour my perceptions. The world of Darkness is meant to be a shitty place, and I believe the very worst of both left and right theories should be used and exaggerated. Mortal institutions are meant to be deeply corrupt. Vampires are meant to be completely corrupt. <br /> <br /> I'll admit, yes, I am swayed by the fact that dudes who join special forces wanna kick ass. But they also want to be the best. More of them want to kick down than punch up. For more normal law enforcement; if tolerating a generous possible-vampire gives police more oppertunity to power-fantasy their way through the poor, is it really that smart to bite his hand?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T18:17:37-07:00","id":1382025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381965#post1381965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Firstly, do you believe real multi-millionaires and billionaires are paying their taxes? Lets say you need to pay 20 million in tax every year. You can pay an accountant 30k to pull some tricks with your money and an influentual politician 1 million to ensure that, not only is tax low, tax codes remain a mess so your accountant can do more things with it, oh, and you can donate 5 million to charity to write some money off. you only need to pay 5 million now in tax. You're ten million better off than you'd be if you just paid up honestly. That isn't even going into options like claiming you actually made no money because of patents your tax-haven subsidiary owns...</div> </div> </div> </div>I grew up to the manor born country club set before my father's fortune was wiped in 2008 and I can tell you I know plenty of the tricks, trades, and lies that the wealthy do to avoid dealing with any form of law. Believe me, I know the kind of complete scummy assholes that form the kind of conspiracies that exist to keep the rich from any sort of consequence in Mitch McConnell's Kentucky. I also know the tried and true people who try to ice skate uphill and manage to take one or two of them down at a time that exist in the state as well.<br /> <br /> Part of the issue here is the fact that billionaires and millionaires are almost invulnerable but you seem to forget that many-many people dedicate their lives to destroying them nevertheless. They spend months, years, and decades building lawsuits and criminal actions that will fail 90% of the time but that 9% partial success or 1% that does succeed gives meaning to their lives. They exist not by the dozens but by the thousands and is a note that I think kind of gets overlooked here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't pay taxes, you make 'generous contributions'. Bruce Wayne can spend millions on orphanedges to avoid tenfold taxes. The FBI isn't mad at vampires because they aren't funded by vampire tax, as they undoubtedly recieve many magnanimous donations from pale parasites.<br /> Obviously, I'm exaggerating here (Am I?) I realise I'm looking a bit like a rabid supporter of an ideology. But I can assure you I don't let it colour my perceptions. The world of Darkness is meant to be a shitty place, and I believe the very worst of both left and right theories should be used and exaggerated. Mortal institutions are meant to be deeply corrupt. Vampires are meant to be completely corrupt. </div> </div> </div>Basically, my objection to your worldbuilding isn't that it's wrong, it's the fact you're describing the Camarilla and only the Camarilla. The game was created with the view of the vampires being neonates caught up in a society run behind the scenes by undead parasites. However, those people are not the only vampires, Going back to FORGED IN STEEL the original chronicle, you have the player characters who are introduced to Modius as an embodiment of a failing aristocracy, Juggler as a corrupt Anarch Baron, and the various vampires around them (with Lucien the shipping magnate as the real power in the region).<br /> <br /> But even then, you had:<br /> <br /> * Sullivan Dane: The iconic witch hunter and fanatic who is going to kill your ass.<br /> * William Shepherd: An FBI agent investigating the vampires with plans of taking them down.<br /> * Gregory Stephens: A police officer trying to navigate the law to bring down the Cainites while not bringing down their wrath on them.<br /> <br /> I think that human institutions can be worse than vampires in the setting as well, particularly if you're part of a World of Darkness. The Second Inquisition isn't a bunch of heroes, they're a bunch of insane and evil zealots that are carrying out a purge of people they're racist against. A lot of them have it coming but the worst of them (the rich Camarilla) are protected while the least scummy are the ones who suffer most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll admit, yes, I am swayed by the fact that dudes who join special forces wanna kick ass. But they also want to be the best. More of them want to kick down than punch up. For more normal law enforcement; if tolerating a generous possible-vampire gives police more oppertunity to power-fantasy their way through the poor, is it really that smart to bite his hand? </div> </div> </div>You can run it that way, but that flat out was not true in Vampire: The Masquerade 2nd Edition or Revised, let alone V20 or V5.<br /> <br /> You are basically ignoring how the government was treated in all previous editions.<br /> <br /> The NSA and SAD were enemies of vampires as early as 1992.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-16-2020, 09:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-16T22:24:37-07:00","id":1382063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1381943#post1381943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Part of why I like the Camarilla/Anarch split is the fact that it does nicely make one the slobs (Anarchs) and the other the snobs (Camarilla).<br /> <br /> I never understood why the Camarilla would include the Illuminati/Eyes Wide Shut types with the dirty hillbilly vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div>Initially I think the Anarchs were originally intended to be basically Shadowrunners. They were the guys the Elders(corporate heads) and Methuselahs(dragons) hired and manipulated to fight for them. That's why you had things like the Anarchs having de facto status in the city in first edition. Later editions changed what being an anarch meant, but a lot of things survived on sheer inertia even though they no longer really fit together neatly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T09:25:53-07:00","id":1382187,"title":"","content":"I actually disagree with CTPhipps notion of VTM. Its a TTRP game, it shouldn't lean toward any particular &quot;view&quot;. The game shouldn't be about neonates in any particular pattern. Players should be given the options to build up their base and abilities as they grow as a character in the World of Darkness. Thats the reason why I vehemently disdain how V5 has removed 6+ Disciplines and all the Elders going to this &quot;beckoning&quot; event. The writers are explicitly forcing you to play a Neonate style type of game, especially with all the strange nerfs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T09:34:42-07:00","id":1382189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382063#post1382063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Initially I think the Anarchs were originally intended to be basically Shadowrunners. They were the guys the Elders(corporate heads) and Methuselahs(dragons) hired and manipulated to fight for them. That's why you had things like the Anarchs having de facto status in the city in first edition. Later editions changed what being an anarch meant, but a lot of things survived on sheer inertia even though they no longer really fit together neatly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a very similar view but slightly different. The PCs are Shadowrunners doing jobs for the Anarchs, Elders, and other people in a megacorp ruled world.<br /> <br /> The Anarchs are the criminal syndicates, the Camarilla Elders are the megacorps, and the Methusalehs are the Dragons.<br /> <br /> You can work for all three but it's all about survival.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T10:37:28-07:00","id":1382197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382187#post1382187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually disagree with CTPhipps notion of VTM. Its a TTRP game, it shouldn't lean toward any particular &quot;view&quot;. The game shouldn't be about neonates in any particular pattern. Players should be given the options to build up their base and abilities as they grow as a character in the World of Darkness. Thats the reason why I vehemently disdain how V5 has removed 6+ Disciplines and all the Elders going to this &quot;beckoning&quot; event. The writers are explicitly forcing you to play a Neonate style type of game, especially with all the strange nerfs.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is ultimately my biggest issue with 5th edition. In previous editions it felt like there were lots of options of playstyles (Neonates, Elders, Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs, Tal'mahe'Ra, etc) but 5th Edition feels like it's trying to shoehorn players into a singular type of game. I'm hoping that as more books are released they'll start adding more options for players, but we'll just have to wait and see. But that's enough off-topic 5th edition griping for me, at least for this thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T11:07:04-07:00","id":1382202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382197#post1382197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is ultimately my biggest issue with 5th edition. In previous editions it felt like there were lots of options of playstyles (Neonates, Elders, Camarilla, Sabbat, Anarchs, Tal'mahe'Ra, etc) but 5th Edition feels like it's trying to shoehorn players into a singular type of game. I'm hoping that as more books are released they'll start adding more options for players, but we'll just have to wait and see. But that's enough off-topic 5th edition griping for me, at least for this thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's restrictions, I think they're taking their time introducing new elements. Not just doing it all in one book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T14:31:51-07:00","id":1382245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382202#post1382202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think there's restrictions, I think they're taking their time introducing new elements. Not just doing it all in one book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant more in the sense that there were such massive changes to both the setting and the mechanics in 5th edition, that 5th edition is not &quot;backwards compatible&quot; with the older editions.<br /> <br /> When the V20 corebook first came out, I got my group together and we ran a Tal'mahe'Ra game (this was before the v20 Guide to the TMR was released). I was able to whip out my well-worn Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand and use that, and the players were able to use older Disciplines and we just kind of eyeballed them and updated them into the new edition.<br /> <br /> 5th edition though has undergone enormous setting and mechanics changes though that I couldn't really do that. I mean, does the Tal'mahe'Ra even still exist? If it does, what does it look like in light of the Beckoning? How would elder Disciplines work in the new paradigm? I guess I could just try and homebrew all of that, but it would be a lot more work than I'd be willing to put in. Alternatively I could wait a year (or two, or five or possibly even more) for them to release the new rules and setting info on those things. Or as a third alternative I could just <i>not</i> play 5th edition and stick to the older editions (which, so far, is what my group has primarily decided to do).<br /> <br /> I understand, of course, that White Wolf is functionally a new studio, they want to put their own spin on the setting, and also from a simple economic point of view, it's more profitable if players can't just buy and use older editions of the books and instead have to purchase the new products. Please don't think I'm ragging on White Wolf or 5th edition in that regard, because I'm not. Still, there's a certain level of aggravation in the rollover to 5th edition that didn't happen with the rollovers to the previous new editions, since the setting and rules were all mostly similar enough that you could get by with the old material until newer stuff was released.<br /> <br /> Right now, at least with 5th edition, there's really only a couple of playstyles that are possible (Camarilla/Anarch neonates), and since I don't see them releasing a Guide to the Sabbat or Guide to the Elders type books any time in the near future, those will probably remain the only real playstyles for the foreseeable future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-17T16:10:19-07:00","id":1382262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382245#post1382245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, at least with 5th edition, there's really only a couple of playstyles that are possible (Camarilla/Anarch neonates), and since I don't see them releasing a Guide to the Sabbat or Guide to the Elders type books any time in the near future, those will probably remain the only real playstyles for the foreseeable future.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the blurb, the upcoming Players\u2019 Guide is explicitly meant to discuss alternative play styles and games. It\u2019s not been released yet, so maybe you could write to Modiphius to let them know what you want? <br /> <br /> They\u2019ve only scheduled and announced supplements for about the next year (less than that now, really) of releases, including Onyx Path. I wouldn\u2019t write off any nominal supplement moving beyond that point.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T01:54:37-07:00","id":1382296,"title":"","content":"A big issue i have with V5 is that it's less speculative. It's moved from &quot;what would happen&quot; to &quot;what would we like to happen&quot;.<br /> <br /> The setting has turned into one person's vision of a game; It's a persecution complex for being different. The Goverments of the world have turned against you, the Camarilla has abandoned you, you have much less power and much less control over yourself as you struggle with the mental health issue known as &quot;The Beast&quot;. The Anarchs have vered sharply towards being a group of &quot;Allies&quot; but the Sabbat have gone just ic case someone notices your choice of &quot;allies&quot; has an unhealthy relationship. The Game has moved towards this very specific feeling/theme/playstyle. But it's not the realistic option: The Cam wouldn't give up their power over you/the anarchs, the efforts of hunters have grown preposterously, and the Sabbat and elders leaving is both unreasonable and has no precedent. (Do not cite the &quot;reasons&quot;, I know them, they're not good)<br /> <br /> Hunters, even the dudes in the goverment, have always been a few crazies. Bob Schnoblin might be a bit extreme, but the people after supernatural forces lean his way more than any other.<br /> Vampire has largely been about hierarchical power structures. V5 has flattened them and turned everything against the player. Players can't really take advantage of power structures any more, it's a setting where nobody knows their place. Fundamentally, you can't do other styles of play with the setting given. Everyone's persecuted and on even footing. Even if we were to do an elder game, you'd still be lacking power as your subordinates have gone to shit and the inquisition would still be after you.<br /> <br /> V5 hunters do not make logistic sense. They cannot conceivably work. They must be exaggerated at least fivefold. But the devs are doing &quot;What would we like to happen&quot; rather than &quot;what would happen&quot;. It's comparable to an alternate history where Nazi Germany won WW2; They can only win if you removed the &quot;nazi&quot; part and wrote their opponents into utter and unreasonable ineptitude. V5 has written the SI's opponents into utter and unreasonable ineptitude, but still the SI can only exist on the scale it does now if... No, it can't. Logistically, it's impossible, even with mages involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T02:53:32-07:00","id":1382300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382296#post1382296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big issue i have with V5 is that it's less speculative. It's moved from &quot;what would happen&quot; to &quot;what would we like to happen&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>The setting has turned into one person's vision of a game; </b>It's a persecution complex for being different. The Goverments of the world have turned against you, the Camarilla has abandoned you, you have much less power and much less control over yourself as you struggle with the mental health issue known as &quot;The Beast&quot;. The Anarchs have vered sharply towards being a group of &quot;Allies&quot; but the Sabbat have gone just ic case someone notices your choice of &quot;allies&quot; has an unhealthy relationship. The Game has moved towards this very specific feeling/theme/playstyle. But it's not the realistic option:<b> The Cam wouldn't give up their power over you/the anarchs, the efforts of hunters have grown preposterously, and the Sabbat and elders leaving is both unreasonable and has no precedent.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Bluntly, you've just kind of written yourself into a corner. This is very much your one person's vision of the game. I don't have to cite the &quot;reasons&quot; but you are basically saying your interpretation of the game is the correct one and that's fine at your table but the simple fact is that it is not everyone else's table and if you don't want to hear arguments about why it might work, that's not really improving things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hunters, even the dudes in the goverment, have always been a few crazies. </div> </div> </div>Except for the NSA, a group supported by the Catholic Church, and an entire department of the FBI. Plus there's the Arcanum that is large enough and powerful enough that the Camarilla can't shut it down.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire has largely been about hierarchical power structures. V5 has flattened them and turned everything against the player. </div> </div> </div>You can play as a Camarilla ally still. Being an Anarch is my preferred playstyle but the Camarilla is entirely an option for gaming. So is now being a member of the Hecata and a independent Blood Cult.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Players can't really take advantage of power structures any more, it's a setting where nobody knows their place. </div> </div> </div>1. Except for the Camarilla, a Blood Cult, or a power structure in the Anarchs.<br /> 2. Has anyone in the history of gaming EVER wanted to know their place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fundamentally, you can't do other styles of play with the setting given. </div> </div> </div>You can still play someone who is part of the Camarilla. I'm confused by this. Indeed, the first Chronicle &quot;THE SACRIFICE&quot; has you aiding a Prince and getting a Clan to join the Camarilla.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everyone's persecuted and on even footing. Even if we were to do an elder game, you'd still be lacking power as your subordinates have gone to shit and the inquisition would still be after you. </div> </div> </div>Ummm, isn't challenge part of the fyun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 hunters do not make logistic sense. They cannot conceivably work. </div> </div> </div>You seem to actively not want to acknowledge large scale hunting organizations existed in previous editions. How did the Society of Leopold exist and kill hundreds of vampires every year in your games?<br /> <br /> Hunters weren't just the Frog Brothers even in previous editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T07:49:53-07:00","id":1382328,"title":"","content":"The Society of Leopold is fundamentally different from &quot;the government&quot;. <br /> <br /> Quick google search tells me the head of the CIA is Gina Cheri Haspel. To find her, I'd go to the CIA headquarters at Langley, McLean, Virginia, United States. I'm sure they've got a sign somewhere. There's a clear easy channel to get to the goverment's leaders. Who leads the society of Leopold? Where are they? Is it the pope? I probably need co-ordinates to some secret holy site in the middle of the woods. <br /> Next is motivation. I don't know Gina, I have no insight to her motivations or what she's like as a person. But I can imagine as a whole, people in this job are power hungry, ambitious, flexible, good at making connections. Most of those things would apply to a leader of the Society of Leopold. But the leader of the SoL is also a dogmatic religious nut, the subordinates are dogmatic religious nuts. Maybe I'm wrong and the leader of the SoL is really a wolf taking advantage of sheep. Maybe he/she lives in a luxury manor provided by the funds of defeated vampires, fully capable of taking a bribe from a vampire; so Long as they have the appearance of someone dedicated to hunting vampires, the cult will live on. But it's more likely that the leader of the SoL is also a dogmatic nutter living in a holy site deep in the woods. The point being it's far, far easier for Vampires to get in with the landed, ligitimate authorities than it is to get in with nutters who don't have postal adresses. Then we go into what happens when we actually get in with them. For the society of Leopold, If the leader falls under suspicion of working with vampires, the various disconected cells are likely to denounce and ignore him/her. Whilst if poor Gina starts to direct people against vampires, suddenly a whole lot of people within and without the organization are looking to have her replaced. But if Gina starts to crack down on people working against vampires, what are these people going to do? Disobey their strict, legitimate hierarchical organization with strong legal consequences?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T09:18:55-07:00","id":1382337,"title":"","content":"Fair enough, @MyWifeIsScary<br /> <br /> In any case, &quot;Why not the Imbued?&quot;<br /> <br /> I know, crazy, getting back to the original topic. I think the answer to that question is the fact that the Imbued are supernatural. It's the same issue that the Technocracy, Werewolves, or some sort of vampiric patron have with the undead. The Second Inquisition is based around two concepts that I think are intristic to its existence.<br /> <br /> <b>1:] Do not introduce too much too soon</b><br /> <br /> One of the things that V5 has going for it is the fact it's a &quot;back to basics&quot; approach with the idea that newcomers don't have to absorb a very large amount of lore. It just wants to introduce vampires, some starting clans, and Hunters. A huge amount of content is chucked out, which isn't very good for longtime fans but this is meant to be a Starter Set for people. You can't introduce any of the supernatural factions of other gamelines without getting into the kudzu plot of lore that all of these groups are.<br /> Who, what, when, where, how, and so on of the Imbued is a whole book itself.<br /> <br /> <b>2:] To make mortals scary again</b><br /> <br /> Carmilla and Dracula were the original vampire stories with both of them having plucky mortals put an end to their sinister villains. Vampire hunters are a inseperable piece of vampire lore and something that is at the core of the whole &quot;Masquerade&quot; concept. The idea that vampires cannot control humanity, just influence it, and that if they are ever found out then they will be exterminated by humanity.<br /> <br /> I honestly think they went too far with the SI the same way I think V5 did the Sabbat wrong. I think the SI is too big and powerful for the Masquerade to hold. I also feel its writing is a bit schizophrenic in how many people exist. However, I love the concept because vampires being on the backfoot is something that really adds a new layer to the game. Every edition should add something to the game and the SI is certainly an element that was previously overlooked. Hunters now have a lot more tools at their disposal and it allows new enemies as well as complications to the lives of PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T10:31:56-07:00","id":1382346,"title":"","content":"I don't understand the &quot;back to the basic&quot; thing with these V5 writers. oWoD has global acclaim, its already well known with a considerable fanbase over the years. Why did it have to soft retcon things &quot;back to the basics&quot; for? They could have angled it in writing where even though newcomers come on and be a little out the loop, they can still be engaged with the story, making them interesting to get the older books to look into as I did when I got introduced in oWoD in 2018. It isn't hard at all. This reintroduction is tedious to <i>all</i> fans because we didn't need it at all. Personally (I don't know about anyone else) I just wanted things to move along into the modern age past the 1990s. Also V5 did more than &quot;reintroduce&quot; clans and act as if the series is somehow back to 1e- it has made the nonsensical Hecata &quot;clan&quot; (which should've been a Sect), gas-lighted the Tremere down to bits (which we have discussed in this thread ad naseum), putting personal seemingly political bias in VTM, making the series cater to the Anarchs when by Revised and 2e they were merely a background third neutral faction for the most part, etc. <br /> <br /> Now onto the Second Inquisition and why I believe the Imbued should've been the ones to be the Hunter faction against them? Because the Imbued make the most sense in the context of the oWoD universe. They are decentralized, have a hunter marking way of communication, imbued (as their namesake) abilities to go up against OP Vampires, they consistently delve in conspiracy theories where it would make sense for them to uncover all the shit about Vampire society (I would tack them on as the ones to infiltrate Schrecknet, not the freaking NSA), etc. <br /> <br /> \u200bIt simply doesn't make sense for the SI to gain this much traction as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> has mentioned before. Top of these discretions is how the SI droned the Chantry that is warded against Technology, teleports, and is disguised from mortals. In actuality I would make it so it was the Imbued (who have an allotment of conspiracy laded people) would've bombed the Chantry since they could've seen it with Second Sight (the premiere ability they have that lets them see Supernaturals). It just feels more natural in the context of oWoD.<br /> <br /> Also the series is past the point of ignoring other Supernaturals in a shared universe at this point, I don't agree with V5 going down the route as if WoD hasn't progressed past that niche- as it is 1e still. Already Wraith: The Oblivion was influenced by Mage and Vampire in lieu of the spirit nuke debacle. Beyond that there have been numerous instances of Supernaturals having contact with eachother almost all the time. People keep gassing up Crossovers are unrealistic when numerous piles of evidence show other when they have to the contrary. Longtime fans already know who the Imbued are. Newcomers if they don't know who the Imbued are will get intrigued by them and get interested. Honestly I actually fear nuWolf has completely forgotten about them or won't write anything about them at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T12:16:15-07:00","id":1382366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382346#post1382346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the &quot;back to the basic&quot; thing with these V5 writers. oWoD has global acclaim, its already well known with a considerable fanbase over the years. Why did it have to soft retcon things &quot;back to the basics&quot; for? They could have angled it in writing where even though newcomers come on and be a little out the loop, they can still be engaged with the story, making them interesting to get the older books to look into as I did when I got introduced in oWoD in 2018. It isn't hard at all. This reintroduction is tedious to <i>all</i> fans because we didn't need it at all. Personally (I don't know about anyone else) I just wanted things to move along into the modern age past the 1990s. Also V5 did more than &quot;reintroduce&quot; clans and act as if the series is somehow back to 1e- it has made the nonsensical Hecata &quot;clan&quot; (which should've been a Sect), gas-lighted the Tremere down to bits (which we have discussed in this thread ad naseum), <b>putting personal seemingly political bias in VTM</b>, making the series cater to the Anarchs when by Revised and 2e they were merely a background third neutral faction for the most part, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bolded part is not new. The games that WW made were originally crafted with an awful lot of anger toward past generations and a rather left-leaning bent. Furthermore, all art takes a stance on politics, so even if it had been changed to be right-leaning for some reason, it would still be a personal political bias. You can try to take emotions and feelings out of someone, but the end result is only that they have a rather difficult time making decisions; the Clarity of Alchemical Exalted is not something that humans have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now onto the Second Inquisition and why I believe the Imbued should've been the ones to be the Hunter faction against them? Because the Imbued make the most sense in the context of the oWoD universe. They are decentralized, have a hunter marking way of communication, imbued (as their namesake) abilities to go up against OP Vampires, they consistently delve in conspiracy theories where it would make sense for them to uncover all the shit about Vampire society (I would tack them on as the ones to infiltrate Schrecknet, not the freaking NSA), etc. </div> </div> </div>The Imbued are also pretty rare, and the rate of attrition is high. You can't train someone to become one, either, but you can recruit from a wide pool of operatives for a more conventional organization.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bIt simply doesn't make sense for the SI to gain this much traction as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> has mentioned before. Top of these discretions is how the SI droned the Chantry that is warded against Technology, teleports, and is disguised from mortals. In actuality I would make it so it was the Imbued (who have an allotment of conspiracy laded people) would've bombed the Chantry since they could've seen it with Second Sight (the premiere ability they have that lets them see Supernaturals). It just feels more natural in the context of oWoD.<br /> <br /> Also the series is past the point of ignoring other Supernaturals in a shared universe at this point, I don't agree with V5 going down the route as if WoD hasn't progressed past that niche- as it is 1e still. Already Wraith: The Oblivion was influenced by Mage and Vampire in lieu of the spirit nuke debacle. Beyond that there have been numerous instances of Supernaturals having contact with eachother almost all the time. People keep gassing up Crossovers are unrealistic when numerous piles of evidence show other when they have to the contrary. Longtime fans already know who the Imbued are. Newcomers if they don't know who the Imbued are will get intrigued by them and get interested. Honestly I actually fear nuWolf has completely forgotten about them or won't write anything about them at all. </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't seem to be ignoring a shared universe; if anything, it's shoving it further into our faces, which seems like it was the plan all along. That was what the &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; tagling from back when the buyout happened was all about. They've also been cavalier in employing Garou as walking cuisinarts to threaten the soft, bloody fruit that are Kindred into not venturing into certain locations. Though, if anyone was going to bomb a Kindred stronghold under those circumstances, it would have been spearheaded by the Dies Ultimae camp of Glass Walkers, which is not just a paramilitary group of Garou and kin, but also a doomsday cult that probably doesn't see itself as having much to lose from taking blatant actions like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T12:37:59-07:00","id":1382369,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382346#post1382346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the &quot;back to the basic&quot; thing with these V5 writers. oWoD has global acclaim, its already well known with a considerable fanbase over the years. Why did it have to soft retcon things &quot;back to the basics&quot; for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1. Because they want to appeal to a new global audience, not just the aging fans.<br /> <br /> 2. They want to appeal to people who have fallen out of the WOD over the past two decades.<br /> <br /> 3. Because they don't want people just buying old books or using their old books versus buying the new ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They could have angled it in writing where even though newcomers come on and be a little out the loop, they can still be engaged with the story, making them interesting to get the older books to look into as I did when I got introduced in oWoD in 2018. It isn't hard at all. This reintroduction is tedious to <i>all</i> fans because we didn't need it at all. Personally (I don't know about anyone else) I just wanted things to move along into the modern age past the 1990s. </div> </div> </div>Except it's been incredibly well received by a lot of people. Tens of thousands of new fans have been brought on by LA by Night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also V5 did more than &quot;reintroduce&quot; clans and act as if the series is somehow back to 1e- it has made the nonsensical Hecata &quot;clan&quot; (which should've been a Sect), gas-lighted the Tremere down to bits (which we have discussed in this thread ad naseum), putting personal seemingly political bias in VTM, making the series cater to the Anarchs when by Revised and 2e they were merely a background third neutral faction for the most part, etc. </div> </div> </div>Every single Edition introduces changes to the Clans and sects.<br /> <br /> 1. The Hecata are a sect, they're just a sect based around a variety of Bloodlines linked to the Cappadocians.<br /> 2. Anarch Tremere ftw.<br /> 3. Political bias is fucking bizarre given that it was created as a anti-establishment Goth counterculture RPG. I wrote an essay on it: <a href=\"http://unitedfederationofcharles.blogspot.com/2019/06/the-social-satire-of-vampire-masquerade.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://unitedfederationofcharles.blo...asquerade.html</a><br /> 4. Anarch bias is the silliest goddamn thing ever. That's like saying the Sabbat had Sabbat bias or Kuei-Jin had Kuei-jin bias for having the editions benefit them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now onto the Second Inquisition and why I believe the Imbued should've been the ones to be the Hunter faction against them? Because the Imbued make the most sense in the context of the oWoD universe. They are decentralized, have a hunter marking way of communication, imbued (as their namesake) abilities to go up against OP Vampires, they consistently delve in conspiracy theories where it would make sense for them to uncover all the shit about Vampire society (I would tack them on as the ones to infiltrate Schrecknet, not the freaking NSA), etc. </div> </div> </div>The Imbued are notably a bunch of people who according to their own gameline either will die or go hopelessly insane as their Virtues drive them irrevocably mad. They are also possessed of contradictory Creeds that cannot team up together for long periods of time and are deliberately designed so that Edges don't actually provide them all that many benefits against supernaturals. A Imbued with powerful Edges that allow him to beat a vampire with a baseball bat will never be as effective as a Hunter as a guy with an M16 as the government can very easily outfit but Imbued won't be.<br /> <br /> Mind you, my Second Inquisition does make use of the Imbued. The SI in my campaigns recruited all surviving Imbued for their expertise using Hunter.net to track them down. Many didn't cooperate but many did and some even joined the front lines.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [It simply doesn't make sense for the SI to gain this much traction as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25794_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25794\" data-vbnamecard=\"25794\">MyWifeIsScary</a> has mentioned before. Top of these discretions is how the SI droned the Chantry that is warded against Technology, teleports, and is disguised from mortals. In actuality I would make it so it was the Imbued (who have an allotment of conspiracy laded people) would've bombed the Chantry since they could've seen it with Second Sight (the premiere ability they have that lets them see Supernaturals). It just feels more natural in the context of oWoD. </div> </div> </div>The problem with the argument of &quot;The Chantry was warded against MAGIIICC&quot; is the fact that the Society of Leopold has wizards of its own, artifacts that drain magic [True Faith], and records dating back a 1000 years. The NSA has technology that bypasses magic as of V20 as well as a bunch of psychics. Certainly, their abilities are more reliable than Edges that, again, drive most Imbued insane after an extended period of use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also the series is past the point of ignoring other Supernaturals in a shared universe at this point, I don't agree with V5 going down the route as if WoD hasn't progressed past that niche- as it is 1e still. Already Wraith: The Oblivion was influenced by Mage and Vampire in lieu of the spirit nuke debacle. Beyond that there have been numerous instances of Supernaturals having contact with eachother almost all the time. People keep gassing up Crossovers are unrealistic when numerous piles of evidence show other when they have to the contrary. Longtime fans already know who the Imbued are. Newcomers if they don't know who the Imbued are will get intrigued by them and get interested. Honestly I actually fear nuWolf has completely forgotten about them or won't write anything about them at all. </div> </div> </div>This is just my view but from now on, I wouldn't be surrpised if the Vampires are the central splat with everyone else as a supplement to it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T13:41:09-07:00","id":1382374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382346#post1382346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand the &quot;back to the basic&quot; thing with these V5 writers. oWoD has global acclaim, its already well known with a considerable fanbase over the years. Why did it have to soft retcon things &quot;back to the basics&quot; for? They could have angled it in writing where even though newcomers come on and be a little out the loop, they can still be engaged with the story, making them interesting to get the older books to look into as I did when I got introduced in oWoD in 2018. It isn't hard at all. This reintroduction is tedious to <i>all</i> fans because we didn't need it at all. Personally (I don't know about anyone else) I just wanted things to move along into the modern age past the 1990s. Also V5 did more than &quot;reintroduce&quot; clans and act as if the series is somehow back to 1e- it has made the nonsensical Hecata &quot;clan&quot; (which should've been a Sect), gas-lighted the Tremere down to bits (which we have discussed in this thread ad naseum), putting personal seemingly political bias in VTM, making the series cater to the Anarchs when by Revised and 2e they were merely a background third neutral faction for the most part, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they need new fans to keep the franchise alive. I'm not sure how that is even a question. 'Global acclaim' and 'well known' is a thing for WoD, sure, in very niche gaming circles. There has not been an in print game book for Vampire in years, and not all of the vampire fandom comes to these online forums, despite how much people claim otherwise. V5 is changing that by being the first new vampire book in stores in years. When V5 books first got out into stores, one of the game store owners locally was even surprised that there had been a 20th Anniversary edition, he had thought vampire had ended when they stopped having Requiem product to order. Another one thought the same and had thought that no one played anymore and that it was a dead line. So your 'considerable fanbase' is a very vocal portion, but hardly representative of every person who has played or will ever play vampire.<br /> <br /> Basically you're advocating for gatekeeping, instead of making it immediately accessible and then adding complexity through options. News Flash: You. And. The. Online. Community. Are. Not A. Representative. Of. All. Fans. Constantly saying 'we didn't need' and 'we don't want' represents some very vocal portion of the fanbase, but you do not represent the entire fanbase, just your echo chamber. Besides, largely, V5 has been well-received BECAUSE it's allowing new fans in.with less overwhelming material (sorry not sorry, V20 is a fucking joke for introducing new people because of overload, lack of context, and other factors). It's cool that YOU weren't overwhelmed by everything prior, but YOU are not EVERYONE. <br /> <br /> As far as political, vampire has always been political. Whether that is a plus or a minus is in individual tastes, but man. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now onto the Second Inquisition and why I believe the Imbued should've been the ones to be the Hunter faction against them? Because the Imbued make the most sense in the context of the oWoD universe. They are decentralized, have a hunter marking way of communication, imbued (as their namesake) abilities to go up against OP Vampires, they consistently delve in conspiracy theories where it would make sense for them to uncover all the shit about Vampire society (I would tack them on as the ones to infiltrate Schrecknet, not the freaking NSA), etc. </div> </div> </div>'OP Vampires' here we go with more invincible vampire bullshit. Humans are a threat because numbers, technology, and tons of things that have been detailed ad nauseum in this thread. Just because you don't feel like it's logical, does not mean it is not within the INTERNAL LOGIC of the setting. Imbued have less numbers, less organization, and tend to burn out super fast. So unless there's a new Imbued being empowered every other day, they're going to burn out their numbers faster than 'a guy at the top in the NSA knowing and rerouting anti-terrorist materials to deal with vampires'. Not to mention a conspiracy theorist (or small group of them working to oust a vampire) is also much more trivially destroyed socially once their activities are know. It is more in the logic of what was written about the Imbued in general in past editions .<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T13:46:27-07:00","id":1382375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382369#post1382369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is just my view but from now on, I wouldn't be surrpised if the Vampires are the central splat with everyone else as a supplement to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curious minds inquiring. What makes you say that? I haven't heard anything to that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T13:56:46-07:00","id":1382378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382375#post1382375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curious minds inquiring. What makes you say that? I haven't heard anything to that effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just for ease of marketing. I may be wrong because they've announced Werewolf 5E but it occurs to me they might devote more of their resources to the central game versus trying to dilute it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T17:05:17-07:00","id":1382409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382378#post1382378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just for ease of marketing. I may be wrong because they've announced Werewolf 5E but it occurs to me they might devote more of their resources to the central game versus trying to dilute it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think in the case of V5, you have to remember that Modiphius only came into taking on the license in the 11th hour after the White Wolf team was dissolved. As such, they didn\u2019t really have plans in taking on all the WoD games, and Vampire was always the most profitable one. I expect Modiphius will probably make a few more supplements over the next year or two, and then let Onyx Path continue with supplemental support after then. I don\u2019t know, of course, but I\u2019d expect to see the Players\u2019 Guide followed up by The Second Inquisition in the new year, and maybe it will be a standalone game to compliment V5. I don\u2019t expect any other \u2018fat splats\u2019 though. Maybe they will get round to a Sabbat book, presumably with the Tzmisce at its core, but who knows. Maybe the Ravnos will join the Sabbat! Personally, I think they would make more truck if they made more City Chronicle books, but that is just me.<br /> <br /> We know that Werewolf 5th is to be taken on by Hunter\u2019s Entertainment, a relatively new company albeit with some recognizable faces, and Matt Dawkins will still be co--ordinating it. Curiously, outside of some fans comparing its original 1st edition release unfavorably to V1 and it having a fairly overt political commentary, Werewolf has never really been as controversial as Vampire has when making new editions. I expect the fans will probably switch over to it quite agreeably, particularly if they tie it in effectively with the video game releases. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m really not sure about M5. The current M20 is still planning releases and there has always been an argument that it should stand independent of the other WoD games. The current developer, Brucato, is passionate about his role and so are his fans, so there could be an even bigger negative reaction to any idea of a new edition. Mage is a more complex game than the others in a number of respects, and has a history of bitter flame wars, and any new development crew ought to be fully aware of this. There is a great possible game that could emerge in leaner format, but there is a lot of baggage to let go. <br /> <br /> Wraith and Changeling, bluntly, won\u2019t be commercially lucrative enough to make new editions, I don\u2019t think. Some fans will be upset to say that, but both games never got beyond their 2nd editions first time round, and again, they are pretty well served by the 20th Anniversary editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T17:20:48-07:00","id":1382410,"title":"","content":"I suppose it depends on the licensing as it could be that companies would contact White Wolf about doing it rather than being commissioned to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T17:25:28-07:00","id":1382411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382409#post1382409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think in the case of V5, you have to remember that Modiphius only came into taking on the license in the 11th hour after the White Wolf team was dissolved. As such, they didn\u2019t really have plans in taking on all the WoD games, and Vampire was always the most profitable one. I expect Modiphius will probably make a few more supplements over the next year or two, and then let Onyx Path continue with supplemental support after then. I don\u2019t know, of course, but I\u2019d expect to see the Players\u2019 Guide followed up by The Second Inquisition in the new year, and maybe it will be a standalone game to compliment V5. I don\u2019t expect any other \u2018fat splats\u2019 though. Maybe they will get round to a Sabbat book, presumably with the Tzmisce at its core, but who knows. Maybe the Ravnos will join the Sabbat! Personally, I think they would make more truck if they made more City Chronicle books, but that is just me.<br /> <br /> We know that Werewolf 5th is to be taken on by Hunter\u2019s Entertainment, a relatively new company albeit with some recognizable faces, and Matt Dawkins will still be co--ordinating it. Curiously, outside of some fans comparing its original 1st edition release unfavorably to V1 and it having a fairly overt political commentary, Werewolf has never really been as controversial as Vampire has when making new editions. I expect the fans will probably switch over to it quite agreeably, particularly if they tie it in effectively with the video game releases.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m really not sure about M5. The current M20 is still planning releases and there has always been an argument that it should stand independent of the other WoD games. The current developer, Brucato, is passionate about his role and so are his fans, so there could be an even bigger negative reaction to any idea of a new edition. Mage is a more complex game than the others in a number of respects, and has a history of bitter flame wars, and any new development crew ought to be fully aware of this. There is a great possible game that could emerge in leaner format, but there is a lot of baggage to let go.<br /> <br /> Wraith and Changeling, bluntly, won\u2019t be commercially lucrative enough to make new editions, I don\u2019t think. Some fans will be upset to say that, but both games never got beyond their 2nd editions first time round, and again, they are pretty well served by the 20th Anniversary editions.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Just a nitpick, they weren't dissolved. Tobias left on his own, Martin was let go later, but everyone else is still working. They had a mandate to not write in house (so they are no longer doing core books, which is all they ever said they were going to do in house anyway).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T17:31:19-07:00","id":1382412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382411#post1382411\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Just a nitpick, they weren't dissolved. Tobias left on his own, Martin was let go later, but everyone else is still working. They had a mandate to not write in house (so they are no longer doing core books, which is all they ever said they were going to do in house anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, however we describe it, you know what I mean.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T17:52:48-07:00","id":1382414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Trippy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382412#post1382412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, however we describe it, you know what I mean.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, simply becasue 'dissolved' means WW is no more, which isn't true. And this is something a lot of people repeat verbatim and think that WW isn't even involved any more and/or that they don't exist.<br /> <br /> They're still doing all the brand management and control, just not writing in house, and have heavier oversight from Paradox now being directly involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-18T17:56:53-07:00","id":1382415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382414#post1382414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not really, simply becasue 'dissolved' means WW is no more, which isn't true. And this is something a lot of people repeat verbatim and think that WW isn't even involved any more and/or that they don't exist.<br /> <br /> They're still doing all the brand management and control, just not writing in house, and have heavier oversight from Paradox now being directly involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok lets say it this way: whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2517-trippy","name":"Trippy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2517_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1018"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T05:33:12-07:00","id":1382500,"title":"","content":"I find V5's setting more convoluted, confusing and inaccessible to V20. V5 bombards people with massive events and provides a timeline, which means new people need to consider what things were like before and what things were like after. There are far too many movers and shakers, like the SI, in V5's metaplot for someone new to make sense of. It's like starting to watch a new TV show with the Season finale. It's far easier for both new and old players to come to &quot;Business as usual&quot;. <br /> <br /> The Imbued could have been explained as 'Warriors blessed with seemingly holy abilities. and intentionally kept mysterious. They could've been given a stat block with a little table of cool abilities to roll from. They don't need explaining, they're obviously meant to be something difficult to explain. Just treat them like Werewolf treats formori: any number of minor powers with no explanation necessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T06:07:15-07:00","id":1382505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382500#post1382500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find V5's setting more convoluted, confusing and inaccessible to V20.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet most people disagree, perhaps because they don't try to jam every single Clan and Bloodline into the main book. No one has expressed any confusion about the Second Inquisition or timeline in the new edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 bombards people with massive events and provides a timeline, which means new people need to consider what things were like before and what things were like after. There are far too many movers and shakers, like the SI, in V5's metaplot for someone new to make sense of. It's like starting to watch a new TV show with the Season finale. It's far easier for both new and old players to come to &quot;Business as usual&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Vampires exist, there's the snobby faction, the street faction, and the guys who hunt them. Done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Imbued could have been explained as 'Warriors blessed with seemingly holy abilities. and intentionally kept mysterious. They could've been given a stat block with a little table of cool abilities to roll from. They don't need explaining, they're obviously meant to be something difficult to explain. Just treat them like Werewolf treats formori: any number of minor powers with no explanation necessary. </div> </div> </div>By contrast, you can just say, &quot;SWAT team member with big guns&quot;<br /> <br /> But the big thing is I don't see how the Imbued would be any better than the Second Inquisition because the Imbued were meant to be underdogs who were confused &quot;normal&quot; people and didn't have any organization. H:TR goes out of its way to say you should play Housewives instead of Navy SEALS. That you should have little in the way of weapons, very little in the way of information, and no support. It actually indicates that Hunters are going to be less capable than the Society of Leopold or SAD since we actually got a supplement about those things.<br /> <br /> HUNTER: FIRST CONTACT.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/1/1555-thumb140.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> The government and Inquisition are terrifying to them because the Reckoning isn't actually meant to be badasses kicking supernatural ass but a few extra abilities to the typical Frog Brothers game. Aside from Hunter.net, they don't have any real organization or ability to mount a major offensive against humans. They don't have the numbers, agreement, weapons, or power.<br /> <br /> I like Hunter but the whole point is they are a last ditch effort against the supernatural and mostly mindless ones like zombies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 04-19-2020, 09:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-19T11:55:18-07:00","id":1382566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1382505#post1382505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By contrast, you can just say, &quot;SWAT team member with big guns&quot;<br /> <br /> But the big thing is I don't see how the Imbued would be any better than the Second Inquisition because the Imbued were meant to be underdogs who were confused &quot;normal&quot; people and didn't have any organization. H:TR goes out of its way to say you should play Housewives instead of Navy SEALS. That you should have little in the way of weapons, very little in the way of information, and no support. It actually indicates that Hunters are going to be less capable than the Society of Leopold or SAD since we actually got a supplement about those things.<br /> <br /> HUNTER: FIRST CONTACT.<br /> <br /> The government and Inquisition are terrifying to them because the Reckoning isn't actually meant to be badasses kicking supernatural ass but a few extra abilities to the typical Frog Brothers game. Aside from Hunter.net, they don't have any real organization or ability to mount a major offensive against humans. They don't have the numbers, agreement, weapons, or power.<br /> <br /> I like Hunter but the whole point is they are a last ditch effort against the supernatural and mostly mindless ones like zombies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, if one were revisiting H:tR, some of those points could shift around. None likely near enough to make Imbued into their own SI, but you could dial back the feeling of desperation a bit. Just enough to make it more approachable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T05:35:19-07:00","id":1384170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition#post1379003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't like the Second Inquisition.. It just feels.. so cliche and horrible. From somehow breaking into Schrecknet, then the Vatican getting involved, then this group of mortals just wrecking everything.. Yeah no. The Camarilla nor Sabbat wouldn't be taken out by such a thing in their pre-V5 unnerfed state realistically (even with the whole Beckoning nonsense, lets be real). The worst egress of this Gary-Stu faction was how they somehow <i>bombed</i> the Vienna Chantry- a magic fortress/university basically that has probably existed longer than all the operators within the SI combined and literally can't be comprehended by mortals at all because it always teleports IIRC. Not only that this Gary-Stu faction has cleared out cities with high level Kindred, some Anchillae too who probably weren't compelled by the Beckoning.. somehow... The Second Inquisition.. is horrible.<br /> <br /> What would have been way more compelling was to bring the Imbued in as the primary Human antagonists instead of the SI. More interesting, has clear abilities that would've allowed them to spot Vienna in the first place with True Sight, a clear precedent of their power is known so there is a logical justification for how their KO'ing the Camarilla and the Sabbat (<i>especially the Sabbat</i>), and they would've been generally more compelling. Because I don't understand the fuss about the Second Inquisition, their faction doesn't make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with you. First of all remember first inquisition. Sometimes they had luck and they found vampires based on superstitions (like in &quot;The name of the rose&quot;, black cats, black roosters, people you don't see during the day) sometimes more powerful vampires mark their weaker brothers as targets. During tortures the victims could finger the next one and so on. Second: many alphabet agencies have at least some data about supernaturals. In older editions there were some devices to detect vampires and ghosts in p. ex. Pentagon. They know at least some names (Vetrue are treated as right winged capitalits, Brujah are left winger anarchists, most lupines are in german, scandinavian, celtic and indians population), FBI X-files (Special Division) was given additional funds to find senator's missing granddaughter (Thandi Grubbhold, Philodox Fianna, abducted by lupines before her First Change). There was even a paranoid scheme created by Bob Schnoblin, CIA, which mentions Verbena, Euthanatos, Technocracy and NWO (mages), Black Furies, Shadow Lords and Children of Gaia (werewolves) and Ventrue. FBI have &quot;10 most wanted&quot; list which mentions werewolves (Black Spiral Dancers and Wendigo), Vampires (Brujah). NPC from Contacts and Victims linked a few terrorist organizations, not knowing that he really discovered a Sabat cell. That's for start. Third: there are many people/organizations which would like to eliminate their competitors/enemies. Many of them are high placed: the General from Seventh Generation who could use his influence to eliminate werewolves, Marsha Crowe, East Coast FBI Director who is a werewolf's daughter and is likely to help his father and his friends fighting the Wyrm, many Wyrm controlled corporations and DNA fighting werewolves etc. Fourth: many NPCs are walking in the open like Spooky Tooth, a Glass Walkers heavy metal band. There was also a few moments where Masquerade/Veil/etc. crashed: massive Awakenings in Chicago in 1986 or war in Chicago 1993. In Giovanni Chronicles IV : Nuova Malattia ghoul characters are arrested by FBI, a puppet of vampires. Ok, he was dominated to think that they are ordinary mobsters, but domination can be reversed. There are means to detect supernaturals: IR detectors for vampires, blood tests for werewolves and ghouls. And based on these facts it's not hard to imagine a clandestine operation. As for Tremere Chantry bombing they could detonate the bomb NEAR or OVER the Chantry thus not triggering the wards. Not to mention the holy objects provided by Society of Leopold.<br /> <br /> But But I don't discard the Imbued. Hell, some of them could also help the SI.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T08:44:20-07:00","id":1384197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nail Eater</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1384170#post1384170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't agree with you. First of all remember first inquisition. Sometimes they had luck and they found vampires based on superstitions (like in &quot;The name of the rose&quot;, black cats, black roosters, people you don't see during the day) sometimes more powerful vampires mark their weaker brothers as targets. During tortures the victims could finger the next one and so on. Second: many alphabet agencies have at least some data about supernaturals. In older editions there were some devices to detect vampires and ghosts in p. ex. Pentagon. They know at least some names (Vetrue are treated as right winged capitalits, Brujah are left winger anarchists, most lupines are in german, scandinavian, celtic and indians population), FBI X-files (Special Division) was given additional funds to find senator's missing granddaughter (Thandi Grubbhold, Philodox Fianna, abducted by lupines before her First Change). There was even a paranoid scheme created by Bob Schnoblin, CIA, which mentions Verbena, Euthanatos, Technocracy and NWO (mages), Black Furies, Shadow Lords and Children of Gaia (werewolves) and Ventrue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I liked the joke in Hunters Hunted II that while it was easy to make fun of Bob Schnoblin, it turned out his Pyramid of Satanic Power was probably more accurate than 90% of what actual supernaturals knew since it created a decent framework of showing the various factions all controlling large elements of society versus the fact that each faction assuming they controlled everything alone.<br /> <br /> [quote]FBI have &quot;10 most wanted&quot; list which mentions werewolves (Black Spiral Dancers and Wendigo), Vampires (Brujah). NPC from Contacts and Victims linked a few terrorist organizations, not knowing that he really discovered a Sabat cell. That's for start. Third: there are many people/organizations which would like to eliminate their competitors/enemies.[/quote<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think very few gamers read Project: Twilight and get annoyed that agencies are treated as anything but utterly ignorant of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But But I don't discard the Imbued. Hell, some of them could also help the SI. </div> </div> </div>Hunter: First Contact treated the SAD as going, &quot;Oh god, these guys are a bunch of domestic terriorists who are going to fuck it up for everyone!&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T09:38:28-07:00","id":1384204,"title":"","content":"The SoL, Arcanum and 'Goverment' are a triad of forces that shouldn't mix. The SoL have too much zeal and probably view the other two parties as tools of the devil. The Arcanum is doing weird shit that they need to keep secret from the other parties, the goverment is looking at a terrorist organization and a bunch of people who are probably doing something illegal. <br /> <br /> That said, Imbued: If the religious nuts/Goverment wanted to swoop them up, they could. It shouldn't take more than three months to train them up. And since most members of attack teams likely have more downtime than not (it's difficult to find a vampire, let alone hunt one), there's more opportunity to train them beyond that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T09:58:17-07:00","id":1384209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1384197#post1384197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I liked the joke in Hunters Hunted II that while it was easy to make fun of Bob Schnoblin, it turned out his Pyramid of Satanic Power was probably more accurate than 90% of what actual supernaturals knew since it created a decent framework of showing the various factions all controlling large elements of society versus the fact that each faction assuming they controlled everything alone.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think very few gamers read Project: Twilight and get annoyed that agencies are treated as anything but utterly ignorant of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Hunter: First Contact treated the SAD as going, &quot;Oh god, these guys are a bunch of domestic terriorists who are going to fuck it up for everyone!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>As for Schnoblin's pyramid it's only one thing of many that alphabets know. And many more conspiracy theorist could search for hidden knowledge in very strange places (like in &quot;Queen of the Damned&quot;). And of course it should be remembered that during Cold War (and II WW) both sides try to find anything to get a foot ahead their enemies, not omiting occult.<br /> <br /> I know that many people don't know (or ignore) Project Twilight. For me it's one of the best books ever created for WoD. On the other hand I'm a big fan of political fiction, from Clancy, Forsythe and Brown to conspiracy theories. That's why mortals are usually the biggest threat for PCs. And usually they cannot do anything to remove this threat (at least not harming themselves) \ud83d\ude08.<br /> <br /> Ok, SAD could treat Imbued like a bunch of religious fanatics but &quot;enemy of my enemy is my friend&quot;. And I think that many Imbued don't reveal their nature. Most people know that talking with angels is the fastest way to the asylum. And I don't think that there's a pure mundane scientific method to discover an Imbued. During my games they aren't even detected by Sense the True Form. Sometimes they can be found by Detect Magic or sth like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":13141,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","user":"Nail Eater","date":". 04-27-2020, 02:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T10:17:31-07:00","id":1384214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1384204#post1384204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The SoL, Arcanum and 'Goverment' are a triad of forces that shouldn't mix. The SoL have too much zeal and probably view the other two parties as tools of the devil. The Arcanum is doing weird shit that they need to keep secret from the other parties, the goverment is looking at a terrorist organization and a bunch of people who are probably doing something illegal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but still &quot;enemy of my enemy is my friend&quot;. Also there are always some more rational people in their ranks. <br /> <br /> As for SoL if the governement wants to help with the hunt well, good for us.<br /> As for Arcanum I once run a story about bunch of friends attacked by vampires. They lost one during the assault. They started to search for any info about their attackers. They run at the Arcanum cell, joined, learn anything they could and then left to hunt vampires. They ended when they was betrayed by one of them who wanted power so he traded his teammates for an Embrace. But I think they weren't the only ones who joined Arcanum to gain knowledge and use it for hunting. And people like these could join SI.<br /> <br /> As for governement, even religious fanatics could be useful. Just equip them and point the target. And you have a political fiction story: SI could be easily removed by vampires. If they (vampires) reveal that governement funds religious fanatics the governement could be easily compromised. Cause either the people would be angry or, if the alphabets reveal the existence of vampires, treat the governement as nuts. Of course the proof should be produced, either fake or real, by both sides. On the other hand SI will not want to be stopped so they could use their influences to silence the signalists. And you have a political thriller to run \ud83d\ude42. Trust me, the media is a powerful weapon. I used to be a journalist so I know that first hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:10:31-07:00","id":1384261,"title":"","content":"&quot;The enemy of my enemy is my friend,&quot; is something that frequently sees the original context lost as a situational and contextual relationship. Today's friend is tomorrow's enemy, and that's supposed to temper how much you approach this friend.<br /> <br /> History is full of examples of what happens when people forget this, especially when it comes to governments teaming up with religious fanatics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T14:49:53-07:00","id":1384271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1379003-why-not-the-imbued-instead-of-the-second-inquisition?p=1384261#post1384261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&amp;quot;History is full of examples of what happens when people forget this, especially when it comes to governments teaming up with religious fanatics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Touch\u00e9. But still I think it's easier to eliminate religious fanatics tomorrow. Today let them help us eliminate blankbodies \ud83d\ude0e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}